{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke2fsvnAwYVYAQL2crP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CtFvFh2dt2nEnULzrCAdjd","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","offset":151,"limit":200},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5291,"cache_read_input_tokens":28874,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5291},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"7fb401d9-d85a-43df-85d1-21b61ba75149","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:02.862Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke2ffXUpi5YoYZVURGo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01CtFvFh2dt2nEnULzrCAdjd":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","offset":151,"limit":200}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CtFvFh2dt2nEnULzrCAdjd","type":"tool_result","content":"151\t(Final settlement. The microphone is gone. His jaw keeps moving. The voice keeps coming, from the thing on his neck. It always did.)\n152\t(She stamps the form on it.)\n153\tMAX: Claim denied.\n154\t\n155\tENDING (dawn, the launch. The Dame writes a cheque.)\n156\tDAME: Your fee. Less deductions.\n157\tMAX: This is for three pounds seventy-five.\n158\tDAME: You dripped.\n159\tPYM: Ms. Ransom, one thing for the file. The island appears in our books. As a client.\n160\tMAX: Since when?\n161\tPYM: Since eighteen forty. Please hold.\n162\t(On-hold jingle over black. Last shot: a limpet on the launch's hull opens, slowly.)\n163\t```\n164\t\n165\t**Commodore Tannoy lines** (one per Tannoy, each can be cut off by shooting it: the text stops at a `-`, Max says `Noted.` or `Thank you.`):\n166\t`A REMINDER: THE FISH MARKET IS CLOSED. THE FISH HAVE WON.` · `MISS RANSOM, I HAVE READ YOUR POLICY. I FIND IT RESTRICTIVE.` · `WHO IS SHOOTING MY LOUDSPEAKERS? THOSE ARE IMPORTED.` · `I AM TOLD YOU WEAR SUNGLASSES AT NIGHT. HOW BRAVE. HOW STUPID.` · `OUR HYMN TODAY IS NUMBER NINE. OUR SURVIVORS TODAY ARE NUMBER NONE.` · `THE BOSUN WOULD LIKE A WORD. HE ONLY HAS THE ONE.` · `DAME OTTOLINE, YOUR GREAT-GRANDFATHER SIGNED IN BLOOD. I HAVE BROUGHT A PEN. IT IS ALSO BLOOD.` · `DO STAY DRY, MISS RANSOM. THE WET ONES GET SO ATTACHED.` · `THIS ISLAND HAS STOOD FOR A THOUSAND YEARS. YOUR COAT WILL NOT.` · `LOST PROPERTY MAY BE COLLECTED FROM THE SEA.` · `THE ABBEY GIFT SHOP IS NOW OPEN. THE ABBEY GIFT IS DEATH.` · `MISS RANSOM, WHAT IS YOUR DEDUCTIBLE? I SHOULD LIKE TO EXCEED IT.` · `A MESSAGE FROM THE CANNERY: WE ARE HIRING. WE ARE ALSO FIRING. MOSTLY FIRING.` · `IF YOU CAN HEAR THIS, YOU ARE TOO CLOSE TO MY VOICE.` · `THAT WAS THE LAST ONE. I HOPE YOU ARE HAPPY.`\n167\t\n168\t**Max barks.** Kill: `Claim closed.` `Pre-existing condition.` `You're not covered.` `Total loss.` Kick: `Deductible.` `Excess applies.` Reload: `One moment, please.` Low health: `My premium's going up.` Out of ammo: `That's not in the budget.`\n169\t\n170\t**Dame barks.** Follow: `Lead on.` Wait: `I shall wait. I charge for it.` Hide: `In a barrel. At my age.` Hurt: `I felt that in my portfolio.` `Deducted.` Grabbed: `Unhand me, you sardine!` You shoot near her: `Mind the coat.` You kick someone: `Vulgar. Do it again.` Idle: `I have sacked men for less.` `Do you always lurk?`\n171\t\n172\t**Pym radio hints** always start with the on-hold jingle and `Your call is important to Ostrander Mutual.`, then one hint for the current beat, such as: `Ms. Ransom. If you are surrounded, that is a Section 4 event. Kick something.` · `Our records show loudspeakers are not load-bearing. Shoot them.` · `The insured is a protected asset. Please stop leaving her in barrels.` · `Tide is not an Act of God if it was printed in advance.`\n173\t\n174\t**Claim Notes** (6 collectible files, 3-4 lines each, on the Files tab): a tide table with times crossed out; a cannery time sheet where every name is the same after week 9; Actuary's memo (`Skerry Holm: 0 claims since 1840. Investigate why this is suspicious.`); the Hymn of the Tithe (real dread, no joke); Fathom's receipt for 400 harpoons, signed with a bubble; page 40 of Dame Ottoline's application, on which someone has written `SIGN HERE, AND HERE, AND IN THE SEA`.\n175\t\n176\tChapter cards: `CLAIM 1: ACT OF GOD` · `CLAIM 2: WEAR AND TEAR` · `CLAIM 3: ACT OF COMMODORE` · `FINAL SETTLEMENT`. Islander barks are a made-up tongue, shown as small subtitles: `HAAL AN!` `SKARR!` `VOR THOLE!` `BRINNA!` `OV THE TIDE!` `VEN ULDA!`\n177\t\n178\t---\n179\t\n180\t## 3. Controls\n181\t\n182\tPad in standard mapping, with PlayStation names (Xbox glyphs: Cross=A, Circle=B, Square=X, Triangle=Y, L1=LB, R1=RB, L2=LT, R2=RT, Options=Menu, Create=View).\n183\t\n184\t| Action | Pad | Keyboard and mouse |\n185\t| --- | --- | --- |\n186\t| Move | Left stick | WASD |\n187\t| Look / aim | Right stick | Mouse (pointer lock) |\n188\t| Aim (hold) | L2 | Right mouse |\n189\t| Fire | R2 (while aiming) | Left mouse (while aiming) |\n190\t| Knife | R1 | Left mouse (not aiming), or V |\n191\t| Action: kick, open, vault, climb, pick up, talk, QTE 1 | Cross | E |\n192\t| Run (hold) / quick 180° turn (tap with stick back) | Circle | Shift / Q |\n193\t| Reload | Square | R |\n194\t| The Case | Triangle | Tab or I |\n195\t| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\n196\t| Map tab | Create (on release, ignored if Options was pressed: Create+Options belongs to the hub) | M |\n197\t| Next / previous weapon | D-pad up / down | Wheel or 1-4 |\n198\t| Heal (best herb) | D-pad left | H |\n199\t| Command the Dame (Follow/Wait; context: Hide, Boost, Release crane) | D-pad right | C |\n200\t| Throw grenade at the laser dot (while aiming) | L1 | G |\n201\t| Swap shoulder | R3 | T |\n202\t| QTE 2 / dodge | Circle | Space |\n203\t| Menus | Stick or D-pad, Cross confirm, Circle back, L1/R1 change tab, Square secondary, Triangle tertiary | Hover and click, Enter confirm, Esc back, Q/E change tab, wheel scrolls |\n204\t\n205\tThe mouse does what a PC player expects: it looks and aims, you click the world by shooting it (Tannoys, crates, barrels, thrown bottles), and a left click advances dialogue. Never bind Ctrl combinations. Call `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')`. Esc under pointer lock releases the lock and may not reach the page: pause on `pointerlockchange` when the lock is lost during play and you didn't release it yourself. Rumble with `gamepad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` on shots, hits and QTEs, guarded so the test stub doesn't throw.\n206\t\n207\t---\n208\t\n209\t## 4. Systems\n210\t\n211\tAll numbers live in `src/data/tuning.js` and `src/data/*.js`. Treat them as first values and balance with the bot (§15) and the dev sliders (§12).\n212\t\n213\t### 4.1 Movement and camera\n214\t- **Body:** `new CharacterController(physics, { position, speed: TUNING.runSpeed, radius: 0.3, halfHeight: 0.5 })`, tag its collider `noCamera` and `player`. Each fixed step call `setInput(moveVector, false, false)` and `fixedUpdate(dt)`. **[verified]** Velocity is `speed` × the move vector's length (half a vector at speed 4 moves at 2 m/s) and walls stop it, so build the controller with the top speed and scale the vector. Worlds are flat (ground at y=0), so there are no stairs: ladders and floors are scripted.\n215\t- **Speeds:** walk 3.0 m/s at full tilt (under 55% tilt, 1.6 m/s), run 4.8, acceleration 18 m/s², turn 540°/s toward travel while exploring. Quick turn: 180° in 0.3 s.\n216\t- **Camera:** yaw and pitch are game state, shared by explore and aim so nothing snaps. The engine's `third` rig orbits but has no shoulder offset, so replace `step` on the rig instance at runtime (the engine file stays untouched) **[verified]**:\n217\t\n218\t```js\n219\t// In Area.setup. Engine.start used camera: { preset: 'third', fov: 55 }.\n220\tconst rig = ctx.camera; rig.zoomable = false;\n221\trig.step = (u) => {\n222\t  const c = game.cam; // { yaw, pitch, dist, up, side, fov } eased in update()\n223\t  dir.set(Math.sin(c.yaw) * Math.cos(c.pitch), Math.sin(c.pitch), Math.cos(c.yaw) * Math.cos(c.pitch));\n224\t  right.set(-Math.cos(c.yaw), 0, Math.sin(c.yaw));\n225\t  pos.copy(u.target).addScaledVector(dir, -c.dist).addScaledVector(right, c.side * game.shoulder); pos.y += c.up;\n226\t  tmp.copy(pos).sub(u.target); const len = tmp.length(); tmp.normalize();\n227\t  const hit = u.world.raycast?.(u.target, tmp, len); // skips colliders tagged character / noCamera\n228\t  if (hit != null) pos.copy(u.target).addScaledVector(tmp, Math.max(0.4, hit - 0.2));\n229\t  rig.focus.copy(u.target); rig.camera.position.copy(pos);\n230\t  if (rig.camera.fov !== c.fov) { rig.camera.fov = c.fov; rig.camera.updateProjectionMatrix(); }\n231\t  rig.camera.lookAt(look.copy(pos).addScaledVector(dir, 12));\n232\t};\n233\t```\n234\t- **Camera values [verified to frame well]:** `cameraTarget` = feet + 1.3 m. Explore: dist 4.0, up 0.45, side 0.55, fov 55. Aim: dist 2.9, up 0.1, side 0.95, fov 42 (ease over 0.16 s). Scope: fov 16. Hide Max's model when the camera is closer than 0.9 m to her. During cutscenes `rig.step` applies `timeline.camera()` instead.\n235\t- **Look speeds:** the engine feeds the right stick into `input.mouseDelta` at `gamepadLookSpeed` (500 px/s). Recover the stick value with `v = delta / (500 * dt)`, apply `sign(v) * |v|^1.8`, then yaw at 2.2 rad/s exploring and 1.1 rad/s aiming (pitch at 60% of that). Mouse: 0.0026 rad/px exploring, 0.0016 aiming. Pitch range -0.7 to +0.7. Y invert is a setting.\n236\t- **Pointer lock:** the engine only requests it for `first` and `free` cameras. During play, request it yourself in a `pointerdown` listener on `engine.gpu.renderer.domElement` (mouse pointers only), and catch the rejected promise. Chrome refuses a re-lock for about a second after Esc: show `CLICK TO AIM` until it succeeds. `input.mouseDelta` accumulates whenever the pointer is locked **[verified from the source]**. Release the lock in every menu so hover works.\n237\t\n238\t### 4.2 Aiming and shooting\n239\t- Hold aim: Max plants her feet (move vector zero, faces camera yaw), and the laser comes on. `TUNING.aimWalkSpeed` is 0 by default; a slider lets you test otherwise.\n240\t- Aim ray: `rig.rayAt(0, 0, o, d)`, then `ctx.physics.castRay(o, d, 80, ['player', 'enemy'])` for the world (so bullets still hit props tagged `noCamera`), then ray tests against hit zones. Nearest wins.\n241\t- **Laser [verified]:** a `BoxGeometry(0.02, 0.02, 1)` with `glowMaterial(0xff3030)` stretched from the muzzle to the hit point, `castShadow = false`. On the HUD, project the hit point and draw a 3×3 red dot with a white centre. Dot colours: lime on head, sand on legs. Keep the sway: `yaw/pitch += sin/cos(t × 1.7…) × weapon.sway × TUNING.laserSway × 0.003`.\n242\t- Firing: hitscan, `fireInterval`; recoil kick on pitch that recovers; `engine.shake.add(0.12)`; muzzle `ctx.lights.request({ position, color: 0xffc060, intensity: 8, radius: 6, lifetime: 0.06 })`; impact `ctx.particles.burst('impact', hit)`; `Decals` `scorch` on walls.\n243\t- **Pad aim assist:** while the stick is moving, slow look speed by `TUNING.aimAssist` (0.35) when the laser is within 0.6° of a head or torso. Add 0.03 to head radius. Off for mouse.\n244\t\n245\t### 4.3 Hit zones, stagger, melee\n246\tAfter each frame's animation update, cache each enemy's zones from its joints' world positions (**[verified]**: joints pose correctly in Node too): head sphere (Head joint + 0.13 m up × scale, radius 0.2 × scale), torso capsule (Pelvis to Head, r 0.22), arms and legs (two capsules each, r 0.09 and 0.11). Fixed-step shots test against the cache.\n247\t\n248\t| Zone | Damage × | Effect |\n249\t| --- | --- | --- |\n250\t| Head | 2.0 | 70% chance of **Stun** (hands to face, 1.5 s). Pistol has a 6% chance of a head pop (instant kill) |\n251\t| Torso | 1.0 | Flinch 0.25 s; interrupts wind-up if the hit is ≥10 damage |\n252\t| Arm | 0.7 | Drops what it holds: a held bottle explodes on them, a shield drops |\n253\t| Leg | 0.7 | Two pistol hits' worth of leg damage: **Kneel** (1.7 s) |\n254\t\n255\t- **Kick** (prompt on a Stunned enemy within 2.6 m, in front): roundhouse, 120° cone, radius 2.6 m, 25 damage and knockdown to all in it, 40 to the target. Max is invulnerable for 0.5 s. `engine.hitstop(0.05)`, `shake.add(0.35)`. **Takedown** (prompt on a Kneeling enemy): hip throw, 60 damage, knockdown within 1.5 m.\n256\t- **Knife:** 8 damage, 0.4 s, 2 m arc, ×3 on downed enemies, breaks crates for free.\n257\t- Knockdown: `Fall`-type clip, up in 2.2 s. Death: `Death` clip or `new Ragdoll(physics, model, HERO_RAGDOLL).enable({ velocity })` for shotgun and explosion kills (**[verified]** on our puppets; call `sync()` instead of the mixer). Keep at most 8 ragdolls live. Corpses stay (Limpets need them; despawn the oldest above 20).\n258\t- **Hit feedback:** swap the mesh materials to `glowMaterial(white)` for 2 frames (don't mutate shared toon materials), `Decals` `splat` in `plum`, `plum`/`teal` chunk particles. Head pop: scale the Head joint to 0 and burst. Stylised, not realistic.\n259\t\n260\t### 4.4 Weapons\n261\tWeapon data: `src/data/weapons.js`. Footprint = cells in the Case.\n262\t\n263\t| Id | Name | Damage | Interval | Mag | Reload | Sway | Special | Footprint | Price |\n264\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n265\t| pistol | Ostrander .38 | 14 | 0.30 | 12 | 1.35 | 0.8 | head pop chance | 3×2 | start |\n266\t| scatter | Bosun's Scattergun | 9 × 7 pellets | 0.95 | 6 | 2.4 | 0.4 | 5.5° cone, falls off past 9 m, knocks back | 7×2 | 900 |\n267\t| rifle | Sealer's Rifle | 55 | 1.3 | 5 | 2.2 | 1.2 | Scope (fov 16), pierces one body | 8×2 | 1800 |\n268\t| harpoon | Harpoon Gun | 90 | 1.2 | 1 | 2.0 | 0.5 | Pins an enemy to a wall or the ground for 4 s; bolt can be picked up again | 6×2 | 2600 |\n269\t\n270\t- Knife: always available, not in the Case. Grenades (1×2): **Magnesium Flare** (blinds a 6 m radius for 4 s, kills all Limpets in it), **Depth Charge** (explodes after 1.5 s, 80 damage, 4 m), **Whale-Oil Bottle** (burning pool, 3 s, 15 damage per second).\n271\t- **Tuning at Mr. Fathom** (per weapon, 4 levels of Power, Rate, Reload, Capacity, price 300 → 1500). Filling all four unlocks a perk: pistol head pop 30%; scatter wider cone and pushes everyone in it; rifle pierces all; harpoon reloads itself in 1 s.\n272\t\n273\t### 4.5 The Case\n274\t- Grid starts at 10×6, upgraded at the shop to 12×7 (1500) and 14×8 (4000). Cell = 14 art pixels. Weapons, ammo, herbs and grenades take cells; **Valuables** and **Key Items** are lists with no footprint, on their own tabs.\n275\t- Screen (time frozen): the grid on the left, a big icon, name and 2 lines of text on the right. Tabs: CASE · VALUABLES · KEY ITEMS · MAP · FILES · RADIO. Pick up with Cross or click, rotate with Square / right mouse / wheel, drop with Triangle, Use/Equip/Combine via Cross on a stationary item (small 3-item menu). `ARRANGE` packs everything automatically (hold R1 / key F; first-fit decreasing).\n276\t- Picking up with no room opens the Case in arrange mode with the new item in hand; the player places it or leaves it on the ground. The ground item stays.\n277\t- Ammo stacks in its footprint: pistol box 2×1 (max 50), shells 2×1 (max 24), rifle rounds 2×1 (max 20), bolts 3×1 (max 6).\n278\t\n279\t### 4.6 Items, treasure, loot\n280\t- **Herbs (1×2):** Samphire (green, +30%), Dulse (red, heals nothing alone), Sea Holly (yellow, +10 max health when mixed). Combine: S+S 60%, S+S+S 100%, S+D 100%, S+D+H 100% and +10 max. Company First-Aid Tin (1×2): 100%, sold at 800.\n281\t- **Treasure (Valuables):** Pearl 500, Black Pearl 1500, Sea Glass Set 400, Amber 700, Scrimshaw Tusk 900, Gold Tooth 150, Empty Reliquary 1200. **Combining:** the Reliquary has 3 sockets (Pearl, Black Pearl, Amber) and is worth 8000 when full. Mr. Fathom pays full listed value for treasure and half for everything else.\n282\t- **Doubloons:** currency, auto-collected. Mr. Fathom takes nothing else (`He doesn't take plastic`).\n283\t- **Loot Director** (`src/game/loot.js`): when a crate or corpse drops, weight by need: little ammo for carried weapons → that ammo; under 50% health with no herbs → Samphire; otherwise Doubloons (25-80). Crates always drop something. `TUNING.lootRate` and `moneyRate` scale it. The director is the balance safety net: it should be hard, not impossible, to run dry.\n284\t- **Tannoys (15):** shooting all gives a free perk from Mr. Fathom at 5, 10 and 15 (+1000 doubloons, the Case upgrade, a Black Pearl). The Map tab can show them after buying a chart (300).\n285\t\n286\t### 4.7 Mr. Fathom (shop)\n287\tSix appearances (`m` on the maps). Green lantern and a low bubbling loop you hear before you see him. Screen tabs BUY · SELL · TUNE. At most 6 rows at a time, one big item panel, his helmet portrait and a line of text with gibberish voice. Stock grows per chapter. Music switches to the shop song. Prices are in data.\n288\t\n289\t### 4.8 Enemies\n290\tEvery human is a puppet on `HERO_RIG` (§8). Bodies are kinematic capsules (r 0.28, tags `noCamera`, `enemy`) moved along a `NavGrid` flow field with local separation (0.55 m). Own interpolation between fixed steps: `model.position.lerpVectors(prev, cur, ctx.physics.alpha)`.\n291\t\n292\t| Id | Name | HP | Walk m/s | Attack | Notes |\n293\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n294\t| gaffer | Islander | 34 | 1.1-1.5 | Gaff hook 14; wind-up 0.7 s; 20% try a grab (6/s until you mash free) | Three palettes, some with the band bright, some dim |\n295\t| netwife | Net-Wife | 28 | 1.2 | Throws a weighted net at 8 m: slows you 40% for 3 s, can be shot mid-air | Headscarf |\n296\t| bottler | Bottler | 30 | 1.0 | Lobs a whale-oil bottle (arc telegraphed, shootable, 18 + fire) | Shoot the raised bottle: it burns him |\n297\t| runner | Deckhand | 36 | 2.8 | Boathook lunge 16 | From chapter 2. Throws off your aim timing |\n298\t| carrier | Carrier | 60 | 1.6 | Goes for the Dame, shoulders her, walks to the nearest spawn door. 12 s until she is lost | Shoot him: she drops and runs to you |\n299\t| flenser | The Flenser | 220 | 2.2 (lunge 5) | Saw: **kills outright** at full swing (Assisted: 80) unless you QTE dodge | Staggered only by head hits, scatter or explosives. Saw loop (spatial) is heard 30 m away, through walls (`muffle`). Drops 300 and a key item |\n300\t| limpet | Limpet | 15 | 3.0 | Latches: 4/s | 25% of head kills release one. It scuttles to the nearest corpse; if it arrives, that corpse rises as a Re-Salted (fast, 40 HP). Flare kills instantly |\n301\t| monk | Cowled Monk | 70 | 1.3 | Flail 18, wind-up 0.9 | Shield blocks the front; shoot the arm, or kick, to drop it |\n302\t| knight | Reliquary Knight | 300, helmet 40 | 0.9 | Halberd 35, wide | Armour sparks and blocks body shots. Shoot the helmet off, then the head. In the crypt: blind, hunts by sound |\n303\t| drowned | Drowned | 35 | 1.2 | Grabs legs: slows and mashes | Rises out of water on the causeway |\n304\t| harpooner | Boat Harpooner | 50 | n/a | Straight harpoon 22, red glint before firing, shootable | Rides a rowboat beside the causeway and the launch |\n305\t\n306\t**Crowd AI.** A plain state machine per enemy: `WORK` (chores until alerted) → `ALERT` (shout, 0.5 s; alerts within 15 m) → `APPROACH` → `CIRCLE` (hold 3-5 m if no token) → `WINDUP` → `ATTACK` → `RECOVER`; plus `STUN`, `KNEEL`, `FLINCH`, `KNOCKDOWN`, `GETUP`, `GRAB`, `VAULT`, `CLIMB`, `BASH`, `DEAD`. **Attack tokens:** only `TUNING.attackTokens` (2) may be in WINDUP or ATTACK; thrown attacks take 1 token shared across throwers. `maxActive` caps enemies awake per area; others wait at spawn doors. **Adaptive rank** (hidden, 1-5, starting at 2): up on long no-damage streaks and high accuracy, down on each death; rank changes tokens ±1, wind-up ±0.1 s and the wave interval. Show it in dev mode.\n307\t\n308\tDoors, windows, ladders and floors for enemies: flow fields treat `D` and `W` as open. An enemy arriving at a closed door plays `BASH` (door breaks in 6 s or fewer if several bash); at a window it plays `VAULT` and moves through. Ladders and floors: one `NavGrid` per floor plus a link table; an enemy on the wrong floor walks to the nearest link and plays `CLIMB`.\n309\t\n310\t### 4.9 Dame Ottoline\n311\tA `Humanoid` with her own AI (`src/game/companion.js`). Walks 2.6, runs 3.8. Health 100 (dev slider); hurt also adds to the **Deductions** ledger.\n312\t- **Follow** (default): stay 2-4 m behind Max; side-step out of the laser line; duck when an enemy is within 3 m.\n313\t- **Wait:** stands still. **Hide** (context near a barrel or lobster pot): climbs in; safe until called; comic barks.\n314\t- **Boost** (`u`): Max boosts her up to a high hoist chain. **Winch** (`w`), **Crane** (`k`): she operates machines.\n315\t- **Grabbed:** by Carriers. Screen edge warning, `DAME TAKEN` timer (12 s). Lost = game over. Hit by your own bullets = deduction and damage (accident forgiven for scatter at range).\n316\t- Her health shows under Max's. Dead = `CLAIM DENIED`.\n317\t\n318\t### 4.10 Context actions\n319\tOne system (`src/game/interact.js`): each frame pick the best target within 1.6 m and ±70° of facing; show one prompt with the current device's glyph. Priority: Kick/Takedown > ladder knock > door > window > push > pick up > talk > telegraph.\n320\t- **Door:** walking into it with Action kicks it open (0.3 s). An enemy right behind it is knocked down. Collider removed, `nav.setOpen`. Door tween in `ctx.tweens`.\n321\t- **Window (`W`):** vault through, 0.7 s, invulnerable. Enemies follow by vaulting. Glass breaks once.\n322\t- **Ladder:** 1.2 s up or down, exposed. **Knock down** an outside ladder (`E`) from above: it falls with anyone on it.\n323\t- **Push (`p`):** wardrobe slides along one axis at 1 m/s; updates nav; blocks the door until bashed.\n324\t- **Drop:** from upper windows to the ground (0.6 s; onto the hay cart, no damage; otherwise 10).\n325\t- **Tannoy:** any shot; sparks; falls silent mid-line.\n326\t- **Breakables:** `Breakables` from the engine for crates, or a simple swap to chunks. Brine Barrels (red band) explode: 3 m, 60 damage to everyone, chains.\n327\t\n328\t### 4.11 Quick-time events\n329\t`src/game/qte.js`: a large glyph (device-correct) in a shrinking ring at screen centre, `engine.timeScale = 0.5` while open. Types: press (window 0.9 s; dev slider), mash (fill a bar), alternate (Cross/Circle). Used in: Flenser dodge, grabs, Bosun sweep, the belt fight, launch. Fail = hit or death; failed cutscene QTEs restart with a new quip, no reload.\n330\t\n331\t### 4.12 Cutscenes, dialogue, radio\n332\t- `Timeline` drives shots, cues, lines and letterbox **[verified shape]**: `tl.update(dt)`, `tl.camera()`, `tl.line()`, `tl.bars()`, `tl.skip()`. Wrap it in `src/game/cutscene.js`. All skippable (hold Cross / Space 0.6 s, with a small bar). Cues that change the world aren't `cosmetic`.\n333\t- **Dialogue box:** bottom band, name in the speaker's colour, up to 3 lines of 70 characters, typed at 30 chars/s with voice blips (§10). Confirm completes or advances.\n334\t- **Radio:** 32×32 portraits left and right, world dimmed but running unless the area is safe. From the Case RADIO tab (only in dry rooms for long hints) or story-triggered.\n335\t- **Objectives:** small top-left line, fades after 6 s, back on pause.\n336\t\n337\t### 4.13 Saving, dying, difficulty, results\n338\t- **Telegraph key** (`t`) in safe rooms: enemies don't enter; calm music; save slot. Autosave at each area start and before bosses. `localStorage` keys prefixed with a slug from `src/config.js`. In a hub session the client gives an empty storage: don't special-case it.\n339\t- **Death:** slow fall, sting, a big rubber stamp `CLAIM DENIED`, then Continue (last checkpoint) or Quit. Checkpoint data: Run state plus area flags (killed set-piece enemies, opened doors, picked items).\n340\t- **Difficulty** chosen on New Claim: Assisted (enemy damage ×0.6, aim assist ×1.5, saw non-lethal, loot ×1.3), Standard, Professional (enemy damage ×1.4, tokens +1, loot ×0.8).\n341\t- **Claim Form** after each chapter (not dense: 5 big lines): TIME, ACCURACY, HEADSHOTS, KICKS, DEDUCTIONS, then a stamp APPROVED / PENDING / DENIED with a thud, and bonus Doubloons.\n342\t\n343\t---\n344\t\n345\t## 5. Chapters and maps\n346\t\n347\tTarget: 35-45 minutes for a first run, every feature shown at least twice. Each area is one `Game` loaded with `engine.loadGame`.\n348\t\n349\t### Map format\n350\tMaps are painter commands, then rows of characters. Build them with `src/game/mapPaint.js`, keep them in `src/data/levels/*.js`, and use the same rows for geometry, colliders, nav and the Map screen. **All maps below passed a reachability check: every open cell can be reached from `a`.**"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"0c1a4d36-8c74-4ff7-b8d8-ffd885683747","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:02.868Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","content":"(Final settlement. The microphone is gone. His jaw keeps moving. The voice keeps coming, from the thing on his neck. It always did.)\n(She stamps the form on it.)\nMAX: Claim denied.\n\nENDING (dawn, the launch. The Dame writes a cheque.)\nDAME: Your fee. Less deductions.\nMAX: This is for three pounds seventy-five.\nDAME: You dripped.\nPYM: Ms. Ransom, one thing for the file. The island appears in our books. As a client.\nMAX: Since when?\nPYM: Since eighteen forty. Please hold.\n(On-hold jingle over black. Last shot: a limpet on the launch's hull opens, slowly.)\n```\n\n**Commodore Tannoy lines** (one per Tannoy, each can be cut off by shooting it: the text stops at a `-`, Max says `Noted.` or `Thank you.`):\n`A REMINDER: THE FISH MARKET IS CLOSED. THE FISH HAVE WON.` · `MISS RANSOM, I HAVE READ YOUR POLICY. I FIND IT RESTRICTIVE.` · `WHO IS SHOOTING MY LOUDSPEAKERS? THOSE ARE IMPORTED.` · `I AM TOLD YOU WEAR SUNGLASSES AT NIGHT. HOW BRAVE. HOW STUPID.` · `OUR HYMN TODAY IS NUMBER NINE. OUR SURVIVORS TODAY ARE NUMBER NONE.` · `THE BOSUN WOULD LIKE A WORD. HE ONLY HAS THE ONE.` · `DAME OTTOLINE, YOUR GREAT-GRANDFATHER SIGNED IN BLOOD. I HAVE BROUGHT A PEN. IT IS ALSO BLOOD.` · `DO STAY DRY, MISS RANSOM. THE WET ONES GET SO ATTACHED.` · `THIS ISLAND HAS STOOD FOR A THOUSAND YEARS. YOUR COAT WILL NOT.` · `LOST PROPERTY MAY BE COLLECTED FROM THE SEA.` · `THE ABBEY GIFT SHOP IS NOW OPEN. THE ABBEY GIFT IS DEATH.` · `MISS RANSOM, WHAT IS YOUR DEDUCTIBLE? I SHOULD LIKE TO EXCEED IT.` · `A MESSAGE FROM THE CANNERY: WE ARE HIRING. WE ARE ALSO FIRING. MOSTLY FIRING.` · `IF YOU CAN HEAR THIS, YOU ARE TOO CLOSE TO MY VOICE.` · `THAT WAS THE LAST ONE. I HOPE YOU ARE HAPPY.`\n\n**Max barks.** Kill: `Claim closed.` `Pre-existing condition.` `You're not covered.` `Total loss.` Kick: `Deductible.` `Excess applies.` Reload: `One moment, please.` Low health: `My premium's going up.` Out of ammo: `That's not in the budget.`\n\n**Dame barks.** Follow: `Lead on.` Wait: `I shall wait. I charge for it.` Hide: `In a barrel. At my age.` Hurt: `I felt that in my portfolio.` `Deducted.` Grabbed: `Unhand me, you sardine!` You shoot near her: `Mind the coat.` You kick someone: `Vulgar. Do it again.` Idle: `I have sacked men for less.` `Do you always lurk?`\n\n**Pym radio hints** always start with the on-hold jingle and `Your call is important to Ostrander Mutual.`, then one hint for the current beat, such as: `Ms. Ransom. If you are surrounded, that is a Section 4 event. Kick something.` · `Our records show loudspeakers are not load-bearing. Shoot them.` · `The insured is a protected asset. Please stop leaving her in barrels.` · `Tide is not an Act of God if it was printed in advance.`\n\n**Claim Notes** (6 collectible files, 3-4 lines each, on the Files tab): a tide table with times crossed out; a cannery time sheet where every name is the same after week 9; Actuary's memo (`Skerry Holm: 0 claims since 1840. Investigate why this is suspicious.`); the Hymn of the Tithe (real dread, no joke); Fathom's receipt for 400 harpoons, signed with a bubble; page 40 of Dame Ottoline's application, on which someone has written `SIGN HERE, AND HERE, AND IN THE SEA`.\n\nChapter cards: `CLAIM 1: ACT OF GOD` · `CLAIM 2: WEAR AND TEAR` · `CLAIM 3: ACT OF COMMODORE` · `FINAL SETTLEMENT`. Islander barks are a made-up tongue, shown as small subtitles: `HAAL AN!` `SKARR!` `VOR THOLE!` `BRINNA!` `OV THE TIDE!` `VEN ULDA!`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Controls\n\nPad in standard mapping, with PlayStation names (Xbox glyphs: Cross=A, Circle=B, Square=X, Triangle=Y, L1=LB, R1=RB, L2=LT, R2=RT, Options=Menu, Create=View).\n\n| Action | Pad | Keyboard and mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Move | Left stick | WASD |\n| Look / aim | Right stick | Mouse (pointer lock) |\n| Aim (hold) | L2 | Right mouse |\n| Fire | R2 (while aiming) | Left mouse (while aiming) |\n| Knife | R1 | Left mouse (not aiming), or V |\n| Action: kick, open, vault, climb, pick up, talk, QTE 1 | Cross | E |\n| Run (hold) / quick 180° turn (tap with stick back) | Circle | Shift / Q |\n| Reload | Square | R |\n| The Case | Triangle | Tab or I |\n| Pause | Options | Esc or P |\n| Map tab | Create (on release, ignored if Options was pressed: Create+Options belongs to the hub) | M |\n| Next / previous weapon | D-pad up / down | Wheel or 1-4 |\n| Heal (best herb) | D-pad left | H |\n| Command the Dame (Follow/Wait; context: Hide, Boost, Release crane) | D-pad right | C |\n| Throw grenade at the laser dot (while aiming) | L1 | G |\n| Swap shoulder | R3 | T |\n| QTE 2 / dodge | Circle | Space |\n| Menus | Stick or D-pad, Cross confirm, Circle back, L1/R1 change tab, Square secondary, Triangle tertiary | Hover and click, Enter confirm, Esc back, Q/E change tab, wheel scrolls |\n\nThe mouse does what a PC player expects: it looks and aims, you click the world by shooting it (Tannoys, crates, barrels, thrown bottles), and a left click advances dialogue. Never bind Ctrl combinations. Call `input.preventKeys.add('Tab')`. Esc under pointer lock releases the lock and may not reach the page: pause on `pointerlockchange` when the lock is lost during play and you didn't release it yourself. Rumble with `gamepad.vibrationActuator?.playEffect('dual-rumble', …)` on shots, hits and QTEs, guarded so the test stub doesn't throw.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Systems\n\nAll numbers live in `src/data/tuning.js` and `src/data/*.js`. Treat them as first values and balance with the bot (§15) and the dev sliders (§12).\n\n### 4.1 Movement and camera\n- **Body:** `new CharacterController(physics, { position, speed: TUNING.runSpeed, radius: 0.3, halfHeight: 0.5 })`, tag its collider `noCamera` and `player`. Each fixed step call `setInput(moveVector, false, false)` and `fixedUpdate(dt)`. **[verified]** Velocity is `speed` × the move vector's length (half a vector at speed 4 moves at 2 m/s) and walls stop it, so build the controller with the top speed and scale the vector. Worlds are flat (ground at y=0), so there are no stairs: ladders and floors are scripted.\n- **Speeds:** walk 3.0 m/s at full tilt (under 55% tilt, 1.6 m/s), run 4.8, acceleration 18 m/s², turn 540°/s toward travel while exploring. Quick turn: 180° in 0.3 s.\n- **Camera:** yaw and pitch are game state, shared by explore and aim so nothing snaps. The engine's `third` rig orbits but has no shoulder offset, so replace `step` on the rig instance at runtime (the engine file stays untouched) **[verified]**:\n\n```js\n// In Area.setup. Engine.start used camera: { preset: 'third', fov: 55 }.\nconst rig = ctx.camera; rig.zoomable = false;\nrig.step = (u) => {\n  const c = game.cam; // { yaw, pitch, dist, up, side, fov } eased in update()\n  dir.set(Math.sin(c.yaw) * Math.cos(c.pitch), Math.sin(c.pitch), Math.cos(c.yaw) * Math.cos(c.pitch));\n  right.set(-Math.cos(c.yaw), 0, Math.sin(c.yaw));\n  pos.copy(u.target).addScaledVector(dir, -c.dist).addScaledVector(right, c.side * game.shoulder); pos.y += c.up;\n  tmp.copy(pos).sub(u.target); const len = tmp.length(); tmp.normalize();\n  const hit = u.world.raycast?.(u.target, tmp, len); // skips colliders tagged character / noCamera\n  if (hit != null) pos.copy(u.target).addScaledVector(tmp, Math.max(0.4, hit - 0.2));\n  rig.focus.copy(u.target); rig.camera.position.copy(pos);\n  if (rig.camera.fov !== c.fov) { rig.camera.fov = c.fov; rig.camera.updateProjectionMatrix(); }\n  rig.camera.lookAt(look.copy(pos).addScaledVector(dir, 12));\n};\n```\n- **Camera values [verified to frame well]:** `cameraTarget` = feet + 1.3 m. Explore: dist 4.0, up 0.45, side 0.55, fov 55. Aim: dist 2.9, up 0.1, side 0.95, fov 42 (ease over 0.16 s). Scope: fov 16. Hide Max's model when the camera is closer than 0.9 m to her. During cutscenes `rig.step` applies `timeline.camera()` instead.\n- **Look speeds:** the engine feeds the right stick into `input.mouseDelta` at `gamepadLookSpeed` (500 px/s). Recover the stick value with `v = delta / (500 * dt)`, apply `sign(v) * |v|^1.8`, then yaw at 2.2 rad/s exploring and 1.1 rad/s aiming (pitch at 60% of that). Mouse: 0.0026 rad/px exploring, 0.0016 aiming. Pitch range -0.7 to +0.7. Y invert is a setting.\n- **Pointer lock:** the engine only requests it for `first` and `free` cameras. During play, request it yourself in a `pointerdown` listener on `engine.gpu.renderer.domElement` (mouse pointers only), and catch the rejected promise. Chrome refuses a re-lock for about a second after Esc: show `CLICK TO AIM` until it succeeds. `input.mouseDelta` accumulates whenever the pointer is locked **[verified from the source]**. Release the lock in every menu so hover works.\n\n### 4.2 Aiming and shooting\n- Hold aim: Max plants her feet (move vector zero, faces camera yaw), and the laser comes on. `TUNING.aimWalkSpeed` is 0 by default; a slider lets you test otherwise.\n- Aim ray: `rig.rayAt(0, 0, o, d)`, then `ctx.physics.castRay(o, d, 80, ['player', 'enemy'])` for the world (so bullets still hit props tagged `noCamera`), then ray tests against hit zones. Nearest wins.\n- **Laser [verified]:** a `BoxGeometry(0.02, 0.02, 1)` with `glowMaterial(0xff3030)` stretched from the muzzle to the hit point, `castShadow = false`. On the HUD, project the hit point and draw a 3×3 red dot with a white centre. Dot colours: lime on head, sand on legs. Keep the sway: `yaw/pitch += sin/cos(t × 1.7…) × weapon.sway × TUNING.laserSway × 0.003`.\n- Firing: hitscan, `fireInterval`; recoil kick on pitch that recovers; `engine.shake.add(0.12)`; muzzle `ctx.lights.request({ position, color: 0xffc060, intensity: 8, radius: 6, lifetime: 0.06 })`; impact `ctx.particles.burst('impact', hit)`; `Decals` `scorch` on walls.\n- **Pad aim assist:** while the stick is moving, slow look speed by `TUNING.aimAssist` (0.35) when the laser is within 0.6° of a head or torso. Add 0.03 to head radius. Off for mouse.\n\n### 4.3 Hit zones, stagger, melee\nAfter each frame's animation update, cache each enemy's zones from its joints' world positions (**[verified]**: joints pose correctly in Node too): head sphere (Head joint + 0.13 m up × scale, radius 0.2 × scale), torso capsule (Pelvis to Head, r 0.22), arms and legs (two capsules each, r 0.09 and 0.11). Fixed-step shots test against the cache.\n\n| Zone | Damage × | Effect |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Head | 2.0 | 70% chance of **Stun** (hands to face, 1.5 s). Pistol has a 6% chance of a head pop (instant kill) |\n| Torso | 1.0 | Flinch 0.25 s; interrupts wind-up if the hit is ≥10 damage |\n| Arm | 0.7 | Drops what it holds: a held bottle explodes on them, a shield drops |\n| Leg | 0.7 | Two pistol hits' worth of leg damage: **Kneel** (1.7 s) |\n\n- **Kick** (prompt on a Stunned enemy within 2.6 m, in front): roundhouse, 120° cone, radius 2.6 m, 25 damage and knockdown to all in it, 40 to the target. Max is invulnerable for 0.5 s. `engine.hitstop(0.05)`, `shake.add(0.35)`. **Takedown** (prompt on a Kneeling enemy): hip throw, 60 damage, knockdown within 1.5 m.\n- **Knife:** 8 damage, 0.4 s, 2 m arc, ×3 on downed enemies, breaks crates for free.\n- Knockdown: `Fall`-type clip, up in 2.2 s. Death: `Death` clip or `new Ragdoll(physics, model, HERO_RAGDOLL).enable({ velocity })` for shotgun and explosion kills (**[verified]** on our puppets; call `sync()` instead of the mixer). Keep at most 8 ragdolls live. Corpses stay (Limpets need them; despawn the oldest above 20).\n- **Hit feedback:** swap the mesh materials to `glowMaterial(white)` for 2 frames (don't mutate shared toon materials), `Decals` `splat` in `plum`, `plum`/`teal` chunk particles. Head pop: scale the Head joint to 0 and burst. Stylised, not realistic.\n\n### 4.4 Weapons\nWeapon data: `src/data/weapons.js`. Footprint = cells in the Case.\n\n| Id | Name | Damage | Interval | Mag | Reload | Sway | Special | Footprint | Price |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| pistol | Ostrander .38 | 14 | 0.30 | 12 | 1.35 | 0.8 | head pop chance | 3×2 | start |\n| scatter | Bosun's Scattergun | 9 × 7 pellets | 0.95 | 6 | 2.4 | 0.4 | 5.5° cone, falls off past 9 m, knocks back | 7×2 | 900 |\n| rifle | Sealer's Rifle | 55 | 1.3 | 5 | 2.2 | 1.2 | Scope (fov 16), pierces one body | 8×2 | 1800 |\n| harpoon | Harpoon Gun | 90 | 1.2 | 1 | 2.0 | 0.5 | Pins an enemy to a wall or the ground for 4 s; bolt can be picked up again | 6×2 | 2600 |\n\n- Knife: always available, not in the Case. Grenades (1×2): **Magnesium Flare** (blinds a 6 m radius for 4 s, kills all Limpets in it), **Depth Charge** (explodes after 1.5 s, 80 damage, 4 m), **Whale-Oil Bottle** (burning pool, 3 s, 15 damage per second).\n- **Tuning at Mr. Fathom** (per weapon, 4 levels of Power, Rate, Reload, Capacity, price 300 → 1500). Filling all four unlocks a perk: pistol head pop 30%; scatter wider cone and pushes everyone in it; rifle pierces all; harpoon reloads itself in 1 s.\n\n### 4.5 The Case\n- Grid starts at 10×6, upgraded at the shop to 12×7 (1500) and 14×8 (4000). Cell = 14 art pixels. Weapons, ammo, herbs and grenades take cells; **Valuables** and **Key Items** are lists with no footprint, on their own tabs.\n- Screen (time frozen): the grid on the left, a big icon, name and 2 lines of text on the right. Tabs: CASE · VALUABLES · KEY ITEMS · MAP · FILES · RADIO. Pick up with Cross or click, rotate with Square / right mouse / wheel, drop with Triangle, Use/Equip/Combine via Cross on a stationary item (small 3-item menu). `ARRANGE` packs everything automatically (hold R1 / key F; first-fit decreasing).\n- Picking up with no room opens the Case in arrange mode with the new item in hand; the player places it or leaves it on the ground. The ground item stays.\n- Ammo stacks in its footprint: pistol box 2×1 (max 50), shells 2×1 (max 24), rifle rounds 2×1 (max 20), bolts 3×1 (max 6).\n\n### 4.6 Items, treasure, loot\n- **Herbs (1×2):** Samphire (green, +30%), Dulse (red, heals nothing alone), Sea Holly (yellow, +10 max health when mixed). Combine: S+S 60%, S+S+S 100%, S+D 100%, S+D+H 100% and +10 max. Company First-Aid Tin (1×2): 100%, sold at 800.\n- **Treasure (Valuables):** Pearl 500, Black Pearl 1500, Sea Glass Set 400, Amber 700, Scrimshaw Tusk 900, Gold Tooth 150, Empty Reliquary 1200. **Combining:** the Reliquary has 3 sockets (Pearl, Black Pearl, Amber) and is worth 8000 when full. Mr. Fathom pays full listed value for treasure and half for everything else.\n- **Doubloons:** currency, auto-collected. Mr. Fathom takes nothing else (`He doesn't take plastic`).\n- **Loot Director** (`src/game/loot.js`): when a crate or corpse drops, weight by need: little ammo for carried weapons → that ammo; under 50% health with no herbs → Samphire; otherwise Doubloons (25-80). Crates always drop something. `TUNING.lootRate` and `moneyRate` scale it. The director is the balance safety net: it should be hard, not impossible, to run dry.\n- **Tannoys (15):** shooting all gives a free perk from Mr. Fathom at 5, 10 and 15 (+1000 doubloons, the Case upgrade, a Black Pearl). The Map tab can show them after buying a chart (300).\n\n### 4.7 Mr. Fathom (shop)\nSix appearances (`m` on the maps). Green lantern and a low bubbling loop you hear before you see him. Screen tabs BUY · SELL · TUNE. At most 6 rows at a time, one big item panel, his helmet portrait and a line of text with gibberish voice. Stock grows per chapter. Music switches to the shop song. Prices are in data.\n\n### 4.8 Enemies\nEvery human is a puppet on `HERO_RIG` (§8). Bodies are kinematic capsules (r 0.28, tags `noCamera`, `enemy`) moved along a `NavGrid` flow field with local separation (0.55 m). Own interpolation between fixed steps: `model.position.lerpVectors(prev, cur, ctx.physics.alpha)`.\n\n| Id | Name | HP | Walk m/s | Attack | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| gaffer | Islander | 34 | 1.1-1.5 | Gaff hook 14; wind-up 0.7 s; 20% try a grab (6/s until you mash free) | Three palettes, some with the band bright, some dim |\n| netwife | Net-Wife | 28 | 1.2 | Throws a weighted net at 8 m: slows you 40% for 3 s, can be shot mid-air | Headscarf |\n| bottler | Bottler | 30 | 1.0 | Lobs a whale-oil bottle (arc telegraphed, shootable, 18 + fire) | Shoot the raised bottle: it burns him |\n| runner | Deckhand | 36 | 2.8 | Boathook lunge 16 | From chapter 2. Throws off your aim timing |\n| carrier | Carrier | 60 | 1.6 | Goes for the Dame, shoulders her, walks to the nearest spawn door. 12 s until she is lost | Shoot him: she drops and runs to you |\n| flenser | The Flenser | 220 | 2.2 (lunge 5) | Saw: **kills outright** at full swing (Assisted: 80) unless you QTE dodge | Staggered only by head hits, scatter or explosives. Saw loop (spatial) is heard 30 m away, through walls (`muffle`). Drops 300 and a key item |\n| limpet | Limpet | 15 | 3.0 | Latches: 4/s | 25% of head kills release one. It scuttles to the nearest corpse; if it arrives, that corpse rises as a Re-Salted (fast, 40 HP). Flare kills instantly |\n| monk | Cowled Monk | 70 | 1.3 | Flail 18, wind-up 0.9 | Shield blocks the front; shoot the arm, or kick, to drop it |\n| knight | Reliquary Knight | 300, helmet 40 | 0.9 | Halberd 35, wide | Armour sparks and blocks body shots. Shoot the helmet off, then the head. In the crypt: blind, hunts by sound |\n| drowned | Drowned | 35 | 1.2 | Grabs legs: slows and mashes | Rises out of water on the causeway |\n| harpooner | Boat Harpooner | 50 | n/a | Straight harpoon 22, red glint before firing, shootable | Rides a rowboat beside the causeway and the launch |\n\n**Crowd AI.** A plain state machine per enemy: `WORK` (chores until alerted) → `ALERT` (shout, 0.5 s; alerts within 15 m) → `APPROACH` → `CIRCLE` (hold 3-5 m if no token) → `WINDUP` → `ATTACK` → `RECOVER`; plus `STUN`, `KNEEL`, `FLINCH`, `KNOCKDOWN`, `GETUP`, `GRAB`, `VAULT`, `CLIMB`, `BASH`, `DEAD`. **Attack tokens:** only `TUNING.attackTokens` (2) may be in WINDUP or ATTACK; thrown attacks take 1 token shared across throwers. `maxActive` caps enemies awake per area; others wait at spawn doors. **Adaptive rank** (hidden, 1-5, starting at 2): up on long no-damage streaks and high accuracy, down on each death; rank changes tokens ±1, wind-up ±0.1 s and the wave interval. Show it in dev mode.\n\nDoors, windows, ladders and floors for enemies: flow fields treat `D` and `W` as open. An enemy arriving at a closed door plays `BASH` (door breaks in 6 s or fewer if several bash); at a window it plays `VAULT` and moves through. Ladders and floors: one `NavGrid` per floor plus a link table; an enemy on the wrong floor walks to the nearest link and plays `CLIMB`.\n\n### 4.9 Dame Ottoline\nA `Humanoid` with her own AI (`src/game/companion.js`). Walks 2.6, runs 3.8. Health 100 (dev slider); hurt also adds to the **Deductions** ledger.\n- **Follow** (default): stay 2-4 m behind Max; side-step out of the laser line; duck when an enemy is within 3 m.\n- **Wait:** stands still. **Hide** (context near a barrel or lobster pot): climbs in; safe until called; comic barks.\n- **Boost** (`u`): Max boosts her up to a high hoist chain. **Winch** (`w`), **Crane** (`k`): she operates machines.\n- **Grabbed:** by Carriers. Screen edge warning, `DAME TAKEN` timer (12 s). Lost = game over. Hit by your own bullets = deduction and damage (accident forgiven for scatter at range).\n- Her health shows under Max's. Dead = `CLAIM DENIED`.\n\n### 4.10 Context actions\nOne system (`src/game/interact.js`): each frame pick the best target within 1.6 m and ±70° of facing; show one prompt with the current device's glyph. Priority: Kick/Takedown > ladder knock > door > window > push > pick up > talk > telegraph.\n- **Door:** walking into it with Action kicks it open (0.3 s). An enemy right behind it is knocked down. Collider removed, `nav.setOpen`. Door tween in `ctx.tweens`.\n- **Window (`W`):** vault through, 0.7 s, invulnerable. Enemies follow by vaulting. Glass breaks once.\n- **Ladder:** 1.2 s up or down, exposed. **Knock down** an outside ladder (`E`) from above: it falls with anyone on it.\n- **Push (`p`):** wardrobe slides along one axis at 1 m/s; updates nav; blocks the door until bashed.\n- **Drop:** from upper windows to the ground (0.6 s; onto the hay cart, no damage; otherwise 10).\n- **Tannoy:** any shot; sparks; falls silent mid-line.\n- **Breakables:** `Breakables` from the engine for crates, or a simple swap to chunks. Brine Barrels (red band) explode: 3 m, 60 damage to everyone, chains.\n\n### 4.11 Quick-time events\n`src/game/qte.js`: a large glyph (device-correct) in a shrinking ring at screen centre, `engine.timeScale = 0.5` while open. Types: press (window 0.9 s; dev slider), mash (fill a bar), alternate (Cross/Circle). Used in: Flenser dodge, grabs, Bosun sweep, the belt fight, launch. Fail = hit or death; failed cutscene QTEs restart with a new quip, no reload.\n\n### 4.12 Cutscenes, dialogue, radio\n- `Timeline` drives shots, cues, lines and letterbox **[verified shape]**: `tl.update(dt)`, `tl.camera()`, `tl.line()`, `tl.bars()`, `tl.skip()`. Wrap it in `src/game/cutscene.js`. All skippable (hold Cross / Space 0.6 s, with a small bar). Cues that change the world aren't `cosmetic`.\n- **Dialogue box:** bottom band, name in the speaker's colour, up to 3 lines of 70 characters, typed at 30 chars/s with voice blips (§10). Confirm completes or advances.\n- **Radio:** 32×32 portraits left and right, world dimmed but running unless the area is safe. From the Case RADIO tab (only in dry rooms for long hints) or story-triggered.\n- **Objectives:** small top-left line, fades after 6 s, back on pause.\n\n### 4.13 Saving, dying, difficulty, results\n- **Telegraph key** (`t`) in safe rooms: enemies don't enter; calm music; save slot. Autosave at each area start and before bosses. `localStorage` keys prefixed with a slug from `src/config.js`. In a hub session the client gives an empty storage: don't special-case it.\n- **Death:** slow fall, sting, a big rubber stamp `CLAIM DENIED`, then Continue (last checkpoint) or Quit. Checkpoint data: Run state plus area flags (killed set-piece enemies, opened doors, picked items).\n- **Difficulty** chosen on New Claim: Assisted (enemy damage ×0.6, aim assist ×1.5, saw non-lethal, loot ×1.3), Standard, Professional (enemy damage ×1.4, tokens +1, loot ×0.8).\n- **Claim Form** after each chapter (not dense: 5 big lines): TIME, ACCURACY, HEADSHOTS, KICKS, DEDUCTIONS, then a stamp APPROVED / PENDING / DENIED with a thud, and bonus Doubloons.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Chapters and maps\n\nTarget: 35-45 minutes for a first run, every feature shown at least twice. Each area is one `Game` loaded with `engine.loadGame`.\n\n### Map format\nMaps are painter commands, then rows of characters. Build them with `src/game/mapPaint.js`, keep them in `src/data/levels/*.js`, and use the same rows for geometry, colliders, nav and the Map screen. **All maps below passed a reachability check: every open cell can be reached from `a`.**","numLines":200,"startLine":151,"totalLines":885}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CtFvFh2dt2nEnULzrCAdjd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke2pUMoYspj3aGRT1Lp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UqnKhGkefNTgn7aUwznqVL","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","offset":351,"limit":250},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11272,"cache_read_input_tokens":34165,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11272},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"d12e793f-7ff4-4e01-b308-7e55c8284629","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:04.929Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke2pEiogoYBaTDSnpZV","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UqnKhGkefNTgn7aUwznqVL":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","offset":351,"limit":250}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UqnKhGkefNTgn7aUwznqVL","type":"tool_result","content":"351\t\n352\t- `map name W H fill`: a grid of `fill`. `R x0 y0 x1 y1 c`: filled rectangle. `B x0 y0 x1 y1 wall floor`: walls round a floor. `P x y c`: one cell. Commands on a line are separated by ` | `, in order.\n353\t- 1 cell = 1 m. World: `x = col + 0.5 - W/2`, `z = row + 0.5 - H/2`, north is -Z. `NavGrid.fromRows(rows, { cell: 1, origin: [-W/2, 0, -H/2], blocked: '#T~HBSG' })`. Open `B`, `S` and `G` cells with `setOpen` when they break or open. `D`, `W`, `E` and `L` stay open in nav and are solid only for Max until used (§4.8).\n354\t\n355\t| Char | Meaning | Char | Meaning |\n356\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n357\t| `#` | Stone wall or cliff, 3 m+, solid | `D` | Door, solid until opened |\n358\t| `T` | Timber or plaster wall, 3 m, solid | `G` | Gate, shut until the story opens it |\n359\t| `~` | Deep water. An invisible wall stops Max. Enemies kicked in sink and die | `S` | Roll-up shutter |\n360\t| `H` | Low cover, 1 m, blocks walking but not bullets above 1 m | `W` | Window, vaultable |\n361\t| `.` | Cobbles | `B` | Breakable crate or barrel, solid until broken |\n362\t| `,` | Dirt or turf | `L` / `E` | Inside ladder / outside ladder at an upper window |\n363\t| `=` | Planks | `c` | Conveyor belt, walkable, carries whoever stands on it (add velocity by map cell) |\n364\t| `:` | Indoor boards | `%` | Shallow water, walkable, 70% speed |\n365\t| `_` | Flagstones | `r` | Crane rail (walkable) |\n366\t\n367\tMarkers (walkable): `a` start · `1-5` spawn doors · `m` Mr. Fathom · `t` telegraph · `y` Tannoy · `$` treasure chest · `p` pushable wardrobe · `n` net-mender · `d` the Dame · `w` winch · `u` boost spot · `k` crane cab · `z` crane drop zone · `o` boss entrance · `s` statue · `q` clue mosaic · `v` trapdoor · `h` hiding niche · `l` lever.\n368\t\n369\t```text\n370\tmap quay 64 48 #\n371\tR 2 2 47 45 . | R 3 2 21 14 , | R 48 2 51 45 = | R 52 0 63 47 ~ | R 52 30 54 32 =\n372\tR 55 30 57 44 = | R 54 4 60 10 # | B 22 4 37 13 T : | R 29 13 30 13 D | P 22 8 W | P 37 8 W\n373\tP 24 6 L | R 31 15 33 16 H | B 42 4 47 11 T : | R 47 5 47 10 : | P 44 7 m | B 39 15 46 21 T :\n374\tR 42 21 43 21 D | P 42 15 W | B 38 30 46 38 T : | R 41 30 42 30 D | P 46 34 W | P 43 35 n\n375\tB 5 16 16 30 # _ | R 16 22 16 23 D | P 7 18 t | R 26 21 27 22 H | R 31 27 33 29 H\n376\tR 15 38 19 39 H | R 23 38 27 39 H | R 31 38 35 39 H | R 15 42 19 43 H | R 23 42 27 43 H\n377\tR 31 42 35 43 H | R 3 33 4 34 H | R 7 33 8 34 H | R 3 38 4 39 H | R 7 38 8 39 H | R 6 6 7 11 H\n378\tR 11 6 12 11 H | R 16 6 17 11 H | R 0 8 1 9 G | R 18 32 24 35 T | R 30 32 35 35 T\n379\tR 17 31 17 37 T | P 27 11 p | P 20 18 y | P 35 19 y | P 28 31 y | P 44 24 y | P 10 13 y\n380\tP 49 40 y | P 44 18 $ | P 14 28 $ | P 5 42 $ | P 56 43 a | P 3 3 1 | P 47 3 2 | P 3 44 3\n381\tP 46 44 4 | P 50 26 5 | P 44 41 B | P 45 41 B | P 40 43 B | P 12 3 B | P 13 3 B | P 49 12 B\n382\tmap loft 16 10 T\n383\tR 1 1 14 8 : | P 2 2 L | P 4 9 W | P 10 9 W | P 8 0 W | P 15 5 E | P 0 5 E\n384\tmap road 22 64 #\n385\tR 8 1 13 62 , | R 4 44 17 54 , | R 6 47 9 47 H | R 12 47 15 47 H | R 0 26 21 33 ~\n386\tR 10 26 11 33 = | R 4 10 17 22 , | R 1 36 7 40 , | R 4 20 6 22 H | R 15 12 17 14 H\n387\tR 10 0 11 0 D | P 10 61 a | P 5 16 m | P 2 38 $ | P 9 52 y | P 13 18 y\n388\tmap cannery 48 36 #\n389\tR 18 27 30 34 _ | R 24 35 25 35 D | R 6 10 41 25 _ | R 23 26 25 26 _ | R 10 13 37 14 c\n390\tR 10 21 37 22 c | R 10 17 15 18 H | R 20 17 27 18 H | R 32 17 37 18 H | R 1 12 4 20 _\n391\tR 5 15 5 17 D | R 34 2 44 8 _ | R 37 9 38 9 D | P 41 4 d | R 4 2 14 8 _ | R 9 9 10 9 D | P 6 4 w\n392\tP 12 10 u | R 22 2 26 9 _ | R 23 1 25 1 S | R 42 16 42 18 D | R 43 14 46 20 _\n393\tB 31 26 39 34 # _ | R 31 30 31 31 D | P 36 29 t | P 20 33 m | P 24 34 a | P 43 3 $ | P 2 19 $\n394\tP 40 11 y | P 8 24 y | P 2 16 1 | P 45 17 2 | P 24 28 3\n395\tmap yard 36 36 #\n396\tR 2 2 33 33 . | R 7 8 9 10 H | R 26 8 28 10 H | R 7 25 9 27 H | R 26 25 28 27 H\n397\tR 16 12 19 13 H | R 16 22 19 23 H | R 4 18 31 18 r | R 13 17 15 19 z | R 22 17 24 19 z\n398\tP 3 18 k | R 17 34 18 35 D | R 17 0 18 1 G | P 17 32 a | P 17 4 o | P 31 31 m | P 4 4 $\n399\tP 31 4 y\n400\tmap causeway 16 96 ~\n401\tR 3 2 12 93 % | R 5 2 10 93 . | R 0 62 4 68 , | R 11 34 15 40 , | R 6 0 9 1 G | R 5 94 10 95 ,\n402\tP 7 94 a | P 1 65 m | P 14 37 $ | P 12 37 y | P 4 75 1 | P 11 58 2 | P 4 45 3 | P 11 25 4\n403\tP 4 15 5\n404\tmap abbey 44 40 #\n405\tR 8 8 35 31 _ | R 12 12 31 27 , | R 21 32 23 38 _ | R 21 39 23 39 D | P 22 38 a | R 20 7 23 7 G\n406\tR 20 1 23 6 _ | P 21 3 t | R 21 0 22 0 D | P 14 14 s | P 29 14 s | P 22 25 s | P 22 19 q\n407\tR 12 12 12 12 H | R 16 12 16 12 H | R 27 12 27 12 H | R 31 12 31 12 H | R 12 27 12 27 H\n408\tR 16 27 16 27 H | R 27 27 27 27 H | R 31 27 31 27 H | R 12 18 12 18 H | R 31 18 31 18 H\n409\tR 12 22 12 22 H | R 31 22 31 22 H | P 10 20 v | R 1 10 6 34 _ | R 3 14 4 15 H | R 3 20 4 21 H\n410\tR 3 26 4 27 H | P 1 16 h | P 6 22 h | P 1 28 h | P 3 33 l | R 7 30 7 31 D | R 36 19 36 20 D\n411\tR 37 14 42 26 _ | P 40 18 m | P 41 25 $ | P 2 11 $ | P 10 30 y | P 33 10 y | P 34 9 1 | P 9 9 2\n412\tP 34 30 3\n413\tmap nave 28 48 #\n414\tR 2 2 25 45 _ | R 8 10 9 11 H | R 18 10 19 11 H | R 8 18 9 19 H | R 18 18 19 19 H\n415\tR 8 26 9 27 H | R 18 26 19 27 H | R 8 34 9 35 H | R 18 34 19 35 H | R 11 5 16 7 H\n416\tR 13 46 14 47 D | R 26 4 27 5 G | P 13 44 a | P 13 12 o | P 3 3 $ | P 24 44 y\n417\t```\n418\t\n419\tThe quay, printed for orientation, with repeated rows left out (north up; the pier is bottom right, the Net Loft top centre, the chapel left, the sea right, the Foghorn rock top right):\n420\t\n421\t```text\n422\t    0         1         2         3         4         5         6\n423\t  0 ####################################################~~~~~~~~~~~~\n424\t  2 ##.,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,..........................====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n425\t  3 ##.1,,,,,,,,BB,,,,,,,,.........................2====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n426\t  4 ##.,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,TTTTTTTTTTTTTTTT....TTTTTT====~~#######~~~\n427\t  6 ##.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,T:L::::::::::::T....T:::::====~~#######~~~\n428\t  7 ##.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,T::::::::::::::T....T:m:::====~~#######~~~\n429\t  8 GG.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,W::::::::::::::W....T:::::====~~#######~~~\n430\t 11 ##.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,T::::p:::::::::T....TTTTTT====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n431\t 13 ##.,,,,,,,y,,,,,,,,,,,TTTTTTTDDTTTTTTT..........====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n432\t 14 ##.,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,..........................====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n433\t 15 ##.............................HHH.....TTTWTTTT.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n434\t 16 ##...############..............HHH.....T::::::T.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n435\t 18 ##...#_t________#...y..................T::::$:T.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n436\t 21 ##...#__________#.........HH...........TTTDDTTT.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n437\t 22 ##...#__________D.........HH....................====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n438\t 24 ##...#__________#...........................y...====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n439\t 27 ##...#__________#..............HHH..............====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n440\t 28 ##...#________$_#..............HHH..............====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n441\t 30 ##...############.....................TTTDDTTTT.==========~~~~~~\n442\t 31 ##...............T..........y.........T:::::::T.==========~~~~~~\n443\t 32 ##...............TTTTTTTT.....TTTTTT..T:::::::T.==========~~~~~~\n444\t 34 ##.HH..HH........TTTTTTTT.....TTTTTT..T:::::::W.====~~~===~~~~~~\n445\t 35 ##...............TTTTTTTT.....TTTTTT..T::::n::T.====~~~===~~~~~~\n446\t 38 ##.HH..HH......HHHHH...HHHHH...HHHHH..TTTTTTTTT.====~~~===~~~~~~\n447\t 42 ##...$.........HHHHH...HHHHH...HHHHH............====~~~===~~~~~~\n448\t 43 ##.............HHHHH...HHHHH...HHHHH....B.......====~~~=a=~~~~~~\n449\t 44 ##.3..........................................4.====~~~===~~~~~~\n450\t 46 ####################################################~~~~~~~~~~~~\n451\t```\n452\t\n453\tThe loft is the Net Loft's upper floor: offset col 22, row 4, floor at y = 3.2. Solid `T` blocks are uninhabited houses with roofs. Dress generously (§8).\n454\t\n455\t### Chapter 1: CLAIM 1: ACT OF GOD. Mourne Quay, bruised dusk (10-12 min)\n456\t\n457\t1. **Arrival.** Cutscene on the pier (script). Control at `a`. Hints fade as you do them: move, look, run.\n458\t2. **First Tannoy** at (49,40): the Commodore's line. Hint: aim and shoot it. Max says `Noted.`\n459\t3. **First cottage** (door 41-42,30). Hint: Action kicks doors. Net-mender scene, first fight: hints for head or legs, then the kick prompt. Then the boat burns, and 2 Islanders break in through the door while a window hint shows `W` (46,34): vault out to the quay.\n460\t4. **Quay front:** crate (49,12), 3 Islanders, first Doubloons and herb. Net shed `m`: Mr. Fathom's intro; first shop; first Case tip (pick up shells with a full-ish Case: place and rotate).\n461\t5. **The Square.** Entering from row 14 or the main street (rows 22-29) triggers a 6 s cutscene: 14 Islanders round the bonfire with an effigy in a suit. Siege starts.\n462\t6. **The Siege (the demo's signature).** Total 30 Islanders and 4 Bottlers from 1:00; `maxActive` 12; spawn doors 1-5. The Flenser arrives at 1:30 from door 2: you hear the saw first. Tools: the Net Loft door (29-30,13) with the wardrobe `p` to push across it; vault its windows (22,8), (37,8); inside ladder to the loft; loft windows look down on the Square; Islanders raise outside ladders to `E` at 1:00 and again every 25 s, knock them down; drop onto the hay cart (31-33,15). Three loops let you kite: Square → row 14 → quay → main street; Square → drying yard → back lane → row 14; Square → lane (25-29,32-35) → market → graveyard → west side.\n463\t7. **The Foghorn.** After 3:30, or 34 kills, whichever comes first (never leave the player waiting). The horn from the rock at (57,7) (camera shake, gulls scatter, all sound drops). Script scene: tools drop as props, every enemy walks to the nearest `~` cell, wades in and sinks, the Flenser last. Silence.\n464\t8. **Aftermath.** Free roam, loot left on the ground, `$` at (44,18), (14,28), (5,42). Chapel = safe room with telegraph `t`, Claim Note. West Gate `G` is now open. Exit: Claim Form, load Road.\n465\t\n466\t### Chapter 2: CLAIM 2: WEAR AND TEAR. Rain at night (14-16 min)\n467\t\n468\t**Salt Road (`road`).** Roadblock clearing: 6 Islanders, 1 Bottler on a wagon, Brine Barrels to shoot. Side alcove `$` (2,38) with an ambush. **The bridge** (10-11,26-33): 2 m wide over the gorge, 3 Bottlers on ledges ahead (elevated, unreachable, shoot the bottles); kick enemies off the edge (`~` kills them). North clearing: Mr. Fathom in a beached rowboat, the Rifle on sale, 4 Deckhands, a far Tannoy to snipe at (13,18). Door to the cannery.\n469\t\n470\t**Thole Cannery (`cannery`).** The door locks behind you. Telegraph office, Fathom in the bay.\n471\t1. **The Hall.** Two belts running opposite ways, 1.5 m/s, carcasses swinging from a moving overhead rail, machines as cover, 10 Islanders and 2 Bottlers. Riding a belt moves you and them.\n472\t2. **The Flenser again.** Saw room door (5,15-17) bursts open. Kill him for the Cold Room key.\n473\t3. **Cold Room** `d`: no music, breath particles. Meeting the Dame. Escort begins; hint for Follow/Wait.\n474\t4. **Boost** `u` (12,10): Winch Room is chained from a high hoist. Max boosts her; she pulls; the door opens. First Carrier ambush from door 2: teach shooting him off.\n475\t5. **Hold the Winch.** She takes `w` (6,4), the shutter `S` rises 1% per second (90 s; pauses while she's disturbed). Waves from 1, 2, 3 with Deckhands and a Carrier. Max defends the door (9-10,9) and hall. At 100% she runs to the corridor.\n476\t6. **The belt:** crossing the hall to the shutter, Max is hooked off her feet by Mate Ansgar's gaff, and they go down together on the belt, riding toward the can press at its east end. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11). He goes into the press. A can rolls out. Telegraph in the north corridor (autosave).\n477\t\n478\t**Cannery Yard (`yard`).** Boss: the Bosun (§6). After: Dame's confession (script), Mr. Fathom at `m`, Claim Form, north gate.\n479\t\n480\t### Chapter 3: CLAIM 3: ACT OF COMMODORE. Moonlit, then candlelit (12-15 min)\n481\t\n482\t**The Causeway (`causeway`).** A 90 m stone road to the abbey as the tide comes in. Timer 240 s, shown as a tide gauge. Water level goes from -0.6 to +0.9 (`WaterSurface` y; Max in water over road ankle: 70% speed; over 0.7: 2 damage/s). Rocks at rows 34-40 and 62-68 stay dry (Fathom and `$`). Drowned rise as you pass spawn points; two rowboats with Harpooners shadow you at 10 m. At the gate the Dame turns a wheel for 6 s while you hold. Missing the deadline drowns you.\n483\t\n484\t**The Abbey (`abbey`).** Monks and 2 Reliquary Knights, moonlit cloister.\n485\t1. **Lens puzzle:** three lamp statues `s`; each rotates in 45° steps with Action (1.2 s, exposed). The floor mosaic `q` shows which way each must face so all three beams hit the lenses over gate `G`. Beams are glow boxes. Solved: gate opens with a heavy sound.\n486\t2. **Trapdoor** `v` (10,20): as you cross the arcade, the floor drops under the Dame. Cut to the crypt.\n487\t3. **The Dame alone (90-120 s).** You control her: walk 2.2 m/s, hold run for 3.2 m/s (loud), Action to whack (stuns 2 s, once per 8 s), `h` niches to hide, floor lamps to throw for a noise distraction. 3 blind Knights patrol the hall, hearing radius: run 9 m, walk 4 m, still 0. Two hits and you restart the segment. Horror beat: low drone, no music, Pym on hold. Goal: lever `l` (3,33), then door (7,30-31). Then control returns to Max, finishing a fight in the arcade as the Dame arrives.\n488\t4. **Armoury** (door 36,19-20): Fathom, `$`, last stock. Vestibule telegraph, door to the nave.\n489\t\n490\t**The Nave (`nave`).** Final boss (§6). The side gate opens.\n491\t\n492\t**The Launch (on rails, 80-100 s).** The island is coming down. The Dame drives; Max stands on the stern deck with free aim and the Harpoon Gun or Rifle. A spline through sea stacks, `WaterSurface` with `WAVES_CHOPPY`, 14 m/s. Shoot: mines, pursuing boats' Harpooners, falling rock (a QTE if you miss), Limpets crawling onto the deck (kick). End: arch collapse QTE. Dawn (`skyAt(6.5)`). **Ending** (script), Final Claim Form, credits with the on-hold jingle.\n493\t\n494\t### Dressing and the world's edge\n495\tEvery area needs a backdrop: far silhouettes (dark low-poly cliffs, abbey on its rock, the Foghorn tower) so the world doesn't end at a plane. Fog colour must match the background. No bare wall over 6 m; a prop or two per 4×4 m of floor; vertical things (Tannoy poles, lamp posts, drying racks, chimneys, masts) everywhere. Performance budget is unlimited: be lavish, with up to 16 lights and `quality: 'high'`.\n496\t\n497\t---\n498\t\n499\t## 6. Bosses\n500\t\n501\t### The Bosun (cannery yard, rain)\n502\t4 m tall (`HERO_RIG` puppet, root scale 2.6). Three brine sacs on his back (180 HP each) that glow when exposed. Weak everywhere else: 25% damage from the front, 100% on sacs.\n503\t- **Attacks:** Anchor Sweep (range 7 m, wind-up 1.0 s, QTE dodge when close, 45). Anchor Throw (18 m, wind-up 1.2 s, lands with a 2 m blast, chain drags back over 2 s, 40). Stomp (3 m, 25 + knockdown). Grab (within 3 m, mash, 60). Throws crate stacks when you hide behind them for over 4 s (`H` stacks can break).\n504\t- **The crane:** the Dame sits in the cab `k`. The pallet travels along the rail on its own between drop zones `z`, painted yellow. A lamp lights when the pallet is over a zone. Press Command when he is under it. Hit: he's on his knees for 8 s, sacs exposed and ×2 damage. A harpoon through the chain adds 3 s. The pallet reloads in 15 s. Brine Barrels also stagger him for 4 s.\n505\t- **Phases:** each sac burst makes him 15% faster. Phase 2 adds 4 Islanders every 40 s. Phase 3 adds a double sweep and heavier rain.\n506\t- **End:** falls with a huge shake (`hitstop`, `shockwave`), drops a Black Pearl and 2000 Doubloons. Commodore, on Tannoy: `...HE ONLY HAD THE ONE.`\n507\t\n508\t### The Commodore's Bathysphere (flooded nave)\n509\tA walking brass ball on legs (`HERO_RIG` root scale 2.4; brass ball torso, porthole showing an armchair and a figure at a microphone, pipes, steam `smoke` particles). Water rises by phase.\n510\t- **Phase 1, Plumbing.** Four valves (shoulders, hips: 140 HP each, glowing red). Attacks: Steam Jet (6 m cone, 30 + slow), Stomp (AoE), Rivet Burst (3 shots, shootable), **Charge** down the aisle (whistle tell, 8 m/s): if he hits a column (`H`), it shatters and he's stunned for 3 s. Each burst valve: 4 Monks, and water rises 0.15 m.\n511\t- **Phase 2, Hatch.** All valves gone: he sags. Three hatch locks (60 HP each). Shoot them while he flails; then a Kick prompt (cutscene: Max climbs, tears the hatch).\n512\t- **Phase 3, The Mother.** Out he falls, and the thing on his neck bursts out and takes the altar: a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, still broadcasting. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and births Limpets; flares kill them all at once. The brass microphone on his chest has 200 HP: shooting it cuts him off mid-sentence one last time, and this is the horror beat, because the voice carries on without it. Then the eye under his jaw has 400 HP. Then **Final Settlement:** QTE (press, press, mash); stamp; `Claim denied.`\n513\t- The Font cracks, water floods, side gate opens, run to the Launch.\n514\t\n515\t---\n516\t\n517\t## 7. Night Shift and multiplayer\n518\t\n519\t### Mode: Night Shift\n520\tA 4-minute hold-out on the quay map at night in the rain, solo or co-op: keep each other alive until dawn. Everyone is a Max in their seat's colour (scarf and name tag). Loadout: pistol and scattergun with fixed ammo and tuned starting values; crates and drops give ammo, herbs and grenades. Waves by clock (cap 24 enemies alive): 0:00 8 Islanders; 1:00 Bottlers; 2:00 a Flenser; 3:00 two Flensers and Deckhands; 3:40 the horn warning; 4:00 **dawn: the Foghorn sounds, everyone walks into the sea, and you win.** Downed: 20 s bleed-out, hold Action 2 s to revive; bleed-out ends your shift for that round (solo: over). Score: hits, kills, head and kick bonus, combo multiplier. Standalone solo score goes on a local board.\n521\t\n522\tFrom the title menu: `NIGHT SHIFT` → SOLO / HOST PARTY / JOIN PARTY.\n523\t\n524\t### Hub integration **[verified with a minimal engine game: 2 players; 4 players at latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5; host-leave; server: all pass `__hubCheck`]**\n525\t- Mode **`shared-world`**, seats `[1, 4]`, own card. Follow https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md. Vendor `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same folder into `vendor/hub/` once. The README is short; read it. `examples/arena.html` in the same folder is a complete shared-world game, including the server case.\n526\t- In `<head>`, in this order: `<meta charset>`; the `session.js` text **unmodified, not through esbuild**, as the first script; then the tags:\n527\t```html\n528\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n529\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n530\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n531\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Hold the quay together until dawn\">\n532\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move, hold aim, fire; kick stunned enemies; revive friends\">\n533\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n534\t<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n535\t```\n536\t- Flow:\n537\t```js\n538\tasync function boot() {\n539\t  if (window.AIHub?.active) {\n540\t    const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n541\t    if (info) return startSession(info); // straight to the card: no title, menu or attract\n542\t  }\n543\t  return startStandalone();\n544\t}\n545\t```\n546\t`startSession`: `Engine.start` (seed from `info.seed`; no WebGPU: `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`), build the quay, show **our card**, then `AIHub.ready()` with no key press. Card shows: the game's name, the players in colour with ready ticks, how to win, this player's controls with the right glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Enter/Cross/tap → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle/M/tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round. Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0` (show the 3-2-1 from `start`).\n547\t- In a session: no quitting or restarting, no pausing the world (Options opens a small Settings overlay while the round runs), no attract, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no other network, no chat or emotes. Use `AIHub.rng(label)` where copies must agree. Ignore Options while Create is held.\n548\t- **Round end:** host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })` once: on dawn, on all down, or on `time-up` (immediately, within `graceMs`). `standings` lists every player once, by score, best first (`[[2],[0,3],[1]]`); `won: true` at dawn; `stats` up to 6 per player (Score, Kills, Heads, Kicks, Revives, Accuracy); `awards` up to 3 per player, title ≤24 and detail ≤40 characters (`Chief Adjuster`, `Steel Toe`, `Good Samaritan`). On `end`: stop input and sound (`stopMusic`, `stopLoops`), send nothing more. `leave`: remove that player; the hub voids the round if the host leaves.\n549\t- **`AIHub.server`** (a copy with no player of its own): run the host simulation with no local player, a slow overview camera, no local input. `info.isHost` is true and `info.me` isn't in `players`. Never assume a local player exists on the host.\n550\t\n551\t### The session interface and the game on its own\n552\tTASK.md wants multiplayer for AI Hub and for the game on its own. Write the co-op against one small interface, `session`, shaped exactly like `AIHub`: `me, players, host, isHost, server, seed, limitMs, send(data, {to, reliable}), on(event, fn), time(), rng(label), ready(), finish(o)`. In a hub session `session` is `window.AIHub`. Outside one it's `LocalSession` (`src/net/local.js`), which never runs in a session:\n553\t- **Same computer:** `BroadcastChannel` named from the slug, with a lobby that lists hosts automatically. **[verified between two `file://` pages]**\n554\t- **Two computers:** WebRTC invite codes: the host's `RTCPeerConnection` makes an offer, waits for ICE gathering, shows it as a copyable code; the guest pastes it and returns an answer code; the host pastes that. A small DOM `<textarea>` overlay is the one allowed exception to pixel UI (text can't be typed on a TV with a pad anyway: label it `KEYBOARD NEEDED`). Use a public STUN server; two data channels, reliable and unordered/no-retransmit. Star topology: guests only talk to the host. **[verified: two pages connect with `iceServers: []`; an offer is about 650 bytes, base64 it]** The test drives this with `iceServers: []` (a `?g_nostun=1` flag).\n555\t- Lobby: the host sees seats fill, presses Start; a shared 3 s countdown with a one-ping clock offset for `time()`; 1 s heartbeat; 4 s silence = `leave`; host silence = `end` with `host-left` and a clean return to the menu. Results screen from the same `finish` object.\n556\t\n557\t### The shared-world protocol\n558\t`src/net/shift.js`. The host simulates everything on 60 Hz fixed steps: enemies, drops, damage, waves, score. Clients: own player only.\n559\t\n560\t| Message | From → to | Reliable | Rate | Content |\n561\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n562\t| `i` | client → host (`to: host`) | no | 12/s | `[xCm, zCm, yawDeg, pitchDeg, flags, weapon]` own pose (clients own their position) |\n563\t| `a` | client → host | yes | batched ≤6/s | actions: fire `[w, ox, oy, oz, dx, dy, dz]`, kick, knife, use, revive, reload |\n564\t| `w` | host → all | no | 9/s | snapshot `{n, t, e: [[id, type, xCm, zCm, yawDeg, state, hpPct], ...], p: [[id, xCm, zCm, yawDeg, flags, hp], ...], s: [clock, wave, teamScore]}`. Must stay under 1,200 bytes (test asserts): 24 enemies max |\n565\t| `e` | host → all | yes | batched ≤8/s | events: hit, kill, hurt, downed, revived, drop spawned/taken, wave, horn |\n566\t\n567\tHard limits: JSON ≤16 KB, at most 20 messages/s per copy, unreliable ≤1,200 bytes. Clients run the fire effects at once on their own shots, and the host resolves hits with its own zones. Enemies on clients are `GhostEnemy` views: same puppets, clips chosen from `state`, interpolated 120 ms behind. If `send` returns false, drop it: the next snapshot corrects it.\n568\t\n569\t---\n570\t\n571\t## 8. Art\n572\t\n573\t### Look **[verified]**\n574\tNative pixel pipeline at 480×270, palette toon materials, plus a soft vignette:\n575\t```js\n576\tlook: { scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: 0.5, softness: 0.55 } }],\n577\t        actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0.65, crease: 0.12 }, filters: [] },\n578\t        environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0.4, crease: 0.08 }, filters: [] } }\n579\t```\n580\tOnly the 16 palette colours (`ink plum red orange sand lime green teal navy blue sky cyan white mist slate night`). Enemies are `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`, world isn't. The Settings screen offers `native`, `spooky`, `ps1_horror`, `noir` and the engine's pixel options.\n581\t\n582\t**Moods (dusk, rain and abbey [verified: they look right]; dawn is a first guess, so check it):**\n583\t| Mood | `skyAt` hour | sun | ambient | `groundFog` colour, top, amount, near, far | Background | Extra |\n584\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n585\t| dusk (chapter 1) | 18.6 | 1.0 | 1.1 | `0x4a3a5a`, 1.2, 0.55, 12, 70 | `PALETTE.plum` | gulls, torch-lit windows |\n586\t| rain (chapter 2, Night Shift) | 21.5 | 0.5 | 1.0 | `PALETTE.night`, 2.0, 0.7, 8, 46 | `PALETTE.ink` | `new Precipitation({ kind: 'rain', count: 900, area: [36, 14, 36], color: PALETTE.slate })` with `wind.set(3, 1)` and `update(dt, ctx.camera.focus)` (3000 drops is far too heavy) |\n587\t| abbey (chapter 3) | 2 | 0.25 | 0.8 | `PALETTE.ink`, 0.8, 0.5, 10, 40 | `PALETTE.ink` | candles and braziers, strong warm pools, moon `setSunDirection` |\n588\t| launch dawn | 6.5 | 1.2 | 1.2 | `0x94b0c2`, 1, 0.3, 30, 120 | `PALETTE.sky`→`PALETTE.mist` | sunrise after the whole dark game |\n589\t\n590\tApply with `applySky(engine, skyAt(h))`, then set `engine.sun.intensity`, `engine.ambient.intensity`, `scene.background`, `scene.fogNode = mist.node`. Lamps: `lamp-post` with `{ light: { intensity: 16, radius: 10 } }`. A fill light on Max: `ctx.lights.request({ follow: model, offset: [0.3, 1.8, 0.5], color: 0xffe0a0, intensity: 1.2, radius: 5, priority: 8 })`. Higher washes her out. She must never be the brightest thing on screen.\n591\t\n592\t### Characters: puppets on the hero rig **[verified]**\n593\tEvery human is a `model()` of nested pivots named as `HERO_RIG`'s joints, so `HERO_CLIPS` and your clips play on it through `compileClips(clips, HERO_RIG, object)`. Rest positions are the hero's (feet at y=0, 1.6 m tall, big readable head). Each `buildModel` returns its own object. Compile each clip set once and share the `AnimationClip`s between instances of the same proportions: each instance only needs its own mixer. `check.mjs --sheets src/models/index.js` draws them **[verified from a subfolder]**. Keep `model()` defs in `src/models/` with no engine start in those modules.\n594\t\n595\t```js\n596\tconst J = (name, at, parts) => ({ group: parts, name, pivot: true, at });\n597\t// Joints and rest offsets to keep:\n598\t// Pelvis [0,0.62,0] → Torso [0,0,0] → Head [0,0.6,0]; ArmR [-0.27,0.52,0] → ForearmR [0,-0.25,0] → HandR [0,-0.16,0]; ArmL mirrored\n599\t// Pelvis → LegR [-0.14,0,0] → ShinR [0,-0.3,0] → FootR [0,-0.22,0]; LegL mirrored\n600\texport const islander = model({ id: 'islander', about: 'Oilskin-clad islander on the hero rig', tags: ['character'],"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"7fa5bd1f-f9d7-485f-8b1f-1544a1027e3b","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:05.078Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n- `map name W H fill`: a grid of `fill`. `R x0 y0 x1 y1 c`: filled rectangle. `B x0 y0 x1 y1 wall floor`: walls round a floor. `P x y c`: one cell. Commands on a line are separated by ` | `, in order.\n- 1 cell = 1 m. World: `x = col + 0.5 - W/2`, `z = row + 0.5 - H/2`, north is -Z. `NavGrid.fromRows(rows, { cell: 1, origin: [-W/2, 0, -H/2], blocked: '#T~HBSG' })`. Open `B`, `S` and `G` cells with `setOpen` when they break or open. `D`, `W`, `E` and `L` stay open in nav and are solid only for Max until used (§4.8).\n\n| Char | Meaning | Char | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `#` | Stone wall or cliff, 3 m+, solid | `D` | Door, solid until opened |\n| `T` | Timber or plaster wall, 3 m, solid | `G` | Gate, shut until the story opens it |\n| `~` | Deep water. An invisible wall stops Max. Enemies kicked in sink and die | `S` | Roll-up shutter |\n| `H` | Low cover, 1 m, blocks walking but not bullets above 1 m | `W` | Window, vaultable |\n| `.` | Cobbles | `B` | Breakable crate or barrel, solid until broken |\n| `,` | Dirt or turf | `L` / `E` | Inside ladder / outside ladder at an upper window |\n| `=` | Planks | `c` | Conveyor belt, walkable, carries whoever stands on it (add velocity by map cell) |\n| `:` | Indoor boards | `%` | Shallow water, walkable, 70% speed |\n| `_` | Flagstones | `r` | Crane rail (walkable) |\n\nMarkers (walkable): `a` start · `1-5` spawn doors · `m` Mr. Fathom · `t` telegraph · `y` Tannoy · `$` treasure chest · `p` pushable wardrobe · `n` net-mender · `d` the Dame · `w` winch · `u` boost spot · `k` crane cab · `z` crane drop zone · `o` boss entrance · `s` statue · `q` clue mosaic · `v` trapdoor · `h` hiding niche · `l` lever.\n\n```text\nmap quay 64 48 #\nR 2 2 47 45 . | R 3 2 21 14 , | R 48 2 51 45 = | R 52 0 63 47 ~ | R 52 30 54 32 =\nR 55 30 57 44 = | R 54 4 60 10 # | B 22 4 37 13 T : | R 29 13 30 13 D | P 22 8 W | P 37 8 W\nP 24 6 L | R 31 15 33 16 H | B 42 4 47 11 T : | R 47 5 47 10 : | P 44 7 m | B 39 15 46 21 T :\nR 42 21 43 21 D | P 42 15 W | B 38 30 46 38 T : | R 41 30 42 30 D | P 46 34 W | P 43 35 n\nB 5 16 16 30 # _ | R 16 22 16 23 D | P 7 18 t | R 26 21 27 22 H | R 31 27 33 29 H\nR 15 38 19 39 H | R 23 38 27 39 H | R 31 38 35 39 H | R 15 42 19 43 H | R 23 42 27 43 H\nR 31 42 35 43 H | R 3 33 4 34 H | R 7 33 8 34 H | R 3 38 4 39 H | R 7 38 8 39 H | R 6 6 7 11 H\nR 11 6 12 11 H | R 16 6 17 11 H | R 0 8 1 9 G | R 18 32 24 35 T | R 30 32 35 35 T\nR 17 31 17 37 T | P 27 11 p | P 20 18 y | P 35 19 y | P 28 31 y | P 44 24 y | P 10 13 y\nP 49 40 y | P 44 18 $ | P 14 28 $ | P 5 42 $ | P 56 43 a | P 3 3 1 | P 47 3 2 | P 3 44 3\nP 46 44 4 | P 50 26 5 | P 44 41 B | P 45 41 B | P 40 43 B | P 12 3 B | P 13 3 B | P 49 12 B\nmap loft 16 10 T\nR 1 1 14 8 : | P 2 2 L | P 4 9 W | P 10 9 W | P 8 0 W | P 15 5 E | P 0 5 E\nmap road 22 64 #\nR 8 1 13 62 , | R 4 44 17 54 , | R 6 47 9 47 H | R 12 47 15 47 H | R 0 26 21 33 ~\nR 10 26 11 33 = | R 4 10 17 22 , | R 1 36 7 40 , | R 4 20 6 22 H | R 15 12 17 14 H\nR 10 0 11 0 D | P 10 61 a | P 5 16 m | P 2 38 $ | P 9 52 y | P 13 18 y\nmap cannery 48 36 #\nR 18 27 30 34 _ | R 24 35 25 35 D | R 6 10 41 25 _ | R 23 26 25 26 _ | R 10 13 37 14 c\nR 10 21 37 22 c | R 10 17 15 18 H | R 20 17 27 18 H | R 32 17 37 18 H | R 1 12 4 20 _\nR 5 15 5 17 D | R 34 2 44 8 _ | R 37 9 38 9 D | P 41 4 d | R 4 2 14 8 _ | R 9 9 10 9 D | P 6 4 w\nP 12 10 u | R 22 2 26 9 _ | R 23 1 25 1 S | R 42 16 42 18 D | R 43 14 46 20 _\nB 31 26 39 34 # _ | R 31 30 31 31 D | P 36 29 t | P 20 33 m | P 24 34 a | P 43 3 $ | P 2 19 $\nP 40 11 y | P 8 24 y | P 2 16 1 | P 45 17 2 | P 24 28 3\nmap yard 36 36 #\nR 2 2 33 33 . | R 7 8 9 10 H | R 26 8 28 10 H | R 7 25 9 27 H | R 26 25 28 27 H\nR 16 12 19 13 H | R 16 22 19 23 H | R 4 18 31 18 r | R 13 17 15 19 z | R 22 17 24 19 z\nP 3 18 k | R 17 34 18 35 D | R 17 0 18 1 G | P 17 32 a | P 17 4 o | P 31 31 m | P 4 4 $\nP 31 4 y\nmap causeway 16 96 ~\nR 3 2 12 93 % | R 5 2 10 93 . | R 0 62 4 68 , | R 11 34 15 40 , | R 6 0 9 1 G | R 5 94 10 95 ,\nP 7 94 a | P 1 65 m | P 14 37 $ | P 12 37 y | P 4 75 1 | P 11 58 2 | P 4 45 3 | P 11 25 4\nP 4 15 5\nmap abbey 44 40 #\nR 8 8 35 31 _ | R 12 12 31 27 , | R 21 32 23 38 _ | R 21 39 23 39 D | P 22 38 a | R 20 7 23 7 G\nR 20 1 23 6 _ | P 21 3 t | R 21 0 22 0 D | P 14 14 s | P 29 14 s | P 22 25 s | P 22 19 q\nR 12 12 12 12 H | R 16 12 16 12 H | R 27 12 27 12 H | R 31 12 31 12 H | R 12 27 12 27 H\nR 16 27 16 27 H | R 27 27 27 27 H | R 31 27 31 27 H | R 12 18 12 18 H | R 31 18 31 18 H\nR 12 22 12 22 H | R 31 22 31 22 H | P 10 20 v | R 1 10 6 34 _ | R 3 14 4 15 H | R 3 20 4 21 H\nR 3 26 4 27 H | P 1 16 h | P 6 22 h | P 1 28 h | P 3 33 l | R 7 30 7 31 D | R 36 19 36 20 D\nR 37 14 42 26 _ | P 40 18 m | P 41 25 $ | P 2 11 $ | P 10 30 y | P 33 10 y | P 34 9 1 | P 9 9 2\nP 34 30 3\nmap nave 28 48 #\nR 2 2 25 45 _ | R 8 10 9 11 H | R 18 10 19 11 H | R 8 18 9 19 H | R 18 18 19 19 H\nR 8 26 9 27 H | R 18 26 19 27 H | R 8 34 9 35 H | R 18 34 19 35 H | R 11 5 16 7 H\nR 13 46 14 47 D | R 26 4 27 5 G | P 13 44 a | P 13 12 o | P 3 3 $ | P 24 44 y\n```\n\nThe quay, printed for orientation, with repeated rows left out (north up; the pier is bottom right, the Net Loft top centre, the chapel left, the sea right, the Foghorn rock top right):\n\n```text\n    0         1         2         3         4         5         6\n  0 ####################################################~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  2 ##.,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,..........................====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  3 ##.1,,,,,,,,BB,,,,,,,,.........................2====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  4 ##.,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,TTTTTTTTTTTTTTTT....TTTTTT====~~#######~~~\n  6 ##.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,T:L::::::::::::T....T:::::====~~#######~~~\n  7 ##.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,T::::::::::::::T....T:m:::====~~#######~~~\n  8 GG.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,W::::::::::::::W....T:::::====~~#######~~~\n 11 ##.,,,HH,,,HH,,,HH,,,,T::::p:::::::::T....TTTTTT====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 13 ##.,,,,,,,y,,,,,,,,,,,TTTTTTTDDTTTTTTT..........====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 14 ##.,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,..........................====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 15 ##.............................HHH.....TTTWTTTT.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 16 ##...############..............HHH.....T::::::T.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 18 ##...#_t________#...y..................T::::$:T.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 21 ##...#__________#.........HH...........TTTDDTTT.====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 22 ##...#__________D.........HH....................====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 24 ##...#__________#...........................y...====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 27 ##...#__________#..............HHH..............====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 28 ##...#________$_#..............HHH..............====~~~~~~~~~~~~\n 30 ##...############.....................TTTDDTTTT.==========~~~~~~\n 31 ##...............T..........y.........T:::::::T.==========~~~~~~\n 32 ##...............TTTTTTTT.....TTTTTT..T:::::::T.==========~~~~~~\n 34 ##.HH..HH........TTTTTTTT.....TTTTTT..T:::::::W.====~~~===~~~~~~\n 35 ##...............TTTTTTTT.....TTTTTT..T::::n::T.====~~~===~~~~~~\n 38 ##.HH..HH......HHHHH...HHHHH...HHHHH..TTTTTTTTT.====~~~===~~~~~~\n 42 ##...$.........HHHHH...HHHHH...HHHHH............====~~~===~~~~~~\n 43 ##.............HHHHH...HHHHH...HHHHH....B.......====~~~=a=~~~~~~\n 44 ##.3..........................................4.====~~~===~~~~~~\n 46 ####################################################~~~~~~~~~~~~\n```\n\nThe loft is the Net Loft's upper floor: offset col 22, row 4, floor at y = 3.2. Solid `T` blocks are uninhabited houses with roofs. Dress generously (§8).\n\n### Chapter 1: CLAIM 1: ACT OF GOD. Mourne Quay, bruised dusk (10-12 min)\n\n1. **Arrival.** Cutscene on the pier (script). Control at `a`. Hints fade as you do them: move, look, run.\n2. **First Tannoy** at (49,40): the Commodore's line. Hint: aim and shoot it. Max says `Noted.`\n3. **First cottage** (door 41-42,30). Hint: Action kicks doors. Net-mender scene, first fight: hints for head or legs, then the kick prompt. Then the boat burns, and 2 Islanders break in through the door while a window hint shows `W` (46,34): vault out to the quay.\n4. **Quay front:** crate (49,12), 3 Islanders, first Doubloons and herb. Net shed `m`: Mr. Fathom's intro; first shop; first Case tip (pick up shells with a full-ish Case: place and rotate).\n5. **The Square.** Entering from row 14 or the main street (rows 22-29) triggers a 6 s cutscene: 14 Islanders round the bonfire with an effigy in a suit. Siege starts.\n6. **The Siege (the demo's signature).** Total 30 Islanders and 4 Bottlers from 1:00; `maxActive` 12; spawn doors 1-5. The Flenser arrives at 1:30 from door 2: you hear the saw first. Tools: the Net Loft door (29-30,13) with the wardrobe `p` to push across it; vault its windows (22,8), (37,8); inside ladder to the loft; loft windows look down on the Square; Islanders raise outside ladders to `E` at 1:00 and again every 25 s, knock them down; drop onto the hay cart (31-33,15). Three loops let you kite: Square → row 14 → quay → main street; Square → drying yard → back lane → row 14; Square → lane (25-29,32-35) → market → graveyard → west side.\n7. **The Foghorn.** After 3:30, or 34 kills, whichever comes first (never leave the player waiting). The horn from the rock at (57,7) (camera shake, gulls scatter, all sound drops). Script scene: tools drop as props, every enemy walks to the nearest `~` cell, wades in and sinks, the Flenser last. Silence.\n8. **Aftermath.** Free roam, loot left on the ground, `$` at (44,18), (14,28), (5,42). Chapel = safe room with telegraph `t`, Claim Note. West Gate `G` is now open. Exit: Claim Form, load Road.\n\n### Chapter 2: CLAIM 2: WEAR AND TEAR. Rain at night (14-16 min)\n\n**Salt Road (`road`).** Roadblock clearing: 6 Islanders, 1 Bottler on a wagon, Brine Barrels to shoot. Side alcove `$` (2,38) with an ambush. **The bridge** (10-11,26-33): 2 m wide over the gorge, 3 Bottlers on ledges ahead (elevated, unreachable, shoot the bottles); kick enemies off the edge (`~` kills them). North clearing: Mr. Fathom in a beached rowboat, the Rifle on sale, 4 Deckhands, a far Tannoy to snipe at (13,18). Door to the cannery.\n\n**Thole Cannery (`cannery`).** The door locks behind you. Telegraph office, Fathom in the bay.\n1. **The Hall.** Two belts running opposite ways, 1.5 m/s, carcasses swinging from a moving overhead rail, machines as cover, 10 Islanders and 2 Bottlers. Riding a belt moves you and them.\n2. **The Flenser again.** Saw room door (5,15-17) bursts open. Kill him for the Cold Room key.\n3. **Cold Room** `d`: no music, breath particles. Meeting the Dame. Escort begins; hint for Follow/Wait.\n4. **Boost** `u` (12,10): Winch Room is chained from a high hoist. Max boosts her; she pulls; the door opens. First Carrier ambush from door 2: teach shooting him off.\n5. **Hold the Winch.** She takes `w` (6,4), the shutter `S` rises 1% per second (90 s; pauses while she's disturbed). Waves from 1, 2, 3 with Deckhands and a Carrier. Max defends the door (9-10,9) and hall. At 100% she runs to the corridor.\n6. **The belt:** crossing the hall to the shutter, Max is hooked off her feet by Mate Ansgar's gaff, and they go down together on the belt, riding toward the can press at its east end. Interactive cutscene, 4 press QTEs and 1 mash (§4.11). He goes into the press. A can rolls out. Telegraph in the north corridor (autosave).\n\n**Cannery Yard (`yard`).** Boss: the Bosun (§6). After: Dame's confession (script), Mr. Fathom at `m`, Claim Form, north gate.\n\n### Chapter 3: CLAIM 3: ACT OF COMMODORE. Moonlit, then candlelit (12-15 min)\n\n**The Causeway (`causeway`).** A 90 m stone road to the abbey as the tide comes in. Timer 240 s, shown as a tide gauge. Water level goes from -0.6 to +0.9 (`WaterSurface` y; Max in water over road ankle: 70% speed; over 0.7: 2 damage/s). Rocks at rows 34-40 and 62-68 stay dry (Fathom and `$`). Drowned rise as you pass spawn points; two rowboats with Harpooners shadow you at 10 m. At the gate the Dame turns a wheel for 6 s while you hold. Missing the deadline drowns you.\n\n**The Abbey (`abbey`).** Monks and 2 Reliquary Knights, moonlit cloister.\n1. **Lens puzzle:** three lamp statues `s`; each rotates in 45° steps with Action (1.2 s, exposed). The floor mosaic `q` shows which way each must face so all three beams hit the lenses over gate `G`. Beams are glow boxes. Solved: gate opens with a heavy sound.\n2. **Trapdoor** `v` (10,20): as you cross the arcade, the floor drops under the Dame. Cut to the crypt.\n3. **The Dame alone (90-120 s).** You control her: walk 2.2 m/s, hold run for 3.2 m/s (loud), Action to whack (stuns 2 s, once per 8 s), `h` niches to hide, floor lamps to throw for a noise distraction. 3 blind Knights patrol the hall, hearing radius: run 9 m, walk 4 m, still 0. Two hits and you restart the segment. Horror beat: low drone, no music, Pym on hold. Goal: lever `l` (3,33), then door (7,30-31). Then control returns to Max, finishing a fight in the arcade as the Dame arrives.\n4. **Armoury** (door 36,19-20): Fathom, `$`, last stock. Vestibule telegraph, door to the nave.\n\n**The Nave (`nave`).** Final boss (§6). The side gate opens.\n\n**The Launch (on rails, 80-100 s).** The island is coming down. The Dame drives; Max stands on the stern deck with free aim and the Harpoon Gun or Rifle. A spline through sea stacks, `WaterSurface` with `WAVES_CHOPPY`, 14 m/s. Shoot: mines, pursuing boats' Harpooners, falling rock (a QTE if you miss), Limpets crawling onto the deck (kick). End: arch collapse QTE. Dawn (`skyAt(6.5)`). **Ending** (script), Final Claim Form, credits with the on-hold jingle.\n\n### Dressing and the world's edge\nEvery area needs a backdrop: far silhouettes (dark low-poly cliffs, abbey on its rock, the Foghorn tower) so the world doesn't end at a plane. Fog colour must match the background. No bare wall over 6 m; a prop or two per 4×4 m of floor; vertical things (Tannoy poles, lamp posts, drying racks, chimneys, masts) everywhere. Performance budget is unlimited: be lavish, with up to 16 lights and `quality: 'high'`.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Bosses\n\n### The Bosun (cannery yard, rain)\n4 m tall (`HERO_RIG` puppet, root scale 2.6). Three brine sacs on his back (180 HP each) that glow when exposed. Weak everywhere else: 25% damage from the front, 100% on sacs.\n- **Attacks:** Anchor Sweep (range 7 m, wind-up 1.0 s, QTE dodge when close, 45). Anchor Throw (18 m, wind-up 1.2 s, lands with a 2 m blast, chain drags back over 2 s, 40). Stomp (3 m, 25 + knockdown). Grab (within 3 m, mash, 60). Throws crate stacks when you hide behind them for over 4 s (`H` stacks can break).\n- **The crane:** the Dame sits in the cab `k`. The pallet travels along the rail on its own between drop zones `z`, painted yellow. A lamp lights when the pallet is over a zone. Press Command when he is under it. Hit: he's on his knees for 8 s, sacs exposed and ×2 damage. A harpoon through the chain adds 3 s. The pallet reloads in 15 s. Brine Barrels also stagger him for 4 s.\n- **Phases:** each sac burst makes him 15% faster. Phase 2 adds 4 Islanders every 40 s. Phase 3 adds a double sweep and heavier rain.\n- **End:** falls with a huge shake (`hitstop`, `shockwave`), drops a Black Pearl and 2000 Doubloons. Commodore, on Tannoy: `...HE ONLY HAD THE ONE.`\n\n### The Commodore's Bathysphere (flooded nave)\nA walking brass ball on legs (`HERO_RIG` root scale 2.4; brass ball torso, porthole showing an armchair and a figure at a microphone, pipes, steam `smoke` particles). Water rises by phase.\n- **Phase 1, Plumbing.** Four valves (shoulders, hips: 140 HP each, glowing red). Attacks: Steam Jet (6 m cone, 30 + slow), Stomp (AoE), Rivet Burst (3 shots, shootable), **Charge** down the aisle (whistle tell, 8 m/s): if he hits a column (`H`), it shatters and he's stunned for 3 s. Each burst valve: 4 Monks, and water rises 0.15 m.\n- **Phase 2, Hatch.** All valves gone: he sags. Three hatch locks (60 HP each). Shoot them while he flails; then a Kick prompt (cutscene: Max climbs, tears the hatch).\n- **Phase 3, The Mother.** Out he falls, and the thing on his neck bursts out and takes the altar: a 3.5 m limpet with the Commodore fused on top, still broadcasting. It spits brine globs (shootable, 20) and births Limpets; flares kill them all at once. The brass microphone on his chest has 200 HP: shooting it cuts him off mid-sentence one last time, and this is the horror beat, because the voice carries on without it. Then the eye under his jaw has 400 HP. Then **Final Settlement:** QTE (press, press, mash); stamp; `Claim denied.`\n- The Font cracks, water floods, side gate opens, run to the Launch.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Night Shift and multiplayer\n\n### Mode: Night Shift\nA 4-minute hold-out on the quay map at night in the rain, solo or co-op: keep each other alive until dawn. Everyone is a Max in their seat's colour (scarf and name tag). Loadout: pistol and scattergun with fixed ammo and tuned starting values; crates and drops give ammo, herbs and grenades. Waves by clock (cap 24 enemies alive): 0:00 8 Islanders; 1:00 Bottlers; 2:00 a Flenser; 3:00 two Flensers and Deckhands; 3:40 the horn warning; 4:00 **dawn: the Foghorn sounds, everyone walks into the sea, and you win.** Downed: 20 s bleed-out, hold Action 2 s to revive; bleed-out ends your shift for that round (solo: over). Score: hits, kills, head and kick bonus, combo multiplier. Standalone solo score goes on a local board.\n\nFrom the title menu: `NIGHT SHIFT` → SOLO / HOST PARTY / JOIN PARTY.\n\n### Hub integration **[verified with a minimal engine game: 2 players; 4 players at latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5; host-leave; server: all pass `__hubCheck`]**\n- Mode **`shared-world`**, seats `[1, 4]`, own card. Follow https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md. Vendor `session.js`, `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` from the same folder into `vendor/hub/` once. The README is short; read it. `examples/arena.html` in the same folder is a complete shared-world game, including the server case.\n- In `<head>`, in this order: `<meta charset>`; the `session.js` text **unmodified, not through esbuild**, as the first script; then the tags:\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Hold the quay together until dawn\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move, hold aim, fire; kick stunned enemies; revive friends\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">\n```\n- Flow:\n```js\nasync function boot() {\n  if (window.AIHub?.active) {\n    const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true });\n    if (info) return startSession(info); // straight to the card: no title, menu or attract\n  }\n  return startStandalone();\n}\n```\n`startSession`: `Engine.start` (seed from `info.seed`; no WebGPU: `AIHub.fail('WebGPU unavailable')`), build the quay, show **our card**, then `AIHub.ready()` with no key press. Card shows: the game's name, the players in colour with ready ticks, how to win, this player's controls with the right glyphs, time left from the `card` event. Enter/Cross/tap → `AIHub.answer('ready')`. Triangle/M/tap → `AIHub.answer('more')`. Nothing on the card changes the round. Play starts when `AIHub.time() >= 0` (show the 3-2-1 from `start`).\n- In a session: no quitting or restarting, no pausing the world (Options opens a small Settings overlay while the round runs), no attract, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no other network, no chat or emotes. Use `AIHub.rng(label)` where copies must agree. Ignore Options while Create is held.\n- **Round end:** host calls `AIHub.finish({ standings, scores, won, stats, awards })` once: on dawn, on all down, or on `time-up` (immediately, within `graceMs`). `standings` lists every player once, by score, best first (`[[2],[0,3],[1]]`); `won: true` at dawn; `stats` up to 6 per player (Score, Kills, Heads, Kicks, Revives, Accuracy); `awards` up to 3 per player, title ≤24 and detail ≤40 characters (`Chief Adjuster`, `Steel Toe`, `Good Samaritan`). On `end`: stop input and sound (`stopMusic`, `stopLoops`), send nothing more. `leave`: remove that player; the hub voids the round if the host leaves.\n- **`AIHub.server`** (a copy with no player of its own): run the host simulation with no local player, a slow overview camera, no local input. `info.isHost` is true and `info.me` isn't in `players`. Never assume a local player exists on the host.\n\n### The session interface and the game on its own\nTASK.md wants multiplayer for AI Hub and for the game on its own. Write the co-op against one small interface, `session`, shaped exactly like `AIHub`: `me, players, host, isHost, server, seed, limitMs, send(data, {to, reliable}), on(event, fn), time(), rng(label), ready(), finish(o)`. In a hub session `session` is `window.AIHub`. Outside one it's `LocalSession` (`src/net/local.js`), which never runs in a session:\n- **Same computer:** `BroadcastChannel` named from the slug, with a lobby that lists hosts automatically. **[verified between two `file://` pages]**\n- **Two computers:** WebRTC invite codes: the host's `RTCPeerConnection` makes an offer, waits for ICE gathering, shows it as a copyable code; the guest pastes it and returns an answer code; the host pastes that. A small DOM `<textarea>` overlay is the one allowed exception to pixel UI (text can't be typed on a TV with a pad anyway: label it `KEYBOARD NEEDED`). Use a public STUN server; two data channels, reliable and unordered/no-retransmit. Star topology: guests only talk to the host. **[verified: two pages connect with `iceServers: []`; an offer is about 650 bytes, base64 it]** The test drives this with `iceServers: []` (a `?g_nostun=1` flag).\n- Lobby: the host sees seats fill, presses Start; a shared 3 s countdown with a one-ping clock offset for `time()`; 1 s heartbeat; 4 s silence = `leave`; host silence = `end` with `host-left` and a clean return to the menu. Results screen from the same `finish` object.\n\n### The shared-world protocol\n`src/net/shift.js`. The host simulates everything on 60 Hz fixed steps: enemies, drops, damage, waves, score. Clients: own player only.\n\n| Message | From → to | Reliable | Rate | Content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `i` | client → host (`to: host`) | no | 12/s | `[xCm, zCm, yawDeg, pitchDeg, flags, weapon]` own pose (clients own their position) |\n| `a` | client → host | yes | batched ≤6/s | actions: fire `[w, ox, oy, oz, dx, dy, dz]`, kick, knife, use, revive, reload |\n| `w` | host → all | no | 9/s | snapshot `{n, t, e: [[id, type, xCm, zCm, yawDeg, state, hpPct], ...], p: [[id, xCm, zCm, yawDeg, flags, hp], ...], s: [clock, wave, teamScore]}`. Must stay under 1,200 bytes (test asserts): 24 enemies max |\n| `e` | host → all | yes | batched ≤8/s | events: hit, kill, hurt, downed, revived, drop spawned/taken, wave, horn |\n\nHard limits: JSON ≤16 KB, at most 20 messages/s per copy, unreliable ≤1,200 bytes. Clients run the fire effects at once on their own shots, and the host resolves hits with its own zones. Enemies on clients are `GhostEnemy` views: same puppets, clips chosen from `state`, interpolated 120 ms behind. If `send` returns false, drop it: the next snapshot corrects it.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art\n\n### Look **[verified]**\nNative pixel pipeline at 480×270, palette toon materials, plus a soft vignette:\n```js\nlook: { scene: [{ id: 'vignette', params: { intensity: 0.5, softness: 0.55 } }],\n        actors: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0.65, crease: 0.12 }, filters: [] },\n        environment: { pixel: { size: 1, outline: 0.4, crease: 0.08 }, filters: [] } }\n```\nOnly the 16 palette colours (`ink plum red orange sand lime green teal navy blue sky cyan white mist slate night`). Enemies are `setLookLayer(root, 'actors')`, world isn't. The Settings screen offers `native`, `spooky`, `ps1_horror`, `noir` and the engine's pixel options.\n\n**Moods (dusk, rain and abbey [verified: they look right]; dawn is a first guess, so check it):**\n| Mood | `skyAt` hour | sun | ambient | `groundFog` colour, top, amount, near, far | Background | Extra |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| dusk (chapter 1) | 18.6 | 1.0 | 1.1 | `0x4a3a5a`, 1.2, 0.55, 12, 70 | `PALETTE.plum` | gulls, torch-lit windows |\n| rain (chapter 2, Night Shift) | 21.5 | 0.5 | 1.0 | `PALETTE.night`, 2.0, 0.7, 8, 46 | `PALETTE.ink` | `new Precipitation({ kind: 'rain', count: 900, area: [36, 14, 36], color: PALETTE.slate })` with `wind.set(3, 1)` and `update(dt, ctx.camera.focus)` (3000 drops is far too heavy) |\n| abbey (chapter 3) | 2 | 0.25 | 0.8 | `PALETTE.ink`, 0.8, 0.5, 10, 40 | `PALETTE.ink` | candles and braziers, strong warm pools, moon `setSunDirection` |\n| launch dawn | 6.5 | 1.2 | 1.2 | `0x94b0c2`, 1, 0.3, 30, 120 | `PALETTE.sky`→`PALETTE.mist` | sunrise after the whole dark game |\n\nApply with `applySky(engine, skyAt(h))`, then set `engine.sun.intensity`, `engine.ambient.intensity`, `scene.background`, `scene.fogNode = mist.node`. Lamps: `lamp-post` with `{ light: { intensity: 16, radius: 10 } }`. A fill light on Max: `ctx.lights.request({ follow: model, offset: [0.3, 1.8, 0.5], color: 0xffe0a0, intensity: 1.2, radius: 5, priority: 8 })`. Higher washes her out. She must never be the brightest thing on screen.\n\n### Characters: puppets on the hero rig **[verified]**\nEvery human is a `model()` of nested pivots named as `HERO_RIG`'s joints, so `HERO_CLIPS` and your clips play on it through `compileClips(clips, HERO_RIG, object)`. Rest positions are the hero's (feet at y=0, 1.6 m tall, big readable head). Each `buildModel` returns its own object. Compile each clip set once and share the `AnimationClip`s between instances of the same proportions: each instance only needs its own mixer. `check.mjs --sheets src/models/index.js` draws them **[verified from a subfolder]**. Keep `model()` defs in `src/models/` with no engine start in those modules.\n\n```js\nconst J = (name, at, parts) => ({ group: parts, name, pivot: true, at });\n// Joints and rest offsets to keep:\n// Pelvis [0,0.62,0] → Torso [0,0,0] → Head [0,0.6,0]; ArmR [-0.27,0.52,0] → ForearmR [0,-0.25,0] → HandR [0,-0.16,0]; ArmL mirrored\n// Pelvis → LegR [-0.14,0,0] → ShinR [0,-0.3,0] → FootR [0,-0.22,0]; LegL mirrored\nexport const islander = model({ id: 'islander', about: 'Oilskin-clad islander on the hero rig', tags: ['character'],","numLines":250,"startLine":351,"totalLines":885}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UqnKhGkefNTgn7aUwznqVL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
