{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgke2yv8Tm5CjdGr3Q7FW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0136AZUAdswHhR9KT98fmyrn","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","offset":601,"limit":250},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13456,"cache_read_input_tokens":45437,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13456},"output_tokens":78,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"cfaba27b-70e4-4370-a4fb-3c48059851e7","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:13.386Z","request_id":"req_011Cgke2ygzs7QqkjWuW4bry","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0136AZUAdswHhR9KT98fmyrn":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","offset":601,"limit":250}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0136AZUAdswHhR9KT98fmyrn","type":"tool_result","content":"601\t  palette: { coat: 'teal', band: 'orange', pants: 'night', skin: 'mist', hat: 'navy', boot: 'ink' },\n602\t  parts: [ J('Pelvis', [0, 0.62, 0], [ { box: [0.44, 0.2, 0.28], at: [0, 0.02, 0], c: 'pants' },\n603\t    J('Torso', [0, 0, 0], [ { box: [0.42, 0.48, 0.26], at: [0, 0.32, 0], c: 'coat' },\n604\t      J('Head', [0, 0.6, 0], [ { box: [0.31, 0.3, 0.3], at: [0, 0.13, 0], c: 'skin' },\n605\t                               { box: [0.27, 0.07, 0.04], at: [0, 0.16, 0.16], c: 'band', glow: true } ]),\n606\t      /* ArmR, ArmL */ ]), /* LegR, LegL */ ]) ] });\n607\t```\n608\tA glowing eye band in `orange` reads brilliantly at 15 m **[verified]**. It's the game's signature: all infected have it; Limpet-free people don't.\n609\t\n610\tThe camera sits behind Max all game, so her back is her best side: hair covering the back of the head, scarf, coat belt and seam.\n611\t\n612\tGiants: `object.scale.setScalar(2.6)` (hit-zone radii scale too). Add props to joints: `object.getObjectByName('HandR').add(gun)`. Swap palettes per variant through `buildModel(id, { palette })`. Spring tails: `SpringChain` for Max's scarf and coat skirt, the Bosun's chain.\n613\t\n614\t### Asset list (all `src/models/`, new unless noted)\n615\t- **Characters:** Max, the Dame, Islander (×3 palettes, sou'wester, cap, bare), Net-Wife, Bottler, Deckhand, Carrier (sack), Flenser, Re-Salted, Monk, Reliquary Knight, Drowned, Harpooner, Mate Ansgar, Nils, Commodore, Mr. Fathom (helmet: `ball` + `torus` porthole with `glass` slot glow + bolts), Bosun, Bathysphere, Mother Limpet, Limpet (low crawler: `ball half`, tentacle `tube`s).\n616\t- **Quay props:** Tannoy on a pole (horn `cyl`, breaks), Foghorn tower (backdrop, 20 m), mail boat, rowboat, lobster pot, drying rack with fish, draped net, bollard, buoy, anchor, chain links, fish crate, Brine Barrel (red band), hay cart (re-coloured `cart` + `haystack`), effigy in a suit, telegraph desk.\n617\t- **Cannery:** gutting table, conveyor frames (`beltMaterial` for moving belts), hanging carcasses on a rail, ice blocks, winch, roll-up shutter, gantry crane and pallet, steam pipes, `THOLE & SONS` sign (use `textureDef` `path` layers).\n618\t- **Abbey:** lamp statue with lens beam, floor mosaic, Font, pews, stained-glass panels (flat `glow` parts), organ pipes.\n619\t- **Launch:** launch hull with stern deck, sea stacks, mine, arch.\n620\t- **Weapons:** pistol, scattergun, rifle, harpoon gun, bolt, flare, depth charge, oil bottle, knife, Flenser's saw, gaff hook, boathook, flail, shield, halberd, Dame's cane and handbag.\n621\t- **Library, as they are or re-coloured:** `door window stone-wall wall-corner timber-wall roof chimney fence ladder lamp-post wall-lantern hanging-lantern brazier candles campfire flame barrel crate crate-stack sack rope-coil bucket keg table chair bench desk shelf wardrobe bed fireplace well market-stall cart haystack clothesline dead-tree rock boulders reeds tall-grass tombstone column altar banner portcullis sarcophagus lever wall-chains cage cobweb puddle`. Textures: `cobbles dirt moss deck planks flagstones dry-stone bricks rough-boards metal-plates rust slate-roof wet-sand shallow-water basalt ruined-mosaic`.\n622\t- **Packs (optional, for richness):** `kenney-nature` cliffs (`cliff-large-rock`, `cliff-block-rock`) for backdrops, `kenney-castle` towers and walls for the abbey silhouette. For the single file, each pack goes in `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__` (§14). **[verified]** Credit them on the About screen; they're CC0.\n623\t- **HUD icons:** `textureDef`s using `path` or `pixels`, read through `hudSprite`. Sized to their Case footprint (pistol 42×28 px). Glyphs: §11.\n624\t\n625\t---\n626\t\n627\t## 9. Animation\n628\t\n629\tBase: `compileClips`, `gaitClip`, `ClipDef` data, one `THREE.AnimationMixer` per character. Write a `Humanoid` (`src/game/actor.js`) that all characters share. **Masked layers [verified]:** legs and upper body are separate actions on one mixer:\n630\t\n631\t```js\n632\tconst UPPER = /^(Torso|Head|Arm|Forearm|Hand)/, LOWER = /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/;\n633\tconst mask = (clip, re, name) => new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter((t) => re.test(t.name.split('.')[0])));\n634\t```\n635\tMax walks with `mask(Walk, LOWER)` while `mask(AimPistol, UPPER)` holds the gun up. After the mixer, add the aim pitch to the arms and torso (rotate `ArmR`, `ArmL`, `Torso`, `Head` quaternions) so the gun follows the laser. Locomotion `timeScale = speed / clip.speed` (authored: Walk 2, Run 6, CrouchWalk 1.4; custom `gaitClip`s carry their own). `validateClip` and `analyzeClip` in tests.\n636\t\n637\tFrom `HERO_CLIPS` as they are: `Idle IdleLook Walk Run Crouch Climb Push Hurt HitReact Death GetUp Roll Kick Punch Shout Slam Slash1 Slash2 Slash3 Sit LieIdle`.\n638\t\n639\t**New clips (data in `src/data/clips.js`):**\n640\t- **Max:** AimPistol, AimLong (two-handed), FirePistol / FireLong recoil overlays, ReloadPistol, ReloadPump, ReloadBolt, Roundhouse (the kick: full-body spin), HipThrow, KnifeSlash, DoorKick, Vault, LadderUp, QuickTurn, Throw, Boost, Stagger, KnockedDown, StampForm.\n641\t- **Islanders:** Shamble (`gaitClip(HERO_RIG, { name: 'Shamble', frames: 40, speed: 1.1, stance: 0.62, hip: -0.05, bob: 0.02, lift: 0.04, lean: 16, sway: 7, head: 8, arms: { swing: 8, elbow: 30 } })` **[verified: reads well]**), Lurch (run), WorkChop, WorkMend, RaiseTool (wind-up), Swing, ThrowOverhand, StunHands (hands to face), KneelHit, BashDoor, ClimbIn, WalkToSea (slow, arms slack), Wade.\n642\t- **Others:** SawRev, SawSwing, SawLunge; ShieldWalk, ShieldBlock, FlailSpin; KnightWalk (heavy gait), HalberdSweep; DrownedRise; CarrierShoulder, CarrierWalk; DameWalk (tiny steps, cane), DameCane, DameBarrelIn, DameHoist; FathomIdle (bob, tap helmet), FathomPresent (coat open).\n643\t- **Bosses:** AnsgarHook, AnsgarSwing; BosunDrag, BosunSweep, BosunThrow, BosunStomp, BosunKneel, BosunRoar; BathyWalk, BathyCharge, BathySag; MotherSpit.\n644\t- **Procedural:** head look-at (rotate `Head`), breathing `layers` on idles, `Squash` on landings, `SpringChain` tails, ragdolls on violent deaths.\n645\t\n646\t---\n647\t\n648\t## 10. Audio\n649\t\n650\tAll code, no files. Engine `ctx.audio` (`register`, `play(name, { volume, pitch, pan })`, `loop`, `playMusic`, `Song` data), `spatialize` for positions, `muffle` for through-wall. In Node every call is a counted no-op, and `renderSound(def)` gives samples **[verified]**, so sounds can be tested without a browser.\n651\t\n652\t### Volumes: music 10% by default\n653\t`AudioManager` defaults are master 0.8, sfx 1, music 0.6 and its Reset returns to those **[verified]**. So: set `audio.persist = false`; keep volumes in your own settings (music default **0.10**, sfx 1, voice 1, master 0.8); apply them with `audio.setVolume` at boot and on change; your Settings Reset restores 0.10. Don't show the engine's panel (`settings: { button: false, key: slug }`). The test asserts `engine.audio.volume.music === 0.1` on a first run. Author song tracks loud enough to be heard at 10%: track `volume` about 0.5-0.8; check levels with an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus.\n654\t\n655\t### SFX (`src/audio/sfx.js`, about 45 `SoundDef`s with `layers`)\n656\tPistol (square snap + noise burst + low thump), scatter (bigger, longer noise), rifle (crack + tail), harpoon (twang + thud), dry click, reloads (2-3 clicks each), kick whoosh + impact, knife, body hits, head pop, enemy grunts (noise + pitch), door kick, window glass, ladder, crate break, Brine Barrel, flare hiss, depth charge, fire loop, Tannoy on/off crackle, Tannoy destroyed, foghorn (long, layered low saws, the most important sound in the game), saw loop (saw wave with `vibrato`, pitch rises on lunge), steam jet, rain loop, sea loop, gulls, conveyor loop, crane, chain, telegraph key clicks, bubbling (Fathom), UI move/confirm/back/stamp thud, QTE pop, heartbeat (low health), Limpet skitter, rubber stamp.\n657\t\n658\t### Music (`src/audio/songs.js`, original compositions, `Song` data validated by `parseSong`)\n659\t| Song | Feel |\n660\t| --- | --- |\n661\t| `title` | 66 bpm, D minor. Drone, slow low bell, sparse triangle melody |\n662\t| `explore` | 72 bpm, A minor. Plucked bass, long silences, one uneasy phrase |\n663\t| `combat` | 132 bpm, E minor. Square ostinato, noise hats; layered in when alerted |\n664\t| `siege` | 120 bpm. Drums and low bass with chanted gibberish over it |\n665\t| `shop` | 104 bpm, G major. A jaunty shanty on a detuned square \"accordion\" |\n666\t| `safe` | 60 bpm, C major. Soft triangle chords, faint telegraph rhythm |\n667\t| `boss` | 150 bpm, C minor. Driving, brass-like saw, tolling on the bar |\n668\t| `onhold` | 96 bpm. Cheerful Muzak (the Pym gag, ending credits) |\n669\t| `tide` | Rising pitch each loop, for the causeway |\n670\t| `dawn` | Short resolve for the launch ending |\n671\t\n672\tMusic fades through a small `Mix` helper (tween the channel down, swap, tween up to the user's level). Silence is part of the score: no music in the Cold Room, crypt or Foghorn.\n673\t\n674\t### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish (`src/audio/voice.js`)\n675\tEvery spoken line has text and voice. Pre-register syllables per speaker (5 vowel colours × 2 consonant styles) as `SoundDef`s and play one every 2 letters with `play(name, { pitch, volume, pan })`. Pitch from a hash of the word (the same word sounds the same), falling at `.`, rising at `?`, louder at `!`; pause at spaces and punctuation; typing speed matches the text.\n676\t\n677\t| Speaker | Recipe |\n678\t| --- | --- |\n679\t| Max | Triangle, mid (170 Hz), short, level |\n680\t| Dame | Square duty 0.25, high (320 Hz), `vibrato` wobble, clipped |\n681\t| Commodore | Square, nasal (260 Hz), `crush: 8`, noise crackle layer (Tannoy) |\n682\t| Fathom | Triangle low (110 Hz), slow decay, plus a bubble blip every few syllables (`muffle` feel) |\n683\t| Pym | Sine, flat pitch (200 Hz), `crush: 6` |\n684\t| Islanders | Saw, low (120 Hz), barked, 2-3 syllables, spatial |\n685\t| Monks | Three layered low sines, a chant |\n686\t| Bosun | One long 60 Hz bellow |\n687\t\n688\tA `voice` settings slider scales the volume passed to `play`.\n689\t\n690\t---\n691\t\n692\t## 11. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n693\t\n694\tAll screens are drawn on the engine's pixel HUD (`ctx.hud`), the same screens for every input. Art resolution is 480×270 with adaptive width: lay out from anchors, and test at 4:3 (width 360) too. **[verified: scale 1 text is 28 px tall at 1080p: the minimum, for secondary text only.]** Titles and primary labels use scale 2. At most 6-7 list rows per screen, one large selected item, plenty of empty space. No tables of numbers.\n695\t\n696\t- **Font:** uppercase only. Characters: `0-9 A-Z . , : ; - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ ! ? < > # ' ‘ ’ “ ” * @ ° · & | \\ ~ ^ $`. Anything else draws as `?`. A test scans every string in `src/data`.\n697\t- **Menus run with `engine.timeScale = 0`, never `engine.paused`.** **[verified]** At time scale 0 `update(ctx, 0)` still runs, `fixedUpdate` doesn't, `wasPressed` works; with `paused` the live loop doesn't call `update` at all. Use `wasPressed` in menus and a real-time counter (cosmetic only) for animation.\n698\t- **`src/core/ui.js`:** text, panel, list, slider, tabs, grid. Each widget registers a rectangle. Focus moves by stick/D-pad with key repeat; hover moves focus; click activates; `input.buttonEvents` for clicks; convert `input.pointer` from NDC to art pixels. A clear focus bar with a small arrow. `uiPrompt(action, label)` draws the glyph for the current device, in a prompt bar at the bottom of every screen.\n699\t- **Glyphs:** sprites, about 10×10: PlayStation (Cross blue, Circle red, Square pink, Triangle green; L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, Create as small pills; D-pad; sticks); Xbox (A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow; LB RB LT RT, Menu, View); keycaps (outlined box with the key's letter); mouse (body with left, right or wheel lit).\n700\t- **Last input tracking** (`src/core/device.js`): DOM `keydown`, mouse `pointermove`, `wheel` → keyboard; per-frame `navigator.getGamepads()` with any button or stick past the deadzone → pad. Prompts change at once. Settings: `CONTROLLER GLYPHS: PLAYSTATION / XBOX`. A pad connecting never steals the glyphs until used.\n701\t- **Pad mapping:** set `input.gamepadButtons` to your own codes so pad and keyboard stay distinct: `{0:'PadCross',1:'PadCircle',2:'PadSquare',3:'PadTriangle',4:'PadL1',5:'PadR1',6:'PadL2',7:'PadR2',8:'PadCreate',9:'PadOptions',10:'PadL3',11:'PadR3',12:'PadUp',13:'PadDown',14:'PadLeft',15:'PadRight'}`. A small action map in `src/core/intent.js` turns codes into verbs.\n702\t\n703\t### In-game HUD (`src/game/hud.js`)\n704\tSparse, and gone during cutscenes. Bottom left: `COVERAGE` (Max's health bar; flashes `LAPSED` under 25%) with the Dame's bar under it when she's with you. Bottom right: ammo at scale 2 (`12/15`), weapon icon, grenade count. Top right: Doubloons, only for 3 s after they change. Top left: objective line. Bottom centre: the one context prompt, glyph and verb. Centre: the laser dot (no crosshair). Low health adds a heartbeat and a pulsing `red` screen edge. Damage direction: a short red arc at the screen edge. Drawn with `hud.clear()` then redraw every frame.\n705\t\n706\t### Screens (all in `src/screens/`)\n707\t**Title:** live 3D Foghorn scene with slow camera and fog; the title auto-fitted (scale 3 if `hud.measure` fits, else scale 2 split into two lines at a space, since each builder's title differs). Menu: CONTINUE (if a save exists) · NEW CLAIM · NIGHT SHIFT · SETTINGS · ABOUT. 10 s idle → attract.\n708\t**Pause:** RESUME · SETTINGS · RESTART FROM CHECKPOINT · DEV MODE · QUIT TO TITLE.\n709\t**Case, Shop, Claim Form, Claim Denied:** §4. **Map tab:** map rows drawn 2 px per cell with markers. **Files:** one note per page.\n710\t**Settings:** MUSIC (10% default), SFX, VOICE, master; AIM SPEED pad and mouse, INVERT Y, AIM ASSIST; CONTROLLER GLYPHS; SCREEN SHAKE (`engine.shake.strength`); LOOK, PIXEL SIZE, QUALITY, FRAME RATE (through `engine.settings.set`); FULLSCREEN; RESET. Paged, not dense.\n711\t**About/Credits:** paged, scrolling with stick or wheel. Pages: SOURCE INFORMATION (every TASK.md field), TESTING FEEDBACK, ENGINE FEEDBACK, PROMPT FEEDBACK, CREDITS (engine, three.js, Rapier, any packs, with licences; Usage reads `added on import`). The data lives once in `src/data/about.js`.\n712\t**Night Shift lobby, session card, results.**\n713\t\n714\t### Touch-only devices\n715\tDetect touch-only: `navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` and `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no gamepad. Then: `Engine.start` with `touch: false` (no touch controls), the attract mode running behind, a centred panel `CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED`, and a settings button (tappable, tap is a click through `input.buttonEvents`). The moment a gamepad or keyboard appears, drop the panel and show the title. Tapping anywhere else does nothing and never exits attract.\n716\t\n717\t---\n718\t\n719\t## 12. Dev mode\n720\t\n721\tPause → DEV MODE (not shown in hub sessions). Same pixel UI, works with pad, mouse and keyboard. Tabs:\n722\t- **TOOLS:** god mode, no-clip, infinite ammo, one-hit kills, freeze AI, show hit zones (draw zones as thin glow boxes), show nav and flow, show triggers, game speed (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2), skip cutscene, heal, give 10,000 doubloons, give all weapons and items, fill Case, kill all, unlock all, engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug(true)`), current rank, enemies alive.\n723\t- **TELEPORT:** every chapter, area and beat.\n724\t- **SPAWN:** every enemy type, at the laser dot.\n725\t- **BALANCE: live sliders**, each reading `TUNING` every frame, showing value and default, individually resettable by Triangle, with RESET ALL: `walkSpeed runSpeed aimWalkSpeed padAimSpeed mouseAimSpeed aimAssist laserSway weaponDamage fireRate reloadSpeed enemyHp enemySpeed attackTokens windup maxActive staggerChance kickRadius kickDamage lootRate moneyRate damageTaken dameHp dameGrabTime qteWindow`. 8 per page, sliders 100 art pixels wide. Mouse drags them. Saved separately from settings; off when dev mode isn't used.\n726\t\n727\t---\n728\t\n729\t## 13. Attract mode\n730\t\n731\tAfter **10 seconds** with no input on the title or any menu screen reached from it (count `ctx.time`; any key, mouse move or click, pad button or stick past deadzone resets it), start a looping demo. **Any input exits immediately** back to the title. Input that exits does nothing else. Runs on touch-only devices too, where tapping doesn't exit. It never starts while a Night Shift lobby is open or in a hub session.\n732\t\n733\t`src/screens/attract.js` is a director over a list of clips; each loads an area with `attract: true`, Max driven by `BotIntent` with god mode, infinite ammo and free teleports (stuck for 3 s → next waypoint):\n734\t1. Quay siege, 40 s: kicks, windows, ladders, Flenser, the Foghorn.\n735\t2. Case montage, 8 s: items picked, rotated, ARRANGE. Shop montage, 8 s: tune a gun.\n736\t3. Cannery, 30 s: belts, the Dame following, Carrier shot.\n737\t4. Bosun, 25 s: crane drop, sacs bursting.\n738\t5. Causeway, 15 s. Crypt, 15 s. Bathysphere, 30 s. Launch, 15 s.\n739\t6. Title card, 5 s. Loop.\n740\t\n741\tOverlay: a band with `DEMO` and the title, and `PRESS ANY BUTTON` blinking (`CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED` on touch-only). Cover/reveal transitions between clips. The director must survive any clip failing.\n742\t\n743\t---\n744\t\n745\t## 14. Architecture and engine facts\n746\t\n747\t### Setup\n748\t1. Download the kit from TASK.md's link into its own empty folder, then copy `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs`, `packs/`, `CREDITS.md` to the dev folder root. Never edit `pixel-engine.js` (the check: its hash equals the kit's). Read the kit's `GUIDE.md` whole and `ASSETS.md`; search `API.md`.\n749\t2. `package.json` **must** have `\"type\": \"module\"`. **[verified: `npm init -y` writes `\"type\": \"commonjs\"`, and then Node can't import `pixel-engine.js`.]** `npm install playwright@1.63.0` for `check.mjs`.\n750\t3. Reserved URL flags (the engine reads them): `seed debug look filters camera cam zoom mode res touch quality fps`. **[verified: `?cam=` draws a warning.]** Game flags use `g_` prefixes.\n751\t\n752\t### Folder layout\n753\t```\n754\tpixel-engine.js check.mjs packs/ package.json\n755\tindex.html               dev page that loads src/main.js as a module (what the kit's check.mjs plays)\n756\tsrc/main.js              page entry: session or standalone, Engine.start, first scene\n757\tsrc/config.js            TITLE, slug, tagline: the only place the title is written\n758\tsrc/core/                app.js (scene switching), run.js (persistent state), intent.js, device.js, ui.js, save.js\n759\tsrc/game/                area.js (Game hooks per level), mapPaint.js, levelBuild.js, actor.js (Humanoid), player.js,\n760\t                         companion.js, enemy.js, enemies/*.js, bosses/*.js, combat.js, loot.js, interact.js, director.js,\n761\t                         cutscene.js, qte.js, fx.js, world.js (moods, fog, rain, water, tide, backdrops), hud.js, launch.js, bot.js\n762\tsrc/screens/             title.js attract.js pause.js case.js shop.js settings.js about.js form.js denied.js dev.js card.js lobby.js\n763\tsrc/net/                 local.js (LocalSession), shift.js (Night Shift host and client)\n764\tsrc/audio/               sfx.js songs.js voice.js mix.js\n765\tsrc/data/                tuning.js weapons.js items.js enemies.js shop.js dialogue.js notes.js clips.js about.js levels/*.js\n766\tsrc/models/              index.js (exports every def and a ModelCatalog), humans.js, props.js, weapons.js, icons.js\n767\tvendor/hub/              session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js\n768\ttools/                   build.mjs test.mjs capture.py\n769\ttests/                   node/*.mjs browser/*.py\n770\tdocs/CONTENT.md          how to add an area, enemy, weapon, item, line, song without touching systems\n771\t```\n772\t**Data-driven so designers can build on it:** an area is a data module: map commands, theme (char → texture), mood, prop list, Tannoy lines, beats. Beats are a small step language: `{ on: 'enter', zone }`, `say`, `cutscene`, `spawn`, `objective`, `music`, `flag`, `waitUntil`, `openGate`. A new chapter is a new data file. Write `docs/CONTENT.md` as you go.\n773\t\n774\t### Scene structure\n775\t- One `Engine.start`, then `engine.loadGame(new Area(id, entry))` for everything: `TitleScene`, `Area`, `Launch`, `Attract`, `ShiftArena`. **[verified from the source]** `loadGame` frees scene, physics, triggers, particles, HUD, music, lights. Persistent state lives in the `Run` object outside. Transition: `await engine.screen.cover('iris'); await engine.loadGame(next); await engine.screen.reveal('iris');`. Clear the HUD during covers (HUD sits above them).\n776\t- Start options: `withUrlOptions({ container, camera: { preset: 'third', fov: 55 }, look, quality: 'high', touch: false, settings: { button: false, key: slug }, debugUI: false, background: PALETTE.ink })`.\n777\t- **Intent layer:** the player reads a per-step `Intent` (`move, look, aim, fire, firePressed, reload, knife, action, run, heal, command, throw, …`) from `HumanIntent`, `BotIntent` or `NetIntent`, never from `ctx.input`. This one rule makes attract mode, the playthrough test and co-op easy. `HumanIntent` reads held buttons with `isDown` and presses with `consumePress` in `fixedUpdate` (the engine runs `fixedUpdate` before `update`, zero or more times per frame), and look from `input.mouseDelta` in `update`.\n778\t- **Determinism:** `ctx.random` for gameplay, forks for cosmetics; `ctx.time`, not `performance.now()`, in gameplay. Give each `Game` `status()` and `fingerprint()`. `ready(ctx)` installs `window.__GAME__` for tests.\n779\t- **Level build:** floors as textured planes (UV in metres ÷ tile size: `ground.attributes.uv` scaled, see kit `examples/market.js`), walls as textured boxes, greedy-merged rectangles for colliders (`physics.addStaticBox`), `mergeStaticMeshes` for meshes, library models placed via `buildModel` + `addModelColliders`, and a model's `light` placed with `object.localToWorld`. One large ground collider at y=0. Upper floor: a box at y=3.2 with its own walls.\n780\t- Tag small props and characters `noCamera`. Keep the player from getting caught on prop colliders: props use `collider: 'box'` and are placed clear of doors.\n781\t\n782\t### Single-file build **[verified end to end from `file://`, WebGPU on]**\n783\t`tools/build.mjs`:\n784\t1. `esbuild src/main.js --bundle --format=esm --target=es2022 --outfile=dist/bundle.js`. **Don't minify the session client; it isn't in the bundle.**\n785\t2. Escape `</script` in the bundle to `<\\/script`.\n786\t3. Write the deliverable HTML (its name and location from TASK.md, in one constant in `tools/build.mjs`): `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, the `session.js` text in a classic `<script>`, the hub metas, `<title>`, optional `<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-nature.json':'data:application/json;base64,…'};</script>`, `</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\">BUNDLE</script></body></html>`.\n787\t4. Write the exit interview file from `src/data/about.js` (one source for the About screen and the file) and check it parses.\n788\t\n789\tA minimal game is 5.2 MB this way; a pack adds under 1.5 MB. In Node, read packs with `Engine.headless(game, { assets: async (p) => new Uint8Array(await readFile(new URL(p, root))).buffer })`.\n790\t\n791\t### Engine gotchas [verified]\n792\t- `pg.screenshot` of a WebGPU canvas comes out blank here. Use `await engine.renderer.capture()` plus `engine.hud.canvas`; **set alpha to 255 before saving**: the vignette leaves alpha below 1 in the frame, and a PNG with alpha looks washed out. (On screen the page background is dark, so it's only a capture concern.) `tools/capture.py` does this: launch Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, `await window.__PIXEL_READY__`, `engine.step(30)`, capture, draw HUD canvas over it at full size with `imageSmoothingEnabled = false`, `toDataURL`.\n793\t- `restPoseOf` isn't exported; use `compileClips`.\n794\t- Put `model()` defs in their own modules: importing a module that calls `Engine.start` starts an engine.\n795\t- `CharacterController`'s collider isn't tagged `character`: tag it `noCamera` or the camera ray hits it from inside.\n796\t- `ctx.physics.castRay(from, dir, max, ignoreTags, excludeBody)`. Tags are free strings (`physics.tag(collider, 'player')`).\n797\t- `physics.conveyor` doesn't carry a `CharacterController`. Add the belt's velocity yourself from the map cell under the feet.\n798\t- Wheel and +/- zoom the rig unless `rig.zoomable = false`.\n799\t- `AudioManager` persists under one shared key: set `persist = false` as in §10.\n800\t- Point lights come from the pool: 16 at `quality: 'high'`, nearest and highest-priority first. Never `new PointLight`.\n801\t- Materials are shared: never change a toon material's colour on one enemy.\n802\t- Flow field rebuild on a 64×48 grid is about 1.4 ms: rebuild only when the player changes cell (the engine does this for you).\n803\t\n804\t---\n805\t\n806\t## 15. Testing\n807\t\n808\tOne command: `node tools/test.mjs`. It prints only failures and a final line `N passed, M failed`. `--only <name>` runs one suite; `--fast` skips browsers. Rerun only what your change covers. At most 2 browsers at once, closed afterwards, on `file://` or a 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-picked port you started and stop by PID (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`: without `-u` the port line stays buffered when redirected to a file **[verified]**). Keep files in your folder. Don't use subagents or workflows to review or judge. Screenshots only for what a script can't see (§8 moods, TV view at 1920×1080).\n809\t\n810\t**Node (`Engine.headless`, fast **[verified: 120 frames with 7 puppets in under a second, replay equal, joints posed]**):**\n811\t- Maps: paint, every cell reachable, markers exist. Case: fit, rotate, arrange, overflow, combine. Shop: buy, sell, tune, can't afford. Damage: each zone and weapon; stagger chances with seeded random; kick cone. Loot director needs. Save round trip. Strings: all data strings only use font characters. `parseSong` every song; `renderSound` every sound non-silent and not clipping; voice: every speaker produces blips. `checkModel`/`validateTexture` all defs without problems; `validateClip` all clips.\n812\t- AI: tokens never exceeded; a crowd of 30 reaches a player and attacks; door bash; vault; ladder; floor links; Foghorn sends all to sea; Carrier takes the Dame and shooting drops her; Limpet reaches a corpse; Knight hears running.\n813\t- Set pieces: Winch reaches 100%; crane drop stuns the Bosun; lens puzzle; tide kills on time; QTE success and failure paths.\n814\t- **The whole game, played by a bot (`src/game/bot.js`):** each area's data has a plan (`goto`, `kill`, `interact`, `shop`, `command`, `qte`). The bot computes yaw and pitch to heads, reloads, heals below 40%, kicks prompts, runs when surrounded, buys per script through the same menu actions, and plays from Arrival to the credits on Standard, no cheats. Fails if stuck for 60 s or more than 3 deaths in a chapter. Prints per-chapter ammo, money and deaths in verbose mode: that's your balance report (aim: ends each chapter with some but not plenty).\n815\t- Replay: record 60 s of a siege with `engine.recording()`, replay, compare `fingerprint()`.\n816\t- Attract: idle title 600 frames starts it; any key or pad press exits; it loops through all clips with no error.\n817\t- Co-op sim: host and client game objects through a fake `session` with latency: snapshots stay under 1,200 bytes with 24 enemies, rates under 20/s, shots resolve, revive, dawn and all-down.\n818\t\n819\t**Browser (deliverable from `file://`, unless the harness):**\n820\t- Boots with no console errors; `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty; the kit's own `node check.mjs` passes on the dev page.\n821\t- Gamepad stub (`add_init_script` replacing `navigator.getGamepads` with a standard-mapping pad): menus, aim, fire, Case, pause; prompts show PS glyphs; setting Xbox switches; keyboard press switches to keys at once. Mouse: hover moves focus, click selects, `addPointer` aims.\n822\t- Phone profile (Chromium, touch): touch controls absent, required panel shown, attract running, tap doesn't exit it, settings button opens Settings.\n823\t- Audio: first boot `audio.volume.music === 0.1`; music bus `AnalyserNode` level above silence; Reset returns to 10%.\n824\t- Dev mode reachable from pause; slider changes `TUNING` live; reset restores.\n825\t- About screen has all pages; exit interview parses.\n826\t- **Hub harness:** the harness only loads same-origin pages and imports `./bridge.js` and `./round.js`, so copy the deliverable and the three harness files into one test folder and serve that. Each run goes until `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, needing `window.__hubCheck.pass`: `?game=…&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. **[verified: about 22-33 s each with 4 WebGPU copies.]** Confirm the page is your game first.\n827\t- Standalone: outside a session the deliverable runs normally. Two pages in one context run a Night Shift party over BroadcastChannel, and over WebRTC codes with `?g_nostun=1`; both reach dawn or all-down with a results screen.\n828\t- WebKit and Firefox here have no WebGPU: expect the engine's clear message, and check that it appears and nothing else breaks.\n829\t\n830\tBefore finishing: look at captures of each mood, the Case, the Shop, a menu at 1920×1080 and at 4:3.\n831\t\n832\t---\n833\t\n834\t## 16. Build order\n835\t\n836\tEach milestone ends playable and tested. Commit nothing unless asked. Don't polish one area while others don't exist.\n837\t\n838\t1. **Skeleton:** folder, build script, deliverable from `file://`, hub metas, config, session/standalone split, title scene, test command. Test the harness now, with an empty card and instant finish: it's cheap and keeps you honest.\n839\t2. **Feel:** one test yard. Camera, movement, aim, laser, pistol, Humanoid, puppets, one Islander with zones, stagger, kick. Spend real time here until shooting and kicking feel good.\n840\t3. **Crowd:** AI states, tokens, flow fields, Limpet, Loot Director, knife, crates.\n841\t4. **Case and Shop:** UI kit, Case, Shop, glyphs, device tracking, pause, settings, saves.\n842\t5. **Chapter 1:** map paint, level build, dressing, doors, windows, ladders, wardrobe, Siege, Foghorn, Tannoys. Cutscenes, dialogue, voice, first songs. Bot plays it.\n843\t6. **Dev mode and attract** in their first versions, extended as content grows.\n844\t7. **Chapter 2:** road, cannery, Dame, Flenser, winch, belt fight, Bosun.\n845\t8. **Chapter 3:** causeway, abbey, crypt, nave, Bathysphere, launch, ending, credits.\n846\t9. **Night Shift:** solo, then hub co-op, then LocalSession.\n847\t10. **Polish:** every song and sound, every animation in the list, hit feedback, HUD details, Claim Forms, About, `docs/CONTENT.md`, balance with the bot, then by reading its numbers. Remove anything unfinished.\n848\t11. **Done list** (§17).\n849\t\n850\t**If you truly run out of road, cut whole features from this list in this order, cleanly, with no leftovers:** Launch (end at the nave; keep the ending scene) → WebRTC invite codes (keep same-computer parties) → the Dame's solo crypt (she climbs out; keep the lever beat as a cutscene) → the causeway's rowboats → Claim Notes. **Never cut:** aiming, zones and kicks; the Case and Shop; the Siege and Foghorn; the Dame; the Bosun and final boss; hub multiplayer; dev mode and sliders; attract mode; glyphs; the About screen. Report what you cut."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"6de88e96-d573-475a-b11c-106bf0622c56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:13.680Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","content":"  palette: { coat: 'teal', band: 'orange', pants: 'night', skin: 'mist', hat: 'navy', boot: 'ink' },\n  parts: [ J('Pelvis', [0, 0.62, 0], [ { box: [0.44, 0.2, 0.28], at: [0, 0.02, 0], c: 'pants' },\n    J('Torso', [0, 0, 0], [ { box: [0.42, 0.48, 0.26], at: [0, 0.32, 0], c: 'coat' },\n      J('Head', [0, 0.6, 0], [ { box: [0.31, 0.3, 0.3], at: [0, 0.13, 0], c: 'skin' },\n                               { box: [0.27, 0.07, 0.04], at: [0, 0.16, 0.16], c: 'band', glow: true } ]),\n      /* ArmR, ArmL */ ]), /* LegR, LegL */ ]) ] });\n```\nA glowing eye band in `orange` reads brilliantly at 15 m **[verified]**. It's the game's signature: all infected have it; Limpet-free people don't.\n\nThe camera sits behind Max all game, so her back is her best side: hair covering the back of the head, scarf, coat belt and seam.\n\nGiants: `object.scale.setScalar(2.6)` (hit-zone radii scale too). Add props to joints: `object.getObjectByName('HandR').add(gun)`. Swap palettes per variant through `buildModel(id, { palette })`. Spring tails: `SpringChain` for Max's scarf and coat skirt, the Bosun's chain.\n\n### Asset list (all `src/models/`, new unless noted)\n- **Characters:** Max, the Dame, Islander (×3 palettes, sou'wester, cap, bare), Net-Wife, Bottler, Deckhand, Carrier (sack), Flenser, Re-Salted, Monk, Reliquary Knight, Drowned, Harpooner, Mate Ansgar, Nils, Commodore, Mr. Fathom (helmet: `ball` + `torus` porthole with `glass` slot glow + bolts), Bosun, Bathysphere, Mother Limpet, Limpet (low crawler: `ball half`, tentacle `tube`s).\n- **Quay props:** Tannoy on a pole (horn `cyl`, breaks), Foghorn tower (backdrop, 20 m), mail boat, rowboat, lobster pot, drying rack with fish, draped net, bollard, buoy, anchor, chain links, fish crate, Brine Barrel (red band), hay cart (re-coloured `cart` + `haystack`), effigy in a suit, telegraph desk.\n- **Cannery:** gutting table, conveyor frames (`beltMaterial` for moving belts), hanging carcasses on a rail, ice blocks, winch, roll-up shutter, gantry crane and pallet, steam pipes, `THOLE & SONS` sign (use `textureDef` `path` layers).\n- **Abbey:** lamp statue with lens beam, floor mosaic, Font, pews, stained-glass panels (flat `glow` parts), organ pipes.\n- **Launch:** launch hull with stern deck, sea stacks, mine, arch.\n- **Weapons:** pistol, scattergun, rifle, harpoon gun, bolt, flare, depth charge, oil bottle, knife, Flenser's saw, gaff hook, boathook, flail, shield, halberd, Dame's cane and handbag.\n- **Library, as they are or re-coloured:** `door window stone-wall wall-corner timber-wall roof chimney fence ladder lamp-post wall-lantern hanging-lantern brazier candles campfire flame barrel crate crate-stack sack rope-coil bucket keg table chair bench desk shelf wardrobe bed fireplace well market-stall cart haystack clothesline dead-tree rock boulders reeds tall-grass tombstone column altar banner portcullis sarcophagus lever wall-chains cage cobweb puddle`. Textures: `cobbles dirt moss deck planks flagstones dry-stone bricks rough-boards metal-plates rust slate-roof wet-sand shallow-water basalt ruined-mosaic`.\n- **Packs (optional, for richness):** `kenney-nature` cliffs (`cliff-large-rock`, `cliff-block-rock`) for backdrops, `kenney-castle` towers and walls for the abbey silhouette. For the single file, each pack goes in `window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__` (§14). **[verified]** Credit them on the About screen; they're CC0.\n- **HUD icons:** `textureDef`s using `path` or `pixels`, read through `hudSprite`. Sized to their Case footprint (pistol 42×28 px). Glyphs: §11.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Animation\n\nBase: `compileClips`, `gaitClip`, `ClipDef` data, one `THREE.AnimationMixer` per character. Write a `Humanoid` (`src/game/actor.js`) that all characters share. **Masked layers [verified]:** legs and upper body are separate actions on one mixer:\n\n```js\nconst UPPER = /^(Torso|Head|Arm|Forearm|Hand)/, LOWER = /^(Pelvis|Leg|Shin|Foot)/;\nconst mask = (clip, re, name) => new THREE.AnimationClip(name, clip.duration, clip.tracks.filter((t) => re.test(t.name.split('.')[0])));\n```\nMax walks with `mask(Walk, LOWER)` while `mask(AimPistol, UPPER)` holds the gun up. After the mixer, add the aim pitch to the arms and torso (rotate `ArmR`, `ArmL`, `Torso`, `Head` quaternions) so the gun follows the laser. Locomotion `timeScale = speed / clip.speed` (authored: Walk 2, Run 6, CrouchWalk 1.4; custom `gaitClip`s carry their own). `validateClip` and `analyzeClip` in tests.\n\nFrom `HERO_CLIPS` as they are: `Idle IdleLook Walk Run Crouch Climb Push Hurt HitReact Death GetUp Roll Kick Punch Shout Slam Slash1 Slash2 Slash3 Sit LieIdle`.\n\n**New clips (data in `src/data/clips.js`):**\n- **Max:** AimPistol, AimLong (two-handed), FirePistol / FireLong recoil overlays, ReloadPistol, ReloadPump, ReloadBolt, Roundhouse (the kick: full-body spin), HipThrow, KnifeSlash, DoorKick, Vault, LadderUp, QuickTurn, Throw, Boost, Stagger, KnockedDown, StampForm.\n- **Islanders:** Shamble (`gaitClip(HERO_RIG, { name: 'Shamble', frames: 40, speed: 1.1, stance: 0.62, hip: -0.05, bob: 0.02, lift: 0.04, lean: 16, sway: 7, head: 8, arms: { swing: 8, elbow: 30 } })` **[verified: reads well]**), Lurch (run), WorkChop, WorkMend, RaiseTool (wind-up), Swing, ThrowOverhand, StunHands (hands to face), KneelHit, BashDoor, ClimbIn, WalkToSea (slow, arms slack), Wade.\n- **Others:** SawRev, SawSwing, SawLunge; ShieldWalk, ShieldBlock, FlailSpin; KnightWalk (heavy gait), HalberdSweep; DrownedRise; CarrierShoulder, CarrierWalk; DameWalk (tiny steps, cane), DameCane, DameBarrelIn, DameHoist; FathomIdle (bob, tap helmet), FathomPresent (coat open).\n- **Bosses:** AnsgarHook, AnsgarSwing; BosunDrag, BosunSweep, BosunThrow, BosunStomp, BosunKneel, BosunRoar; BathyWalk, BathyCharge, BathySag; MotherSpit.\n- **Procedural:** head look-at (rotate `Head`), breathing `layers` on idles, `Squash` on landings, `SpringChain` tails, ragdolls on violent deaths.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Audio\n\nAll code, no files. Engine `ctx.audio` (`register`, `play(name, { volume, pitch, pan })`, `loop`, `playMusic`, `Song` data), `spatialize` for positions, `muffle` for through-wall. In Node every call is a counted no-op, and `renderSound(def)` gives samples **[verified]**, so sounds can be tested without a browser.\n\n### Volumes: music 10% by default\n`AudioManager` defaults are master 0.8, sfx 1, music 0.6 and its Reset returns to those **[verified]**. So: set `audio.persist = false`; keep volumes in your own settings (music default **0.10**, sfx 1, voice 1, master 0.8); apply them with `audio.setVolume` at boot and on change; your Settings Reset restores 0.10. Don't show the engine's panel (`settings: { button: false, key: slug }`). The test asserts `engine.audio.volume.music === 0.1` on a first run. Author song tracks loud enough to be heard at 10%: track `volume` about 0.5-0.8; check levels with an `AnalyserNode` on the music bus.\n\n### SFX (`src/audio/sfx.js`, about 45 `SoundDef`s with `layers`)\nPistol (square snap + noise burst + low thump), scatter (bigger, longer noise), rifle (crack + tail), harpoon (twang + thud), dry click, reloads (2-3 clicks each), kick whoosh + impact, knife, body hits, head pop, enemy grunts (noise + pitch), door kick, window glass, ladder, crate break, Brine Barrel, flare hiss, depth charge, fire loop, Tannoy on/off crackle, Tannoy destroyed, foghorn (long, layered low saws, the most important sound in the game), saw loop (saw wave with `vibrato`, pitch rises on lunge), steam jet, rain loop, sea loop, gulls, conveyor loop, crane, chain, telegraph key clicks, bubbling (Fathom), UI move/confirm/back/stamp thud, QTE pop, heartbeat (low health), Limpet skitter, rubber stamp.\n\n### Music (`src/audio/songs.js`, original compositions, `Song` data validated by `parseSong`)\n| Song | Feel |\n| --- | --- |\n| `title` | 66 bpm, D minor. Drone, slow low bell, sparse triangle melody |\n| `explore` | 72 bpm, A minor. Plucked bass, long silences, one uneasy phrase |\n| `combat` | 132 bpm, E minor. Square ostinato, noise hats; layered in when alerted |\n| `siege` | 120 bpm. Drums and low bass with chanted gibberish over it |\n| `shop` | 104 bpm, G major. A jaunty shanty on a detuned square \"accordion\" |\n| `safe` | 60 bpm, C major. Soft triangle chords, faint telegraph rhythm |\n| `boss` | 150 bpm, C minor. Driving, brass-like saw, tolling on the bar |\n| `onhold` | 96 bpm. Cheerful Muzak (the Pym gag, ending credits) |\n| `tide` | Rising pitch each loop, for the causeway |\n| `dawn` | Short resolve for the launch ending |\n\nMusic fades through a small `Mix` helper (tween the channel down, swap, tween up to the user's level). Silence is part of the score: no music in the Cold Room, crypt or Foghorn.\n\n### Voices: Animalese/Simlish gibberish (`src/audio/voice.js`)\nEvery spoken line has text and voice. Pre-register syllables per speaker (5 vowel colours × 2 consonant styles) as `SoundDef`s and play one every 2 letters with `play(name, { pitch, volume, pan })`. Pitch from a hash of the word (the same word sounds the same), falling at `.`, rising at `?`, louder at `!`; pause at spaces and punctuation; typing speed matches the text.\n\n| Speaker | Recipe |\n| --- | --- |\n| Max | Triangle, mid (170 Hz), short, level |\n| Dame | Square duty 0.25, high (320 Hz), `vibrato` wobble, clipped |\n| Commodore | Square, nasal (260 Hz), `crush: 8`, noise crackle layer (Tannoy) |\n| Fathom | Triangle low (110 Hz), slow decay, plus a bubble blip every few syllables (`muffle` feel) |\n| Pym | Sine, flat pitch (200 Hz), `crush: 6` |\n| Islanders | Saw, low (120 Hz), barked, 2-3 syllables, spatial |\n| Monks | Three layered low sines, a chant |\n| Bosun | One long 60 Hz bellow |\n\nA `voice` settings slider scales the volume passed to `play`.\n\n---\n\n## 11. UI and UX: 10-foot, controller first\n\nAll screens are drawn on the engine's pixel HUD (`ctx.hud`), the same screens for every input. Art resolution is 480×270 with adaptive width: lay out from anchors, and test at 4:3 (width 360) too. **[verified: scale 1 text is 28 px tall at 1080p: the minimum, for secondary text only.]** Titles and primary labels use scale 2. At most 6-7 list rows per screen, one large selected item, plenty of empty space. No tables of numbers.\n\n- **Font:** uppercase only. Characters: `0-9 A-Z . , : ; - + = / ( ) [ ] { } % _ ! ? < > # ' ‘ ’ “ ” * @ ° · & | \\ ~ ^ $`. Anything else draws as `?`. A test scans every string in `src/data`.\n- **Menus run with `engine.timeScale = 0`, never `engine.paused`.** **[verified]** At time scale 0 `update(ctx, 0)` still runs, `fixedUpdate` doesn't, `wasPressed` works; with `paused` the live loop doesn't call `update` at all. Use `wasPressed` in menus and a real-time counter (cosmetic only) for animation.\n- **`src/core/ui.js`:** text, panel, list, slider, tabs, grid. Each widget registers a rectangle. Focus moves by stick/D-pad with key repeat; hover moves focus; click activates; `input.buttonEvents` for clicks; convert `input.pointer` from NDC to art pixels. A clear focus bar with a small arrow. `uiPrompt(action, label)` draws the glyph for the current device, in a prompt bar at the bottom of every screen.\n- **Glyphs:** sprites, about 10×10: PlayStation (Cross blue, Circle red, Square pink, Triangle green; L1 R1 L2 R2, Options, Create as small pills; D-pad; sticks); Xbox (A green, B red, X blue, Y yellow; LB RB LT RT, Menu, View); keycaps (outlined box with the key's letter); mouse (body with left, right or wheel lit).\n- **Last input tracking** (`src/core/device.js`): DOM `keydown`, mouse `pointermove`, `wheel` → keyboard; per-frame `navigator.getGamepads()` with any button or stick past the deadzone → pad. Prompts change at once. Settings: `CONTROLLER GLYPHS: PLAYSTATION / XBOX`. A pad connecting never steals the glyphs until used.\n- **Pad mapping:** set `input.gamepadButtons` to your own codes so pad and keyboard stay distinct: `{0:'PadCross',1:'PadCircle',2:'PadSquare',3:'PadTriangle',4:'PadL1',5:'PadR1',6:'PadL2',7:'PadR2',8:'PadCreate',9:'PadOptions',10:'PadL3',11:'PadR3',12:'PadUp',13:'PadDown',14:'PadLeft',15:'PadRight'}`. A small action map in `src/core/intent.js` turns codes into verbs.\n\n### In-game HUD (`src/game/hud.js`)\nSparse, and gone during cutscenes. Bottom left: `COVERAGE` (Max's health bar; flashes `LAPSED` under 25%) with the Dame's bar under it when she's with you. Bottom right: ammo at scale 2 (`12/15`), weapon icon, grenade count. Top right: Doubloons, only for 3 s after they change. Top left: objective line. Bottom centre: the one context prompt, glyph and verb. Centre: the laser dot (no crosshair). Low health adds a heartbeat and a pulsing `red` screen edge. Damage direction: a short red arc at the screen edge. Drawn with `hud.clear()` then redraw every frame.\n\n### Screens (all in `src/screens/`)\n**Title:** live 3D Foghorn scene with slow camera and fog; the title auto-fitted (scale 3 if `hud.measure` fits, else scale 2 split into two lines at a space, since each builder's title differs). Menu: CONTINUE (if a save exists) · NEW CLAIM · NIGHT SHIFT · SETTINGS · ABOUT. 10 s idle → attract.\n**Pause:** RESUME · SETTINGS · RESTART FROM CHECKPOINT · DEV MODE · QUIT TO TITLE.\n**Case, Shop, Claim Form, Claim Denied:** §4. **Map tab:** map rows drawn 2 px per cell with markers. **Files:** one note per page.\n**Settings:** MUSIC (10% default), SFX, VOICE, master; AIM SPEED pad and mouse, INVERT Y, AIM ASSIST; CONTROLLER GLYPHS; SCREEN SHAKE (`engine.shake.strength`); LOOK, PIXEL SIZE, QUALITY, FRAME RATE (through `engine.settings.set`); FULLSCREEN; RESET. Paged, not dense.\n**About/Credits:** paged, scrolling with stick or wheel. Pages: SOURCE INFORMATION (every TASK.md field), TESTING FEEDBACK, ENGINE FEEDBACK, PROMPT FEEDBACK, CREDITS (engine, three.js, Rapier, any packs, with licences; Usage reads `added on import`). The data lives once in `src/data/about.js`.\n**Night Shift lobby, session card, results.**\n\n### Touch-only devices\nDetect touch-only: `navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0` and `!matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches` and no gamepad. Then: `Engine.start` with `touch: false` (no touch controls), the attract mode running behind, a centred panel `CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED`, and a settings button (tappable, tap is a click through `input.buttonEvents`). The moment a gamepad or keyboard appears, drop the panel and show the title. Tapping anywhere else does nothing and never exits attract.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Dev mode\n\nPause → DEV MODE (not shown in hub sessions). Same pixel UI, works with pad, mouse and keyboard. Tabs:\n- **TOOLS:** god mode, no-clip, infinite ammo, one-hit kills, freeze AI, show hit zones (draw zones as thin glow boxes), show nav and flow, show triggers, game speed (0.25 / 0.5 / 1 / 2), skip cutscene, heal, give 10,000 doubloons, give all weapons and items, fill Case, kill all, unlock all, engine debug panel (`engine.showDebug(true)`), current rank, enemies alive.\n- **TELEPORT:** every chapter, area and beat.\n- **SPAWN:** every enemy type, at the laser dot.\n- **BALANCE: live sliders**, each reading `TUNING` every frame, showing value and default, individually resettable by Triangle, with RESET ALL: `walkSpeed runSpeed aimWalkSpeed padAimSpeed mouseAimSpeed aimAssist laserSway weaponDamage fireRate reloadSpeed enemyHp enemySpeed attackTokens windup maxActive staggerChance kickRadius kickDamage lootRate moneyRate damageTaken dameHp dameGrabTime qteWindow`. 8 per page, sliders 100 art pixels wide. Mouse drags them. Saved separately from settings; off when dev mode isn't used.\n\n---\n\n## 13. Attract mode\n\nAfter **10 seconds** with no input on the title or any menu screen reached from it (count `ctx.time`; any key, mouse move or click, pad button or stick past deadzone resets it), start a looping demo. **Any input exits immediately** back to the title. Input that exits does nothing else. Runs on touch-only devices too, where tapping doesn't exit. It never starts while a Night Shift lobby is open or in a hub session.\n\n`src/screens/attract.js` is a director over a list of clips; each loads an area with `attract: true`, Max driven by `BotIntent` with god mode, infinite ammo and free teleports (stuck for 3 s → next waypoint):\n1. Quay siege, 40 s: kicks, windows, ladders, Flenser, the Foghorn.\n2. Case montage, 8 s: items picked, rotated, ARRANGE. Shop montage, 8 s: tune a gun.\n3. Cannery, 30 s: belts, the Dame following, Carrier shot.\n4. Bosun, 25 s: crane drop, sacs bursting.\n5. Causeway, 15 s. Crypt, 15 s. Bathysphere, 30 s. Launch, 15 s.\n6. Title card, 5 s. Loop.\n\nOverlay: a band with `DEMO` and the title, and `PRESS ANY BUTTON` blinking (`CONTROLLER OR KEYBOARD REQUIRED` on touch-only). Cover/reveal transitions between clips. The director must survive any clip failing.\n\n---\n\n## 14. Architecture and engine facts\n\n### Setup\n1. Download the kit from TASK.md's link into its own empty folder, then copy `pixel-engine.js`, `check.mjs`, `packs/`, `CREDITS.md` to the dev folder root. Never edit `pixel-engine.js` (the check: its hash equals the kit's). Read the kit's `GUIDE.md` whole and `ASSETS.md`; search `API.md`.\n2. `package.json` **must** have `\"type\": \"module\"`. **[verified: `npm init -y` writes `\"type\": \"commonjs\"`, and then Node can't import `pixel-engine.js`.]** `npm install playwright@1.63.0` for `check.mjs`.\n3. Reserved URL flags (the engine reads them): `seed debug look filters camera cam zoom mode res touch quality fps`. **[verified: `?cam=` draws a warning.]** Game flags use `g_` prefixes.\n\n### Folder layout\n```\npixel-engine.js check.mjs packs/ package.json\nindex.html               dev page that loads src/main.js as a module (what the kit's check.mjs plays)\nsrc/main.js              page entry: session or standalone, Engine.start, first scene\nsrc/config.js            TITLE, slug, tagline: the only place the title is written\nsrc/core/                app.js (scene switching), run.js (persistent state), intent.js, device.js, ui.js, save.js\nsrc/game/                area.js (Game hooks per level), mapPaint.js, levelBuild.js, actor.js (Humanoid), player.js,\n                         companion.js, enemy.js, enemies/*.js, bosses/*.js, combat.js, loot.js, interact.js, director.js,\n                         cutscene.js, qte.js, fx.js, world.js (moods, fog, rain, water, tide, backdrops), hud.js, launch.js, bot.js\nsrc/screens/             title.js attract.js pause.js case.js shop.js settings.js about.js form.js denied.js dev.js card.js lobby.js\nsrc/net/                 local.js (LocalSession), shift.js (Night Shift host and client)\nsrc/audio/               sfx.js songs.js voice.js mix.js\nsrc/data/                tuning.js weapons.js items.js enemies.js shop.js dialogue.js notes.js clips.js about.js levels/*.js\nsrc/models/              index.js (exports every def and a ModelCatalog), humans.js, props.js, weapons.js, icons.js\nvendor/hub/              session.js harness.html bridge.js round.js\ntools/                   build.mjs test.mjs capture.py\ntests/                   node/*.mjs browser/*.py\ndocs/CONTENT.md          how to add an area, enemy, weapon, item, line, song without touching systems\n```\n**Data-driven so designers can build on it:** an area is a data module: map commands, theme (char → texture), mood, prop list, Tannoy lines, beats. Beats are a small step language: `{ on: 'enter', zone }`, `say`, `cutscene`, `spawn`, `objective`, `music`, `flag`, `waitUntil`, `openGate`. A new chapter is a new data file. Write `docs/CONTENT.md` as you go.\n\n### Scene structure\n- One `Engine.start`, then `engine.loadGame(new Area(id, entry))` for everything: `TitleScene`, `Area`, `Launch`, `Attract`, `ShiftArena`. **[verified from the source]** `loadGame` frees scene, physics, triggers, particles, HUD, music, lights. Persistent state lives in the `Run` object outside. Transition: `await engine.screen.cover('iris'); await engine.loadGame(next); await engine.screen.reveal('iris');`. Clear the HUD during covers (HUD sits above them).\n- Start options: `withUrlOptions({ container, camera: { preset: 'third', fov: 55 }, look, quality: 'high', touch: false, settings: { button: false, key: slug }, debugUI: false, background: PALETTE.ink })`.\n- **Intent layer:** the player reads a per-step `Intent` (`move, look, aim, fire, firePressed, reload, knife, action, run, heal, command, throw, …`) from `HumanIntent`, `BotIntent` or `NetIntent`, never from `ctx.input`. This one rule makes attract mode, the playthrough test and co-op easy. `HumanIntent` reads held buttons with `isDown` and presses with `consumePress` in `fixedUpdate` (the engine runs `fixedUpdate` before `update`, zero or more times per frame), and look from `input.mouseDelta` in `update`.\n- **Determinism:** `ctx.random` for gameplay, forks for cosmetics; `ctx.time`, not `performance.now()`, in gameplay. Give each `Game` `status()` and `fingerprint()`. `ready(ctx)` installs `window.__GAME__` for tests.\n- **Level build:** floors as textured planes (UV in metres ÷ tile size: `ground.attributes.uv` scaled, see kit `examples/market.js`), walls as textured boxes, greedy-merged rectangles for colliders (`physics.addStaticBox`), `mergeStaticMeshes` for meshes, library models placed via `buildModel` + `addModelColliders`, and a model's `light` placed with `object.localToWorld`. One large ground collider at y=0. Upper floor: a box at y=3.2 with its own walls.\n- Tag small props and characters `noCamera`. Keep the player from getting caught on prop colliders: props use `collider: 'box'` and are placed clear of doors.\n\n### Single-file build **[verified end to end from `file://`, WebGPU on]**\n`tools/build.mjs`:\n1. `esbuild src/main.js --bundle --format=esm --target=es2022 --outfile=dist/bundle.js`. **Don't minify the session client; it isn't in the bundle.**\n2. Escape `</script` in the bundle to `<\\/script`.\n3. Write the deliverable HTML (its name and location from TASK.md, in one constant in `tools/build.mjs`): `<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\">`, the `session.js` text in a classic `<script>`, the hub metas, `<title>`, optional `<script>window.__PIXEL_ASSETS__={'packs/kenney-nature.json':'data:application/json;base64,…'};</script>`, `</head><body><div id=\"app\"></div><script type=\"module\">BUNDLE</script></body></html>`.\n4. Write the exit interview file from `src/data/about.js` (one source for the About screen and the file) and check it parses.\n\nA minimal game is 5.2 MB this way; a pack adds under 1.5 MB. In Node, read packs with `Engine.headless(game, { assets: async (p) => new Uint8Array(await readFile(new URL(p, root))).buffer })`.\n\n### Engine gotchas [verified]\n- `pg.screenshot` of a WebGPU canvas comes out blank here. Use `await engine.renderer.capture()` plus `engine.hud.canvas`; **set alpha to 255 before saving**: the vignette leaves alpha below 1 in the frame, and a PNG with alpha looks washed out. (On screen the page background is dark, so it's only a capture concern.) `tools/capture.py` does this: launch Chromium with `--enable-unsafe-webgpu --enable-features=Vulkan --use-vulkan=swiftshader --use-angle=swiftshader --use-webgpu-adapter=swiftshader`, `await window.__PIXEL_READY__`, `engine.step(30)`, capture, draw HUD canvas over it at full size with `imageSmoothingEnabled = false`, `toDataURL`.\n- `restPoseOf` isn't exported; use `compileClips`.\n- Put `model()` defs in their own modules: importing a module that calls `Engine.start` starts an engine.\n- `CharacterController`'s collider isn't tagged `character`: tag it `noCamera` or the camera ray hits it from inside.\n- `ctx.physics.castRay(from, dir, max, ignoreTags, excludeBody)`. Tags are free strings (`physics.tag(collider, 'player')`).\n- `physics.conveyor` doesn't carry a `CharacterController`. Add the belt's velocity yourself from the map cell under the feet.\n- Wheel and +/- zoom the rig unless `rig.zoomable = false`.\n- `AudioManager` persists under one shared key: set `persist = false` as in §10.\n- Point lights come from the pool: 16 at `quality: 'high'`, nearest and highest-priority first. Never `new PointLight`.\n- Materials are shared: never change a toon material's colour on one enemy.\n- Flow field rebuild on a 64×48 grid is about 1.4 ms: rebuild only when the player changes cell (the engine does this for you).\n\n---\n\n## 15. Testing\n\nOne command: `node tools/test.mjs`. It prints only failures and a final line `N passed, M failed`. `--only <name>` runs one suite; `--fast` skips browsers. Rerun only what your change covers. At most 2 browsers at once, closed afterwards, on `file://` or a 127.0.0.1 server on an OS-picked port you started and stop by PID (`python3 -u -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1`: without `-u` the port line stays buffered when redirected to a file **[verified]**). Keep files in your folder. Don't use subagents or workflows to review or judge. Screenshots only for what a script can't see (§8 moods, TV view at 1920×1080).\n\n**Node (`Engine.headless`, fast **[verified: 120 frames with 7 puppets in under a second, replay equal, joints posed]**):**\n- Maps: paint, every cell reachable, markers exist. Case: fit, rotate, arrange, overflow, combine. Shop: buy, sell, tune, can't afford. Damage: each zone and weapon; stagger chances with seeded random; kick cone. Loot director needs. Save round trip. Strings: all data strings only use font characters. `parseSong` every song; `renderSound` every sound non-silent and not clipping; voice: every speaker produces blips. `checkModel`/`validateTexture` all defs without problems; `validateClip` all clips.\n- AI: tokens never exceeded; a crowd of 30 reaches a player and attacks; door bash; vault; ladder; floor links; Foghorn sends all to sea; Carrier takes the Dame and shooting drops her; Limpet reaches a corpse; Knight hears running.\n- Set pieces: Winch reaches 100%; crane drop stuns the Bosun; lens puzzle; tide kills on time; QTE success and failure paths.\n- **The whole game, played by a bot (`src/game/bot.js`):** each area's data has a plan (`goto`, `kill`, `interact`, `shop`, `command`, `qte`). The bot computes yaw and pitch to heads, reloads, heals below 40%, kicks prompts, runs when surrounded, buys per script through the same menu actions, and plays from Arrival to the credits on Standard, no cheats. Fails if stuck for 60 s or more than 3 deaths in a chapter. Prints per-chapter ammo, money and deaths in verbose mode: that's your balance report (aim: ends each chapter with some but not plenty).\n- Replay: record 60 s of a siege with `engine.recording()`, replay, compare `fingerprint()`.\n- Attract: idle title 600 frames starts it; any key or pad press exits; it loops through all clips with no error.\n- Co-op sim: host and client game objects through a fake `session` with latency: snapshots stay under 1,200 bytes with 24 enemies, rates under 20/s, shots resolve, revive, dawn and all-down.\n\n**Browser (deliverable from `file://`, unless the harness):**\n- Boots with no console errors; `engine.errors` and `gpuErrors` empty; the kit's own `node check.mjs` passes on the dev page.\n- Gamepad stub (`add_init_script` replacing `navigator.getGamepads` with a standard-mapping pad): menus, aim, fire, Case, pause; prompts show PS glyphs; setting Xbox switches; keyboard press switches to keys at once. Mouse: hover moves focus, click selects, `addPointer` aims.\n- Phone profile (Chromium, touch): touch controls absent, required panel shown, attract running, tap doesn't exit it, settings button opens Settings.\n- Audio: first boot `audio.volume.music === 0.1`; music bus `AnalyserNode` level above silence; Reset returns to 10%.\n- Dev mode reachable from pause; slider changes `TUNING` live; reset restores.\n- About screen has all pages; exit interview parses.\n- **Hub harness:** the harness only loads same-origin pages and imports `./bridge.js` and `./round.js`, so copy the deliverable and the three harness files into one test folder and serve that. Each run goes until `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, needing `window.__hubCheck.pass`: `?game=…&players=2&auto=1`; `&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`; the same with `&scenario=host-leave`; `&players=2&scenario=server&auto=1`. **[verified: about 22-33 s each with 4 WebGPU copies.]** Confirm the page is your game first.\n- Standalone: outside a session the deliverable runs normally. Two pages in one context run a Night Shift party over BroadcastChannel, and over WebRTC codes with `?g_nostun=1`; both reach dawn or all-down with a results screen.\n- WebKit and Firefox here have no WebGPU: expect the engine's clear message, and check that it appears and nothing else breaks.\n\nBefore finishing: look at captures of each mood, the Case, the Shop, a menu at 1920×1080 and at 4:3.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Build order\n\nEach milestone ends playable and tested. Commit nothing unless asked. Don't polish one area while others don't exist.\n\n1. **Skeleton:** folder, build script, deliverable from `file://`, hub metas, config, session/standalone split, title scene, test command. Test the harness now, with an empty card and instant finish: it's cheap and keeps you honest.\n2. **Feel:** one test yard. Camera, movement, aim, laser, pistol, Humanoid, puppets, one Islander with zones, stagger, kick. Spend real time here until shooting and kicking feel good.\n3. **Crowd:** AI states, tokens, flow fields, Limpet, Loot Director, knife, crates.\n4. **Case and Shop:** UI kit, Case, Shop, glyphs, device tracking, pause, settings, saves.\n5. **Chapter 1:** map paint, level build, dressing, doors, windows, ladders, wardrobe, Siege, Foghorn, Tannoys. Cutscenes, dialogue, voice, first songs. Bot plays it.\n6. **Dev mode and attract** in their first versions, extended as content grows.\n7. **Chapter 2:** road, cannery, Dame, Flenser, winch, belt fight, Bosun.\n8. **Chapter 3:** causeway, abbey, crypt, nave, Bathysphere, launch, ending, credits.\n9. **Night Shift:** solo, then hub co-op, then LocalSession.\n10. **Polish:** every song and sound, every animation in the list, hit feedback, HUD details, Claim Forms, About, `docs/CONTENT.md`, balance with the bot, then by reading its numbers. Remove anything unfinished.\n11. **Done list** (§17).\n\n**If you truly run out of road, cut whole features from this list in this order, cleanly, with no leftovers:** Launch (end at the nave; keep the ending scene) → WebRTC invite codes (keep same-computer parties) → the Dame's solo crypt (she climbs out; keep the lever beat as a cutscene) → the causeway's rowboats → Claim Notes. **Never cut:** aiming, zones and kicks; the Case and Shop; the Siege and Foghorn; the Dame; the Bosun and final boss; hub multiplayer; dev mode and sliders; attract mode; glyphs; the About screen. Report what you cut.","numLines":250,"startLine":601,"totalLines":885}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0136AZUAdswHhR9KT98fmyrn","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
