{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E5qqvbmDDX74xoPQ8ewXCY","type":"tool_result","content":"851\t\n852\t---\n853\t\n854\t## 17. Done, and what TASK.md asks for\n855\t\n856\tNo TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features. Every menu item does what it says. Every enemy, weapon and item in the data is in the game and reachable in play.\n857\t\n858\t| TASK.md asks for | Where in this plan |\n859\t| --- | --- |\n860\t| Source, genre, perspective | §1 |\n861\t| Title (brainstorm, RNG, riff on the source) | Builder, per TASK.md; `src/config.js`; title layout auto-fits (§11) |\n862\t| Research | Plan and kit docs are enough; report what you did |\n863\t| Single HTML package and dev subfolder | §14 |\n864\t| Engine kit, kept as it ships | §14 |\n865\t| Art: native style base, new source-feel assets, library for generic props | §8 |\n866\t| Animation: native system base, new animations | §9 |\n867\t| Audio: code only, gibberish voices, music 10% default | §10 |\n868\t| Online and multiplayer: AI Hub and on its own | §7 |\n869\t| Performance: unlimited budget, lavish | §5 Dressing, §8; `quality: 'high'` |\n870\t| Testing: one command, whole-game scripted playthrough, stand-ins | §15 |\n871\t| Original game, feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure | §1, §5, §14 |\n872\t| Dev mode from pause; live sliders with reset | §12 |\n873\t| Attract mode | §13 |\n874\t| Narrative tone | §2 |\n875\t| 10-foot, DualSense, keyboard and mouse native, prompts follow last input, PS glyphs, Xbox glyph setting | §3, §11 |\n876\t| No dense web-style screens | §11 |\n877\t| Touch-only behaviour | §11 |\n878\t| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback in the reply and About screen; exit interview | Below |\n879\t\n880\t**Final steps:**\n881\t1. `node tools/test.mjs` all green. Note how many issues testing caught, which were critical, the most and least helpful test.\n882\t2. Fill `src/data/about.js` with the real answers, in TASK.md's fields and order. `Plan` is this plan's file name. `Usage` is `added on import`. Unknowns are `unknown`. Rebuild so the screen and file agree.\n883\t3. Exit interview `aiHub` values to start from (name and tagline are yours): `type` Game; `genre` Horror; `source` Resident Evil 4; `series` Resident Evil; `players` 1–4; `controls` one line for pad and keyboard; `tags` such as `3d`, `third-person`, `horror`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `pixel art`. Check the file parses.\n884\t4. In your final reply: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, exactly as TASK.md asks. Remove temporary files, stop every process you started.\n885\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"796dd0c4-16d3-4b94-a7f8-deb30b00ba64","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:21:16.381Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n---\n\n## 17. Done, and what TASK.md asks for\n\nNo TODOs, placeholders or stubbed features. Every menu item does what it says. Every enemy, weapon and item in the data is in the game and reachable in play.\n\n| TASK.md asks for | Where in this plan |\n| --- | --- |\n| Source, genre, perspective | §1 |\n| Title (brainstorm, RNG, riff on the source) | Builder, per TASK.md; `src/config.js`; title layout auto-fits (§11) |\n| Research | Plan and kit docs are enough; report what you did |\n| Single HTML package and dev subfolder | §14 |\n| Engine kit, kept as it ships | §14 |\n| Art: native style base, new source-feel assets, library for generic props | §8 |\n| Animation: native system base, new animations | §9 |\n| Audio: code only, gibberish voices, music 10% default | §10 |\n| Online and multiplayer: AI Hub and on its own | §7 |\n| Performance: unlimited budget, lavish | §5 Dressing, §8; `quality: 'high'` |\n| Testing: one command, whole-game scripted playthrough, stand-ins | §15 |\n| Original game, feature-complete vertical slice, infrastructure | §1, §5, §14 |\n| Dev mode from pause; live sliders with reset | §12 |\n| Attract mode | §13 |\n| Narrative tone | §2 |\n| 10-foot, DualSense, keyboard and mouse native, prompts follow last input, PS glyphs, Xbox glyph setting | §3, §11 |\n| No dense web-style screens | §11 |\n| Touch-only behaviour | §11 |\n| Source Information, Testing, Engine, Prompt Feedback in the reply and About screen; exit interview | Below |\n\n**Final steps:**\n1. `node tools/test.mjs` all green. Note how many issues testing caught, which were critical, the most and least helpful test.\n2. Fill `src/data/about.js` with the real answers, in TASK.md's fields and order. `Plan` is this plan's file name. `Usage` is `added on import`. Unknowns are `unknown`. Rebuild so the screen and file agree.\n3. Exit interview `aiHub` values to start from (name and tagline are yours): `type` Game; `genre` Horror; `source` Resident Evil 4; `series` Resident Evil; `players` 1–4; `controls` one line for pad and keyboard; `tags` such as `3d`, `third-person`, `horror`, `co-op`, `boss fights`, `pixel art`. Check the file parses.\n4. In your final reply: Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback, Prompt Feedback, exactly as TASK.md asks. Remove temporary files, stop every process you started.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":851,"totalLines":885}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01E5qqvbmDDX74xoPQ8ewXCY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
