{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkeLRQHyTz1Y9ywmd9D2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ku3jFYCEkn8Z1nscSefnzA","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/kit/pixel-engine && sed -n 2251,2290p API.md; sed -n 2757,2762p API.md; grep -n \"class WaterSurface\" -A 22 API.md | cut -c1-260 | head -40"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2974,"cache_read_input_tokens":186038,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2974},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"998d97e2-1c28-4dc5-8273-1b6d7dfc8b56","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:25:11.104Z","request_id":"req_011CgkeLQpKHuPWjayUhoAfy","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Ku3jFYCEkn8Z1nscSefnzA":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/kit/pixel-engine && sed -n 2251,2290p API.md; sed -n 2757,2762p API.md; grep -n \"class WaterSurface\" -A 22 API.md | cut -c1-260 | head -40"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ku3jFYCEkn8Z1nscSefnzA","type":"tool_result","content":"### interface ButtonEvent\n\nA pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n\n- `readonly code: string`\n- `readonly down: boolean`\n- `readonly x: number`\n- `readonly y: number`\n\n### DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS: readonly TouchButton[]\n```\n\nDefault buttons for PlatformerCharacter (see character/controls.ts KEYMAP).\n\n### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n```\n\nStandard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\nKEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n\n### interface GamepadLike\n\nThe parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects).\n\n- `readonly connected?: boolean`\n- `readonly mapping?: string`\n- `readonly axes: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value?: number }[]`\n\n### class Input\n\nKeyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n- Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\n\n## 10. HUD\n\n### class Hud\n5086:### class WaterSurface\n5087-\n5088-- `new WaterSurface(o: WaterOptions)`\n5089-- `readonly size: readonly [number, number]`\n5090-- `waves: Wave[]`\n5091-- `readonly ripples: RippleField | null`\n5092-- `readonly uOpacity: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n5093-- `readonly uFoamAt: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n5094-- `setWaves(waves: readonly Wave[]): void`: Change the waves (up to MAX_WAVES; the CPU height follows too).\n5095-- `update(time: number, sun?: Vector3): void`: Per frame: the waves' clock (use physics time: floaters read the same), the ripples, the sun.\n5096-- `heightAt(x: number, z: number, t = this.time): number`: World height of the drawn surface at (x, z) (waves and ripples), at the last `update` time or `t`.\n5097-- `covers(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is (x, z) over this water?\n5098-- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n5099-\n5100-### class Wfc\n5101-\n5102-- `new Wfc(tiles: readonly WfcTile[], width: number, height: number, o: WfcOptions = {})`\n5103-- `readonly tiles: readonly WfcTile[]`\n5104-- `readonly wave: Uint8Array`: Options still open per cell: `wave[cell * tiles + t]` is 1 while tile t is possible.\n5105-- `readonly options: Uint16Array`: How many options each cell has left.\n5106-- `readonly result: Int32Array`: The chosen tile per cell (−1 until it has one option left).\n5107-- `attempt: number`: Starts so far (1 + the contradictions met).\n5108-- `done: boolean`: True once every cell has one tile, false while solving or after giving up.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"3ff7e51d-f734-4e5a-8296-20d71a102878","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:25:11.126Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### interface ButtonEvent\n\nA pointer button pressed or let go (`Input.buttonEvents`): its key, and where the pointer was (normalised device coordinates).\n\n- `readonly code: string`\n- `readonly down: boolean`\n- `readonly x: number`\n- `readonly y: number`\n\n### DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst DEFAULT_TOUCH_BUTTONS: readonly TouchButton[]\n```\n\nDefault buttons for PlatformerCharacter (see character/controls.ts KEYMAP).\n\n### GAMEPAD_BUTTONS\n\n```ts\nconst GAMEPAD_BUTTONS: Readonly<Record<number, string>>\n```\n\nStandard-mapping gamepad buttons → the key codes they press (see character/controls.ts\nKEYMAP). Change `input.gamepadButtons` to remap. Indices follow the W3C \"standard\" layout:\n0 A · 1 B · 2 X · 3 Y · 4 LB · 5 RB · 6 LT · 7 RT · 8 Back · 9 Start · 12–15 d-pad.\n\n### interface GamepadLike\n\nThe parts of the Gamepad API that Input reads (tests can pass plain objects).\n\n- `readonly connected?: boolean`\n- `readonly mapping?: string`\n- `readonly axes: readonly number[]`\n- `readonly buttons: readonly { readonly pressed: boolean; readonly value?: number }[]`\n\n### class Input\n\nKeyboard + pointer + gamepad input.\n- Keys: held state, per-frame presses (`wasPressed`) and queued presses for fixed-step\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\n\n## 10. HUD\n\n### class Hud\n5086:### class WaterSurface\n5087-\n5088-- `new WaterSurface(o: WaterOptions)`\n5089-- `readonly size: readonly [number, number]`\n5090-- `waves: Wave[]`\n5091-- `readonly ripples: RippleField | null`\n5092-- `readonly uOpacity: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n5093-- `readonly uFoamAt: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`\n5094-- `setWaves(waves: readonly Wave[]): void`: Change the waves (up to MAX_WAVES; the CPU height follows too).\n5095-- `update(time: number, sun?: Vector3): void`: Per frame: the waves' clock (use physics time: floaters read the same), the ripples, the sun.\n5096-- `heightAt(x: number, z: number, t = this.time): number`: World height of the drawn surface at (x, z) (waves and ripples), at the last `update` time or `t`.\n5097-- `covers(x: number, z: number): boolean`: Is (x, z) over this water?\n5098-- `dispose(): void`: Frees the GPU-related resources allocated by this instance.\n5099-\n5100-### class Wfc\n5101-\n5102-- `new Wfc(tiles: readonly WfcTile[], width: number, height: number, o: WfcOptions = {})`\n5103-- `readonly tiles: readonly WfcTile[]`\n5104-- `readonly wave: Uint8Array`: Options still open per cell: `wave[cell * tiles + t]` is 1 while tile t is possible.\n5105-- `readonly options: Uint16Array`: How many options each cell has left.\n5106-- `readonly result: Int32Array`: The chosen tile per cell (−1 until it has one option left).\n5107-- `attempt: number`: Starts so far (1 + the contradictions met).\n5108-- `done: boolean`: True once every cell has one tile, false while solving or after giving up.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ku3jFYCEkn8Z1nscSefnzA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
