{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DDaQx1Xt14ArWq44vEEyQN","type":"tool_result","content":"### interface ParticlePreset\n\nA particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\nsquares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n\n- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n- `flatten?: number`: Multiply vertical launch speed (0.2 = dust that hugs the ground). Default 1.\n- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n- `drag?: number`: Velocity damping per second (0 = none).\n- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Size in art pixels at birth and at death (rounded to whole pixels).\n- `colors: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Palette colors stepped through over the lifetime.\n- `radius?: number`: Random spawn offset radius, world units.\n- `max?: number`: Pool size (max alive at once). Default 256.\n\n### type ParticlePresetName\n## 9. Particles\n\n### interface BurstOptions\n\n- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n\n### class ParticlePool\n### class Particles\n\nPixel-art particles: CPU-simulated pools, drawn as camera-facing square sprites in flat\npalette colors. One emitter (one instanced draw call, one pooled instance buffer) per\npreset; sizes are whole art pixels, so in Pixel mode a particle is a crisp N×N block.\nAvailable as `ctx.particles`; emitters are created on first use and freed by `clear()`\n(the engine calls it when a level unloads).\n\n  ctx.particles.burst('dust', hero.feet);\n  ctx.particles.burst('skid', feet, { direction: [-vx, 0.3, -vz], count: 2 });\n\n- `new Particles(view: () => ParticleView)`\n- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`: Engine-owned group holding every emitter.\n- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\n- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).\n- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\n- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is ful\n- `get alive: number`: Particles alive right now, over all emitters.\n- `get emitterCount: number`: Emitters (= draw calls at most) currently allocated.\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Simulate and upload. Called by the engine every frame (frozen while paused).\n- `reseed(rng: Rng): void`: Take bursts' randomness from `rng` (the engine passes each level's `ctx.random` fork).\n- `clear(): void`: Kill every particle and free the emitters (GPU buffers, materials).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### PARTICLES\n\n```ts\nconst PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors: (\"white\" | \"mist\" | \"slate\")[]; radius: number; }; skid: { ...;\n```\n\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\n\n## 10. HUD\n21:15. More: `applySky`, `bayer4`, `BehaviorTree`, `beltMaterial`, `BeltMaterial`, `BoidOptions`, `Boids`, `Branch`, `bt`, `BtNode`, `BtStatus`, `BulletPool`, `CameraKey`, `CameraShake`, `CameraShot`,\n22-\n23-## 1. Engine and games\n24-\n25-### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n26-\n27-```ts\n28-const ADAPTIVE_ASPECT: { readonly min: 0.4; readonly max: 2.4; }\n29-```\n--\n4120:### interface DecalOptions\n4121-\n4122-- `size?: number`: Width of the mark (m). Default 0.5.\n4123-- `rotation?: number`: Turn about the normal (radians). Default random.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"04389716-ae26-4167-b67c-f05008dece5a","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:36:36.994Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"### interface ParticlePreset\n\nA particle effect as data. Sizes are in art pixels (whole pixels, so particles stay crisp\nsquares), colors are palette names stepped over each particle's life (no blending).\n\n- `count: Range`: Particles per burst.\n- `life: Range`: Seconds each particle lives.\n- `speed: Range`: Launch speed, world units / s.\n- `direction?: Vec3`: Main launch direction (default straight up).\n- `spread?: number`: Cone half-angle around `direction`, degrees (180 = every direction). Default 180.\n- `flatten?: number`: Multiply vertical launch speed (0.2 = dust that hugs the ground). Default 1.\n- `gravity?: number`: Downward acceleration, world units / s² (negative floats up). Default 0.\n- `drag?: number`: Velocity damping per second (0 = none).\n- `size: readonly [number, number]`: Size in art pixels at birth and at death (rounded to whole pixels).\n- `colors: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Palette colors stepped through over the lifetime.\n- `radius?: number`: Random spawn offset radius, world units.\n- `max?: number`: Pool size (max alive at once). Default 256.\n\n### type ParticlePresetName\n## 9. Particles\n\n### interface BurstOptions\n\n- `count?: number`: Override the particle count.\n- `direction?: Vec3`: Override the launch direction (e.g. opposite to a skid).\n- `speed?: number`: Multiply launch speed.\n- `scale?: number`: Multiply size.\n- `colors?: readonly PaletteColor[]`: Override the colors for this burst.\n\n### class ParticlePool\n### class Particles\n\nPixel-art particles: CPU-simulated pools, drawn as camera-facing square sprites in flat\npalette colors. One emitter (one instanced draw call, one pooled instance buffer) per\npreset; sizes are whole art pixels, so in Pixel mode a particle is a crisp N×N block.\nAvailable as `ctx.particles`; emitters are created on first use and freed by `clear()`\n(the engine calls it when a level unloads).\n\n  ctx.particles.burst('dust', hero.feet);\n  ctx.particles.burst('skid', feet, { direction: [-vx, 0.3, -vz], count: 2 });\n\n- `new Particles(view: () => ParticleView)`\n- `readonly group: Group<Object3DEventMap>`: Engine-owned group holding every emitter.\n- `readonly presets: Map<string, ParticlePreset>`: Preset registry: the built-ins plus anything registered.\n- `readonly pixelWorld: UniformNode<\"float\", number>`: World units per art pixel at the camera focus (updated every frame).\n- `register(name: string, preset: ParticlePreset): void`: Add or replace a named preset. Replacing frees the old preset's emitter.\n- `burst(preset: string | ParticlePreset, at: Vector3 | readonly [number, number, number], options: BurstOptions = {}): number`: Spawn a burst of `preset` (a name or a ParticlePreset) at `at`. Returns the number of particles spawned (fewer when the pool is ful\n- `get alive: number`: Particles alive right now, over all emitters.\n- `get emitterCount: number`: Emitters (= draw calls at most) currently allocated.\n- `update(dt: number): void`: Simulate and upload. Called by the engine every frame (frozen while paused).\n- `reseed(rng: Rng): void`: Take bursts' randomness from `rng` (the engine passes each level's `ctx.random` fork).\n- `clear(): void`: Kill every particle and free the emitters (GPU buffers, materials).\n- `dispose(): void`\n\n### PARTICLES\n\n```ts\nconst PARTICLES: { dust: { count: [number, number]; life: [number, number]; speed: [number, number]; spread: number; flatten: number; gravity: number; drag: number; size: [number, number]; colors: (\"white\" | \"mist\" | \"slate\")[]; radius: number; }; skid: { ...;\n```\n\nBuilt-in particle effects, as data (see ParticlePreset). Register more with\n`ctx.particles.register(name, preset)`. Sizes are art pixels; colors are PALETTE names.\n\n## 10. HUD\n21:15. More: `applySky`, `bayer4`, `BehaviorTree`, `beltMaterial`, `BeltMaterial`, `BoidOptions`, `Boids`, `Branch`, `bt`, `BtNode`, `BtStatus`, `BulletPool`, `CameraKey`, `CameraShake`, `CameraShot`,\n22-\n23-## 1. Engine and games\n24-\n25-### ADAPTIVE_ASPECT\n26-\n27-```ts\n28-const ADAPTIVE_ASPECT: { readonly min: 0.4; readonly max: 2.4; }\n29-```\n--\n4120:### interface DecalOptions\n4121-\n4122-- `size?: number`: Width of the mark (m). Default 0.5.\n4123-- `rotation?: number`: Turn about the normal (radians). Default random.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DDaQx1Xt14ArWq44vEEyQN","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkfDgHATsiLsuPNhavEW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MChuYgEFsziAYsX2TL7Pty","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/ResidentHull4-ResidentEvil4-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162051 && cat > src/game/fx.js <<'EOF'\n// Effects: particles, decals, muzzle lights, hit sparks, splashes. Cosmetic: draws from forked rng only.\nimport { THREE, Decals } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nconst { Vector3 } = THREE;\n\nexport class Fx {\n  constructor(ctx) {\n    this.ctx = ctx;\n    this.decals = new Decals(ctx.scene);\n    const p = ctx.particles;\n    p.register('blood', { count: [6, 9], life: [0.35, 0.7], speed: [1.5, 3.5], gravity: 9, size: [2, 1], colors: ['plum', 'plum', 'red'], radius: 0.05 });\n    p.register('chunk', { count: [4, 6], life: [0.5, 0.9], speed: [2, 4.5], gravity: 11, size: [2, 2], colors: ['plum', 'teal', 'slate'] });\n    p.register('spark', { count: [5, 8], life: [0.15, 0.35], speed: [2, 5], gravity: 6, size: [1, 1], colors: ['white', 'sand', 'orange'] });\n    p.register('ember', { count: [3, 5], life: [0.6, 1.1], speed: [0.6, 1.6], gravity: -2, size: [1, 1], colors: ['sand', 'orange', 'red'] });\n    p.register('splashp', { count: [10, 14], life: [0.4, 0.8], speed: [1.5, 3.5], gravity: 9, size: [1, 1], colors: ['white', 'sky', 'cyan'] });\n    p.register('boom', { count: [26, 34], life: [0.4, 0.9], speed: [3, 8], gravity: 3, size: [3, 1], colors: ['white', 'sand', 'orange', 'red', 'slate'] });\n    p.register('breath', { count: [1, 1], life: [0.8, 1.2], speed: [0.2, 0.4], gravity: -0.3, size: [2, 1], colors: ['white', 'mist'] });\n    p.register('brine', { count: [8, 12], life: [0.5, 1], speed: [1, 3], gravity: 6, size: [2, 1], colors: ['cyan', 'teal', 'white'] });\n    this.rnd = ctx.random.fork('fx');\n  }\n  bloodAt(pt, blocked) {\n    if (blocked) { this.ctx.particles.burst('spark', pt); return; }\n    this.ctx.particles.burst('blood', pt);\n    if (this.rnd.chance(0.3)) this.ctx.particles.burst('chunk', pt, { count: 3 });\n  }\n  sparks(pt) { this.ctx.particles.burst('spark', pt); }\n  splash(x, z) { this.ctx.particles.burst('splashp', new Vector3(x, 0.1, z)); }\n  boom(pt) { this.ctx.particles.burst('boom', pt); this.ctx.particles.burst('smoke', pt, { count: 10 }); }\n  decal(shape, at, normal, size) { try { this.decals.add(shape, at, normal, { size }); } catch { /* pool full */ } }\n  splat(x, z) { this.decal('splat', new Vector3(x, 0.02, z), new Vector3(0, 1, 0), 0.5 + this.rnd.range(0, 0.5)); }\n  scorch(pt, n) { this.decal('scorch', pt, n || new Vector3(0, 1, 0), 0.35); }\n  muzzle(pos) { this.ctx.lights.request({ position: [pos.x, pos.y, pos.z], color: 0xffc060, intensity: 8, radius: 6, lifetime: 0.06 }); }\n  update(dt) { this.decals.update(dt); }\n}\nEOF\necho ok"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2886,"cache_read_input_tokens":312453,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2886},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"95eb819f-952e-4afc-b710-af34f202e2ce","uuid":"5eeaf3ca-8e56-45f3-a6b3-67123e3b1989","timestamp":"2026-11-05T23:36:46.144Z","request_id":"req_011CgkfDg2n6p4q76qhJrEAJ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01MChuYgEFsziAYsX2TL7Pty":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-162051__xa8053f/work/ResidentHull4-ResidentEvil4-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261105-162051 && cat > src/game/fx.js <<'EOF'\n// Effects: particles, decals, muzzle lights, hit sparks, splashes. Cosmetic: draws from forked rng only.\nimport { THREE, Decals } from '../../pixel-engine.js';\nconst { Vector3 } = THREE;\n\nexport class Fx {\n  constructor(ctx) {\n    this.ctx = ctx;\n    this.decals = new Decals(ctx.scene);\n    const p = ctx.particles;\n    p.register('blood', { count: [6, 9], life: [0.35, 0.7], speed: [1.5, 3.5], gravity: 9, size: [2, 1], colors: ['plum', 'plum', 'red'], radius: 0.05 });\n    p.register('chunk', { count: [4, 6], life: [0.5, 0.9], speed: [2, 4.5], gravity: 11, size: [2, 2], colors: ['plum', 'teal', 'slate'] });\n    p.register('spark', { count: [5, 8], life: [0.15, 0.35], speed: [2, 5], gravity: 6, size: [1, 1], colors: ['white', 'sand', 'orange'] });\n    p.register('ember', { count: [3, 5], life: [0.6, 1.1], speed: [0.6, 1.6], gravity: -2, size: [1, 1], colors: ['sand', 'orange', 'red'] });\n    p.register('splashp', { count: [10, 14], life: [0.4, 0.8], speed: [1.5, 3.5], gravity: 9, size: [1, 1], colors: ['white', 'sky', 'cyan'] });\n    p.register('boom', { count: [26, 34], life: [0.4, 0.9], speed: [3, 8], gravity: 3, size: [3, 1], colors: ['white', 'sand', 'orange', 'red', 'slate'] });\n    p.register('breath', { count: [1, 1], life: [0.8, 1.2], speed: [0.2, 0.4], gravity: -0.3, size: [2, 1], colors: ['white', 'mist'] });\n    p.register('brine', { count: [8, 12], life: [0.5, 1], speed: [1, 3], gravity: 6, size: [2, 1], colors: ['cyan', 'teal', 'white'] });\n    this.rnd = ctx.random.fork('fx');\n  }\n  bloodAt(pt, blocked) {\n    if (blocked) { this.ctx.particles.burst('spark', pt); return; }\n    this.ctx.particles.burst('blood', pt);\n    if (this.rnd.chance(0.3)) this.ctx.particles.burst('chunk', pt, { count: 3 });\n  }\n  sparks(pt) { this.ctx.particles.burst('spark', pt); }\n  splash(x, z) { this.ctx.particles.burst('splashp', new Vector3(x, 0.1, z)); }\n  boom(pt) { this.ctx.particles.burst('boom', pt); this.ctx.particles.burst('smoke', pt, { count: 10 }); }\n  decal(shape, at, normal, size) { try { this.decals.add(shape, at, normal, { size }); } catch { /* pool full */ } }\n  splat(x, z) { this.decal('splat', new Vector3(x, 0.02, z), new Vector3(0, 1, 0), 0.5 + this.rnd.range(0, 0.5)); }\n  scorch(pt, n) { this.decal('scorch', pt, n || new Vector3(0, 1, 0), 0.35); }\n  muzzle(pos) { this.ctx.lights.request({ position: [pos.x, pos.y, pos.z], color: 0xffc060, intensity: 8, radius: 6, lifetime: 0.06 }); }\n  update(dt) { this.decals.update(dt); }\n}\nEOF\necho ok"}}}
